(Preah Vihear): The 54.90 km section of National Road No. 94 from Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park to the Cambodia-Laos border has been repaired by the Road Maintenance Team of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport. After this road was damaged by floods during this year's rainy season.
On the morning of August 6, 2022, Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, said that the section of National Road No. 94 from Techo Sen Russey Trap National Park to the Lao border was damaged by floods. As a result, it is difficult to travel.
In order to make this road easier for people to travel, the department team has repaired it by adding soil, rock mixture, watering, compacting, so that people can travel on this road easily.
Mr. Samleang Try stated that following the instructions of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, especially after the Provincial Governor inspected the actual condition of the road damaged by the flood. The Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport has taken care to repair and maintain the roads managed by the department to facilitate people's travel.
