Minister Khieu Kanharith Receives a Delegation of Royal Thai Army Information Department and Military Staff
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, on the afternoon of September 6, 2022, received Lt. Gen. Direk Bung Kan, Director of the Information Department of the Royal Thai Army and Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Cambodian Armed Forces, Lt. Col. Phinuso Sarakthy. Courtesy and job discussion on the occasion of working visit to Cambodia.
The talks focused on cooperation in exchanging information with each other, especially together against counterfeit information that undermines good relations between Cambodia and Thailand.
Lt. Gen. Direk Bung Kan highlighted his mission with Cambodia over the past 11 years and is now back in Cambodia, seeing the rapid growth and co-development of Cambodia in terms of infrastructure. Roads and skyscrapers.
Regarding the good relations in the field of information between the two countries, Thailand-Cambodia, Lt. Gen. Direk Bungkan mentioned that the cooperation between Thai Channel 5 and Khmer Channel 5 has been going on for a long time and will continue to move forward. In this regard, the Thai side has asked the Ministry of Information to help track down false information and fake news related to our country in order to take measures to correct it so that there is no misunderstanding.
At the same time, Minister Khieu Kanharith highlighted the good cooperation between Khmer and Thai TV Channel 5 by exchanging information with each other. For the Ministry of Information of Cambodia always pays attention to the Ministry of Information of Cambodia related to other information, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen always pays attention to follow up on fake information to respond and correct.
