Ministry of Women's Affairs warns public and private sectors to recruit people with disabilities
(Preah Vihear): The Ministry of Women's Affairs, ADD International Cambodia and Preah Vihear Provincial Administration this morning, September 6, 2022, jointly opened a training course on gender equality and disability environment under the chairmanship of Ms. Nhean Sochetra, Director General of the General Development Department of the Ministry. Women's affairs.
The training was attended by Mr. Sok Sandara, Deputy Governor, Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, and the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council, Mr. Sok Sandara, Director of ADD Cambodia, relevant departments and members of the Multidisciplinary Response Working Group. For gender-based violence at the provincial level at Ly Huot Restaurant in Preah Vihear City, Preah Vihear Province.
She said that the Royal Government, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has launched a strategic plan on disability, carefully considering solutions for people with disabilities to increase employment and economic security in order to reduce poverty. Period of promoting appropriate employment growth and strengthening careers and occupations to improve a decent living standard for people with disabilities.
She also called on all ministries, institutions, and the private sector to promote and implement with high responsibility and awareness of the obligation to recruit people with disabilities with the qualifications and ability to continue to work as others. It is stated in the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.
Mr. Lon Borithy, Director of ADD International Cambodia, stated that the current training course is being held for 3 days from 06 to 08 September 2022 in order to increase the in-depth understanding of service providers. Respond to gender-based violence in target areas Increase in-depth consideration of the needs of women with disabilities affected by violence by the environment, disability and gender perspectives.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Chum Hat, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, this morning, September 6, 2022, participated in the celebration of the 55th Anniversary of the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Socialist Republic of Vietnam (24.06.1964-24.06.2022) between Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Tbong Khmum and Kampong Cham provinces and provinces in Vietnam, held in Tay Ninh, Vietnam.
On that occasion, Mr. Men Vibol, on behalf of Svay Rieng Provincial Authority, expressed his congratulations on the occasion of the 55th Anniversary of the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. State of Tay Ninh province on the occasion of the 77th anniversary of Vietnam's Independence Day, September 2, 1945-2022.
He also wished all the leaders, cadres, warriors, women and the Vietnamese people, especially the people of Tay Ninh province, the best of luck in achieving family and social life. A prosperous nation forever and ever.
He added that over the past 55 years, the two countries have gone through many historical stages, supporting each other for the cause of independence, sovereignty, integrity and development. At present, the people of the border provinces are enjoying the progress of good relations in all fields, which have mutually benefited the socio-economic development, brought about development and prosperity. .
(South Korea): General Chhum Socheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense, is currently leading a delegation of the Cambodian Ministry of National Defense to attend three meetings in Seoul, Republic of Korea.
These include the 2022 Seoul Defense Dialogue, the Korea-ASEAN Deputy Defense Ministers' Meeting and the three-day Working Group on Space Security and Information Security held in Seoul, South Korea. From September 6 to 8, 2022.
The delegation of the Ministry of National Defense that attended these defense meetings included representatives of the General Department of Politics and Foreign Affairs, representatives of the General Department of Research and Intelligence, representatives of the General Department of International Relations, representatives of the Office of Cyber Security, and the Department of Messaging.
The annual International Security Forum, hosted by the South Korean Defense Ministry, discusses North Korea's nuclear disarmament, cyber-threats, space security and other challenges. The Seoul Deputy Defense Minister (SDD) Dialogue was held at the Lotte Hotel in Seoul under the theme "How to Solve Complex Security Challenges": Strengthening International Solidarity.
The SDD meeting is the first face-to-face meeting since 2019 following the 19 outbreak of Kovid, bringing together senior defense officials and civilian experts from 54 countries, the United Nations, the European Union and treaties. North Atlantic or NATO.
South Korean Deputy Defense Minister Shin Beom-chul will host a meeting with counterparts from the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) to discuss medium- and long-term plans for bilateral defense cooperation. The next day, he will hold a series of meetings with three Asia-Pacific partners, Australia, New Zealand and Japan, to discuss cooperation in maintaining unity in upholding "values and norms."
Ministry of Social Affairs opens training course for elderly care
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on September 6, 2022 opened the "Elderly Care Skills Training" at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
Mr. Touch Channy, General Director of Social Services of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, in the dissemination workshop on "Elderly Care Skills Training Program" stated that the purpose of this workshop was to focus on:
1: Disseminate to trainees, students and the public about the skills of caring for the elderly.
2: Want trainees, students and the public who wish to go to work as interns in Japan on the skills of care for the elderly.
3: Want to show that in Cambodia today, the profession of care for the elderly is a new skill that has just been developed, and a new skill with the National Center for the Elderly Protection of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, which is one of the first training institutions on this skill.
4: Progress Asia Co., Ltd. is a partner with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to provide skills training for the elderly.
5: Get job opportunities both inside and outside the country.
The workshop was organized by Brokes and members of the General Association of the International Partnership Center (IPC) in collaboration with the Department of the Elderly and Veterans of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
He added that although Cambodia is in the midst of the Kovid-19 epidemic, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation continues to actively contribute to the better implementation of the National Policy on the Elderly 2017-2030. Period of action plan 2021-2025 of the National Policy on the Elderly 2017-2030.
