DPM Chea Sophara Inaugurates Kampong Speu Provincial Stadium worth Over 4 Million USD
(Kampong Speu): Kampong Speu Provincial Stadium worth more than 4 million dollars was officially inaugurated this morning, September 6, 2022 under the presidency of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. This Kampong Speu Provincial Stadium is a construction initiative of Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency.
Speaking on the occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara said that, in general, sports bring health, bring more unity, the construction of stadiums has increased the revenue of the provincial administration. He emphasized that all construction must be based on the rule of law, the construction of this stadium is legal enough.
He added that currently Kampong Speu province has really interesting development from investors from all directions, and also has a beautiful stadium can add tourists.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara stressed that the country is peaceful, developed, has hospitals, schools, and the country is stable under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. Turn to exercise when you are healthy and we have seen the development of the nation.
It should be informed that Kampong Speu Provincial Stadium was built under the initiative of Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Province, with a total construction cost of $ 4,250,695 in the joint spirit to enhance the image and prestige of Kampong Speu Province. And in order to contribute to the Royal Government in the development of sports in Cambodia to grow towards hosting the upcoming 2023 SEA Games.
The construction project of Kampong Speu Provincial Stadium was built in two phases: the construction phase of the fence around 800 meters and the two main gates of the stadium, and then the construction of the football field and other infrastructure inside and outside the stadium at the same time. Playground, public gym and installation of solar lights in the stadium.
The football field is 110 meters long and 73 meters wide, covered with artificial grass and has a drainage system around the table. The track is 400 meters long, 9.76 meters wide and 10 meters wide from the track to the fence. The four football field lighting poles are 40.20 meters high, weigh 3,000 kilograms and are equipped with 42 lamps with a brightness of 1,200. There are 200 solar lights around the stadium.
