China has refused to condemn Russia's invasion of Ukraine and is not expected to support oil price action due to its concerns over energy security, which the country relies heavily on for oil imports from Russia.
"Oil is one of the global commodities and it is very important to ensure safety," Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Mao Ning was quoted as saying by Reuters. Of the world's energy supply.
"We hope that the countries concerned will make constructive efforts to ease the situation through dialogue and consultation, not vice versa," she added.
China has become one of Russia's biggest buyers of discounted oil as Europe cuts imports.
Russia was China's largest supplier of oil in the three months to July as independent refiners increased purchases of discounted oil supplies while cutting oil purchases. From other rival suppliers such as Angola and Brazil.
Oil imports from Russia in the first seven months of this year reached 48.45 million tons, up 4.4 percent from the same period last year. According to Reuters.
