Understanding the impact as a result, the residents of the site agreed and joined the team to remove the metal for cars or motorcycles to drive on the sidewalk with a friendly smile. Court Continues Trial of Former General Duong Ngiep in Million Dollar Fraud Case
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of September 6, 2022, resumed the hearing on the case of former General Duong Ngiep with a Taiwanese national in connection with the crime of forgery and issuing millions of dollars in checks. The court will announce the next hearing on September 29, 2022.
During this morning's hearing, former General Duong Ngiep was directly warned by Mr. Sin Vanrath, President of the Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, that he would submit a letter to the Ministry of Interior, General Department of Prisons or other relevant institutions, if any. In the absence of the accused, Duong Ngiep and refused to dress like other defendants at the hearing.
Mr. Duong Ngiep was brought into the courtroom by the Phnom Penh Municipal Prison PJ, dressed as an innocent person, which was against the rules of the prison and was not fair before the law for the accused.
Prosecutor Seng Heang also cautioned that Duong Ngiep had not appeared before his trial twice before, but did not follow the rules of procedure. Trial Chamber. Within the circle, Mr. Duong Ngiep claimed that he did not have a lawyer to defend himself, so he failed to attend the previous hearing.
On February 14, 2022, Mr. Duong Ngiep was issued an arrest warrant by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and remanded in custody at PJ Prison in connection with the crime of forgery and issuing millions of dollars in checks. Held between 2020-2021.
Duong Ngiep was arrested on charges of "non-compliance with traded instruments" worth more than $ 7 million, filed by two Taiwanese investors.
Mr. Duong Ngiep had previously applied for bail, but was rejected by the court on July 7, 2022.
