Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications in collaboration with the Ministry of Interior and Security of the Republic of Korea organizes Cambodia-Korea Digital Government Forum
The forum aims to present the status and progress of digital government in Cambodia, as well as to share the knowledge, experience and excellence of the Korean Digital Government to ministries, institutions in the public sector, the private sector and civil society organizations in Cambodia in line with government policy. Digital 2022-2035 launched by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The forum was attended by leaders of ministries, state institutions, public institutions, sub-national administrations, telecommunications operators, technology companies, civil society organizations and key development partners, including about 120 live participants and about 150 video zoom users. .
The Minister also met with Chang-Seob Han for bilateral talks. During the meeting, the Korean side presented the progress and direction of the Korean Government-supported digital government project for the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, including research, regulation and capacity building.
The Minister thanked the Korean side for its active contribution to supporting the digital revolution in Cambodia in the past. He also briefed the Korean side on the ministry's priorities and achievements over the past two years, including the development of legal standards, policies, infrastructure, capacity building, and revenue collection for the state.
The Korean side also praised the achievements of the Ministry in the short term and the clear vision of the Ministry. In response to the Minister's request, the Korean side will raise this request with the Korean Ministry of Foreign Affairs to examine the possibility of supporting Cambodia.
The Digital Government Forum and the Cambodia-Korea Bilateral Meeting reflect the long-term vision of strengthening international cooperation between the two countries, especially the hosting of the event, which proves the leadership of the two countries. Cambodia, which is chairing ASEAN in 2022.
