Cambodian diplomat thanks international partners, especially the United States, for their efforts in finding artifacts and returning them to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, thanked international partners, especially the United States, for their efforts to help find Cambodia's stolen artefacts and return them to Cambodia.
The Cambodian Ambassador made his remarks during the opening remarks of the International Conference on "Prevention and Control of Illegal Cultural Trafficking: Perspectives from ASEAN" via video held in Siem Reap this morning. September 5, 2022.
He believes that the handing over of these artifacts is the return of the ancestral souls to the Cambodian nation. "As Cambodia focuses on economic development, we anticipate that the return of our national treasure will be an inspiration for the creation of new, innovative museums, new art, fashion and music," he said. "Using the latest technology, new entertainment options and expanding our cultural tourism."
According to the Deputy Prime Minister, the economic impact of the return of these national assets will have an impact on future generations. We are confident that we will see a rapid increase in the enthusiasm and pride of our youth for their cultural heritage and in training young people to participate in the protection of their cultural heritage, from conservation to collection. Event management up to law enforcement.
The 51st Ambulance Donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the Navy Coast Guard Command to Provide Timely Service to Citizens
(Kampong Speu): The 51st ambulance donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen was handed over to Kampong Speu Provincial Coast Guard Command through Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana and Tycoon Ly Hiek Ratana to provide better health services to the people.
The handover ceremony took place this morning, August 5, 2022, presided over by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and paid a courtesy call on the Deputy Chief of Staff. Navy, Coast Guard, Navy.
General Ith Sarath stated that on behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces brought a message of greetings and deep memories from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the Deputy Chief of Staff of the Navy Coast Guard Command
