The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has stated that the first public securities auction is worth 100 billion riels or about 25 million US dollars as a one-year loan with a value of 1 million riels at a fixed 2% coupon rate. The interest rate will be calculated every six months.
According to the National Bank of Thailand, the first public securities auction will be held through the NBCP system from 8:00 am to 2:00 pm, where banking and financial institutions can participate in the auction as scheduled on September 7, 2022. This.
Mr. Sou Socheat, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, told Fresh News on September 5 that for the initial sale of state securities, only institutional investors can participate in the bidding. Yes. In particular, the public can not buy this securities. However, the public will be able to buy this state securities in the second phase, which is done through the mechanism of the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
"According to the Ministry of Finance's initial policy document, we will divide the first phase into two, and the second phase will use the market mechanism to issue the securities, but the timing of the second phase depends on when," he said. "On the decision of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which we have just reached the first stage, we use the mechanism through the National Bank."
