In the farewell meeting of Mr. Pan Yarak Poultab, Thai Ambassador to Cambodia after the end of his diplomatic mission on Monday morning, September 5, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted that despite the circumstances of 19 Kovid Cambodia And Thailand are proud to work together to promote bilateral relations and cooperation in trade, education and other fields.
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, maintaining the growth of trade as well as cooperation in various fields during the Kovid 19 crisis is due to the efforts of officials of the two governments. In this regard, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Mr. Panyarak Poultap for his efforts in fulfilling his diplomatic mission to improve relations and cooperation between the two countries.
Mr. Panyarak Poultab also highlighted the efforts to promote relations and cooperation during his diplomatic mission in Cambodia. He informed Samdech Techo that when he came to fulfill his diplomatic mission in Cambodia in 2018, he was determined to further strengthen the cooperation and relations between the two countries on the existing basis.
He said that now his promises have come to fruition, in which cooperation and relations between Cambodia and Thailand have been expanded and trade between the two countries has increased by 10 percent, despite the stage of the disease crisis. Kovid 19. In addition, education, human resource development and other areas are also growing.
The report shows that trade between Cambodia and Thailand in 2021 reached nearly $ 8 billion, an increase of about 10 percent. Of that, exports from Cambodia to Thailand amounted to 894 million US dollars. Imports from Thailand amounted to 6.1 billion US dollars.
Mr. Panyarak Poultab expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Royal Government of Cambodia for their good cooperation in making his diplomatic mission a success.
During the farewell meeting with Samdech Techo this morning, Mr. Poul Thap also thanked Samdech Techo for providing the vaccine to him and the Thai Embassy in Cambodia.
The outgoing Ambassador also congratulated Samdech Techo and the Royal Government of Cambodia on successfully controlling the spread of Kovid 19 and on behalf of the ASEAN Chairmanship reopened the country to chair the Foreign Ministers' Meeting. ASEAN and related meetings have been successful, reflecting Cambodia's strong role in the international arena.
Please note that Mr. Panyarak Poultap came to work as the Thai Ambassador to Cambodia in 2018. During his tenure in Cambodia, he paid close attention to promoting the many relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand, which are neighboring countries.
