At the handover ceremony, Mrs. HUN Mana brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the grandparents of the people who attended this time. She stated that both princes always care about the well-being of parents, relatives, people everywhere and at all times.
Then, this morning, she also led the team to donate 3 wells to the people of Dang Tong district, Kampot province. This well, which is numbered 105 to 107, is a precious gift from Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to provide to the people in Dang Tong District, Kampot Province for special needs. This area during the dry season always has a shortage of water regularly.
On that occasion, she also distributed gifts from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the people who participated in the celebration of the handing over ceremony of the three wells in the most pleasant atmosphere. A 100-year-old silver Buddha statue has been repatriated from Thailand (Video inside)
(Kampong Chhnang): A silver Buddha statue, more than 6 meters high and weighing more than 27 kilograms, is an invaluable national cultural treasure, has been returned home by a procession from Thailand to be worshiped. In Wat Chanbach Chotnaram, called Wat Ta Sot, near Wat Kraing Leav, in Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
During the ceremony, Ms. Born Sophy stated that the statue was built of silver at the end of the reign of King Norodom, who was 100 to 130 years old. Originally, this ancient statue was located in Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province. During 1989, he was cut off from the throne by criminals and sold to a number of antiquities dealers, most recently in Bangkok, Thailand.
During July 2022, after receiving information about the precious ancient statues, which are the national cultural property, the Chief Inspector of Wat Ta Sot, in collaboration with the Provincial Department of Culture and the Department of Heritage, Ministry of Culture, contacted the owner in Bangkok, Thailand. Then, the generous Khmer asked to buy from them for 550,000 baht to return home.
In particular, the celebration of the return of the ancient Buddha statues to be worshiped in Wat Ta Sot, located about 1 km from Wat Kraing Leav, a historical pagoda in France in Rolea Bier district.
Mr. Norak Rattanawadkno said that the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festivals are coming soon, so the pagoda committee and the pagoda's chief priest must prepare the pagoda well to receive the Buddhists to the candle ceremony. According to national tradition. Tens of thousands protest in Prague against Czech government, EU and NATO
Protesters from far-right political parties, including the Communist Party, have said Central European countries should maintain military neutrality and secure direct contracts with gas suppliers, including Russia.
Police estimates put about 70,000 protesters in Saturday afternoon.
Organizers say the purpose of their demonstration is to demand a major shift in tackling energy prices, especially electricity and gas, which will destroy the economy this fall.
The protest in Wenceslas Square in central Prague, Czech Republic, came a day after the government won a vote of no confidence as opposition groups claimed inaction against inflation and rising energy prices. Phnom Penh Governor Visits Vietnam for Nearly a Week to Strengthen and Expand Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): A delegation of Phnom Penh Capital Administration led by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, and his entourage on the evening of September 4, 2022, paid an official visit to Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
The visit will take place for almost a week, from September 4 to 8, 2022, to further strengthen and expand cooperation between cities and cities, especially in the fields of environment, waste, education, tourism and training. And the health sector.
For the planned program, Mr. Khuong will pay official visits to Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam from September 4-8, 2022. The delegation will leave Phnom Penh for Hanoi, visit the Nam Son solid waste treatment plant and proceed to the Bak Theang Long-Vantri plant to manage solid and liquid waste.
The delegation will pay a courtesy call on the Head of State of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and visit the National Assembly of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. The delegation will also attend the Ho Chi Minh City Tourism Fair, followed by a ribbon-cutting ceremony to open the Ho Chi Minh City Tourism Fair on September 8, the last day for the delegation to return home.
