Alumni during the 1980s say that under the leadership of Samdech Techo, the education sector in Cambodia has changed from scarcity to development.
(Kandal): Representative of former high school students in Kampong Kong, Koh Thom district, Kandal province during 1979 to 1988, Mr. Chhun Hour said that the education sector in Cambodia has developed significantly compared to the past, that is, during Cambodia has just been freed from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Mr. Chhun Hour, who currently works at the Bodyguard Command, said that the education sector is currently well-developed in terms of both software and hardware infrastructure, with good school buildings and a rich curriculum, as well as good roads. Easy to travel to study too.
Mr. Chhun Hour made this remark on September 4, 2022 during a gathering of former high school alumni of Kampong Kong, Koh Thom District, Kandal Province.
He said that this meeting was held to show gratitude to the teachers who have taught in the past and to increase friendship and understanding, as well as to help each other in times of emergency. Separated for more than 30 years.
"Under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the country was very developed. In other words, the education sector in my generation did not have good school buildings and not even shoes. "There are beautiful, but now very developed, this generation of children are easy to learn." This is according to Mr. Chhun Hour.
On that occasion, Mr. Chhun Hour called on the current generation of students to work hard to learn and be united to join the Royal Government in the development of Cambodia to continue to grow while the country has Complete peace and development.
Please be informed that the education sector is considered by the Royal Government of Cambodia as one of the four priority areas of the goal of promoting economic growth and development of the country.
