Koh Kong Provincial Authority Dismantles Slums and Prevents Land Acquisition on National Park in Peam Kay Village Reservoir, Kirisakor District
(Koh Kong): Mr. Sok Sothy, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, led the forces of the Provincial Unity Command and local authorities of Kirisakor District under the coordination of Mr. Khun Phoeun, Deputy Prosecutor of the Koh Kong Provincial Prosecutor's Office. The law on national park land is located in the reservoir area of Peam Kay village, Koh Sdach commune, Kirisakor district, Koh Kong province.
During the activities held on September 3, 2022, Mr. Sok Sothy said that the slums were built illegally, and the working group had to follow the law to dismantle 70 huts and hundreds of meters of fence posts to be implemented. Must be removed from the land of the national park area of 6771 hectares where they are building huts and logging to own.
Mr. Sok Sothy said that this land used to be inhabited by only 18 families, but the national policy at the provincial level has been resolved and the construction of all 18 families has already been completed. All 18 families, after receiving compensation from the Royal Government, also left the area. But in recent months, criminals have been stealing and encroaching on state forest land.
Seeing such actions, the provincial authorities, district authorities and local authorities have already informed them three or four times before reaching the law enforcement authorities to immediately remove them to prevent further growth. As for the huts, they are made to identify the landowners, there are no people left, and the builders of the huts encroaching on the national park land are mostly from different provinces with brokers.
He added that the land in the reservoir area in Peam Kay village, Koh Sdach commune, Kirisakor district, is under the management of a drug company that the Royal Government has leased for long-term development, and the area is planned by the company to develop a reservoir for people's needs. Going forward.
