A joint press release obtained by Fresh News on September 4, 2022 states that the "Zero Trap Campaign" officially began in March 2022 in Phnom Penh under the initiative and leadership of the Ministry of Environment. Support from conservation and development partners. The Zero Trap campaign lasts for six months, focusing on six target provinces: Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Kampong Thom and Ratanakkiri.
Seng Teak, Director of WWF Cambodia, said that Cambodia has been at the forefront of Southeast Asia in dealing with the trap crisis, which is a major cause of wildlife extinction and alarming decline. "This trap needs to be addressed in tandem with education strategies, outreach, law enforcement, increasing fines and creating new options for local people," he added.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet emphasized this on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 13th anniversary of the establishment of the Bodyguard Command (September 4, 2009 - September 4, 2020).
The senior military officer of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) highlighted that the bodyguard command traveled with two directions, one for development and the other for conservation. Mr. HUN Manet said that in the last 30 years or so, the bodyguard command has changed a lot. The force has evolved from just 12 men, hundreds of times, from one group to another, and has a rich arsenal of weapons.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet highlighted the development of the force as follows: "Bodyguards play a role in strengthening the military capacity of the unit and play a role in strengthening the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces through human resource building. "Tens of thousands of our human resources have been trained during this time."
The commander of the Army Corps, who graduated from the US Military Academy, said that in addition to developing the force's capabilities, the bodyguard command also expanded its visibility and operational capabilities by expanding from 12 to Directly protect the safety of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, but now the bodyguard command operates in multiple fields.
"Whether it's pumping water to the fields, drought relief, flood relief, we all carry out preventive operations. "Whether to protect the territorial integrity, to protect the national and international leaders." This is Mr. Hun Manet's additional emphasis on the development of the Bodyguard Command.
Along with highlighting the development of the bodyguard command, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also highlighted the work that the bodyguards continue to preserve unchanged. Conservative work is to be loyal, to protect and serve the nation, the people and the head of government, both now and in the future.
The commander of the army, who has made many reforms in the military sector, emphasized that "the development of all capabilities, structures, equipment, but what has not been preserved from the beginning is the approach ." From 12 to one division, still do the same, faithfully defend and serve the nation and the people. Loyal, protect and serve the head of government and family.
Please note that the Bodyguard Command is an institution of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces under the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. The bodyguard command plays a central role in protecting the territorial integrity of the nation, religion and the king. In addition, the Bodyguard Command has a special role to provide security to the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on all missions.
(Mondulkiri): The Ministry of Environment and WWF have expressed a joint position to increase the population of mountain crocodiles in the Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri Province to increase in the natural forest.
The Ministry of Environment and WWF will continue to monitor the situation of mountain crocodiles in the Srepok area and strengthen measures to protect their habitats from threats such as land grabbing, encroachment and illegal activities. Others, consistently applying for regular patrols by all means, both inside and outside the protected area.
On behalf of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra called on all stakeholders to take further joint action for the protection and conservation of mountain crocodiles so that the world's rarest animals can avoid extinction and release Methods to ensure the species is endangered to support its future survival.
The Ministry of Environment is ready to work with international NGOs, local communities and other partners to protect and preserve Cambodia's forest and wildlife heritage for long-term social and economic benefits. This generation and future generations.
The Secretary of State added: "We are now studying together how we can strengthen the population system in the Srepok area. It is important to strengthen the presence of mountain crocodiles in this area as a priority.
According to Seng Teak, President of WWF, his organization will be collaborating with the Srek Pok Sanctuary Conservation Group and the Ministry of Environment to conduct a population-based study of more than 10 species. He said the study found that the reproduction of mountain crocodiles was a bit slow, so in order to increase the number of mountain crocodiles, which are rare and attractive for tourism, will be placed in the field more.
He said that the organization and the government have also tried to attract tourists from Angkor to focus on forest and wildlife tourism. It should be noted that Cambodia is a globally important habitat for the survival of mountain crocodiles, which is estimated to number between 200 and 400 living in natural habitats in the country. In the world, the number of mountain crocodiles of reproductive age is no more than 1,000.
