Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Presides Over the 13th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Bodyguard Command
(Kandal): On the morning of September 4, 2020, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the 5th Prime Minister of Cambodia. Presiding over the 13th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Bodyguard Command (September 4, 2009 - September 4, 2020).
The ceremony took place at the Bodyguard Command in Takhmao City, Kandal Province, with the participation of General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Bodyguards The nation, commanders, deputy commanders, officers, deputies, soldiers and national and international guests participated in large numbers, with a display of military equipment.
The Bodyguard Command was established under the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, headed by General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. The Bodyguard Command is under the direct command of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry of National Defense, and the General Command is responsible for providing logistics, finance, equipment, and training.
The Bodyguard Command was established to provide security for Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Hun Rany Hun Sen, as well as his family and to intervene to maintain security and order in Cambodia and to play a significant role, especially in natural disasters, famines or Clashes on the border.
