The Joint Life Saving Organization of the Republic of Korea is a fund that supports medical and educational infrastructure in developing countries around the world. Ratanakkiri Governor to Plan Market Inspections Across Provinces to Prevent All Kinds of Wildlife Meat Sales
(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, said that the provincial administration will launch a plan for officials to inspect markets throughout the province to prevent illegal wildlife trade in the local sense in order to participate in wildlife conservation. To survive.
This statement was made by the provincial governor on the occasion of attending a press conference on Zero Trap under the chairmanship of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign, with the participation of partner organizations of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Environment in the afternoon. On September 3, 2022, at the Department of Environment of Ratanakkiri Province.
On that occasion, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun urged all people not to enter the forest, hunt animals, do not eat wild meat because many diseases have occurred due to eating wild meat.
The provincial governor also said that for Ratanakkiri province, there is currently a shortage of labor to work in rubber plantations, banana plantations, as well as other work activities, so please people who fall into the forest to hunt wild animals to sell to you. Eat, return to work at the existing location, avoid entering the forest, hunting, which leads to punishment.
In addition, on behalf of the Provincial Board of Governors, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun announced his full support for the Zero Trap Campaign initiated by the Ministry of Environment and partner organizations.
Separately, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that through the zero trap campaign has been becoming part of the message to understand the importance of natural resources and wildlife. However, the campaign has yet to completely eradicate forest encroachment, hunting and wildlife eating by some individuals who still believe that eating wild meat, wild blood and wild bones is a tonic. The body and so on.
The Zero Trap Campaign lasted six months, starting with six provincial targets east of the Mekong River: Stung Treng, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom. Ratanakkiri, on the other hand, is the sixth province to end this zero trap campaign.
It should be recalled that the dire situation of biodiversity decline is not unique to Cambodia, the global wildlife population, both terrestrial and aquatic, has dropped dramatically to an average of 68%. In the last 50 years since 1970.
Illegal hunting from the past to the present, coupled with the large number of traps set in the wild, has been driven by the illegal wildlife trade, which is one of the main reasons why Cambodia's wildlife is facing extinction. In particular, ground-dwelling toenails are part of the increased risk. Traps are hidden killers and a major threat to wildlife.
