(Phnom Penh): In September 2022, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, decided to pilot the program to deduct points from drivers' licenses in violation of road traffic laws.
The driver's license deduction program is another new mechanism by the Royal Government of Cambodia to force all drivers to adhere to the law when driving, in addition to the transitional penalty.
According to Mr. Chhuon Vorn, Director General of the General Department of Land Transport of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the introduction of the program to deduct points on driver's licenses after checking that some drivers do not comply with the law, despite fines. Serious money, however.
Mr. Chhuon Von claimed that on the driver's license, a total of 12 points were assigned and the score would be reduced from 1 point to 6 points depending on the type of crime committed by the driver. When this score is deducted, the driver will have his / her driver's license revoked and will have to wait for 6 months before re-applying for a driver's license.
