(Kampong Chhnang): 7 cows died and 1 head was seriously injured and both hind legs were broken when a truck collided head-on. This incident happened at 8:15 AM on September 3, 2022 on National Road No. 5 in front of the gate of Wat Thom Voan in Trapeang Anchanh village, Kraing Dey Meas commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
After the incident, the police arrested the driver of the car and took him to the Rolea Bier District Police Inspectorate to build a case file. Separately, at the scene, the police facilitated the traffic and made a record to return the dead and injured cows to the people who own the cows and instructed the 3-4 cow owners to file a legal complaint.
Residents at the scene stated that prior to the incident, they had been waving red flags as a signal to ask cars to slow down on the national road or to stop for cattle to pass. But at that time, the provocative car did not slow down or stop, but drove at high speed, overtook a small car in front and also hit a herd of cows crossing the national road, causing an accident.
Both were charged with "fraud" under Articles 377 and 378 of the Penal Code. This is according to Mr. Plang Sophal, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, confirmed by telegram to Fresh News on the afternoon of September 3, 2022. He added that after deciding to indict, the prosecutor made a conclusion and sent the case to the investigating judge according to the procedure.
