(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that the Ministry of Health will expand modern digital systems throughout the country to monitor the health history of patients.
"In the past, our state hospitals, both in Phnom Penh and through some provincial networks, have launched this digital system, and in the future we will cover the whole country," he said.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health of Cambodia during his visit to the new building of the four-story National Children's Hospital in early September 2022.
Prof. Mam Bunheng pointed out that at the National Children's Hospital, the digital system has already been launched by the patients who come for treatment and will be given a patient ID card, with the doctor entering the details of the patient's health. When the patient comes back for another checkup (next time), just scan the card to know the patient's past history.
The Minister of Health said, "Children who come to the National Pediatric Hospital can only be scanned to find out how many vaccines they have been given. For young children, 11 vaccines are required, but for girls, there is also a cervical cancer vaccine." . Therefore, when covering the digital system nationwide, patients can carry a health card with them when visiting public hospitals, doctors will know his history (from small to large).
Professor Mam Bunheng added, "We will strive to provide our patients with high quality and effective care, especially the virtues of doctors to improve the well-being of our people."
