Commentary: American-made "democratic model" is a tragic joke
BEIJING, Aug. 29 (Xinhua) - On August 29, a day before US troops withdrew from Afghanistan, US troops launched an air strike on Afghanistan under the pretext of cracking down on extremist groups. Ten civilians were killed, including seven children, the youngest of whom was just two years old.
This is not only because the "American-style democracy" enforced in Iraq is not in line with the actual situation in Iraq, but also because of what the United States has exported to Iraq: hegemony and oppression. Oppression that wears democratic skin and strategic attempts to maintain American-style hegemony.
Twenty years later, in the Middle East, nearly 1 million innocent people lost their lives in the face of "American democracy." The international community needs to clear up the crimes committed by the United States in the Middle East in order to seek justice for the victims.
