General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of the Disaster Management Secretariat of the Ministry of National Defense, said the disaster relief exercise was an initiative and consensus between the three defense ministers.
According to General Ith Sarath, the disaster relief exercise will take place from September 9 to 16. About 500 people participated in the disaster relief exercise. Laos, the host country, has more than 300 troops, Vietnam has more than 100 and Cambodia has nearly 100.
General Ith Sarath also said that the exercise was conducted under the theme of disaster relief caused by typhoons and floods. In this exercise, the Cambodian Army is tasked with rescuing drowning people, burying people in buildings collapsed by storms, drowning people, and rescuing from landslides.
The director of the Disaster Management Secretariat of the Ministry of National Defense stressed that the disaster relief exercises between the armies of the three countries are a joint cooperation in response to the disasters that often threaten the three Mekong countries.
"This is a joint measure of humanitarian work, as natural disasters often occur in these three countries," said General Ith Sarath. Natural disasters do not happen in Vietnam, in Cambodia or in Laos. "This natural disaster sometimes happens in Vietnam and passes into Cambodia. If this happens, we have to cooperate with his forces to save."
"Our aim is to prevent and rescue natural disasters," he added. Save our people from all these disasters. "This is an initiative of cooperation between the three countries."
It should be noted that in order to ensure the success of the Cambodian Army's participation in the exercise, on the morning of September 2, 2022, General Ith Sarath inspected the materials and equipment used in the disaster relief exercise and met with Troops go out to participate in this exercise directly. The meeting took place at the Special Forces Command of Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey.
During the inspection of equipment and conversation with the troops to participate in this exercise, there were also scenes of rescue operations, including search for drowning, rescue of victims in the water and rescue of victims under the pile of buildings And so on.
In addition to inspecting the equipment and watching the performance on how to rescue the victims, General Ith Sarath also helped to talk with the nearly 100 troops who will be participating in the exercise.
During the meeting, in addition to praising the rescue training efforts, General Ith Sarath highlighted global climate change and frequent natural disasters. The general emphasized that in addition to the core work of protecting the territorial integrity, the army also has another special duty, which is to save the people from various disasters.
General Ith Sarath reminded the troops who have to go out to participate in this disaster relief exercise to pay attention to the exercise in order to absorb the knowledge and skills to help the people in case of natural disasters.
The Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces also instructed the troops to go out and take into account the safety and security of their personal as well as the safety of the equipment and facilities provided.
General Ith Sarath also instructed the army to take care to protect health from Kovi 19. In addition, the rules, regulations and other conditions in the relief exercise must be respected to avoid bad criticism from the participating countries.
