(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the British Embassy show increased cooperation, reduce carbon energy consumption and strengthen the capacity of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The pledge to increase cooperation to reduce carbon emissions between the National Bank of Cambodia and the British Embassy was made on the occasion of Mr. Susan Sith, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, allowing Ken O'Flaherty, Ambassador of the United Nations Conference On the 26th Climate Change (COP26) in the Asia-Pacific Region, accompanied by a delegation from the British Embassy in Cambodia, paid a courtesy call and discussed the work.
Mr. Ken O'Flaherty praised the cooperation between the British Embassy and the National Bank of Cambodia in the past and seeks to increase cooperation on contributions to carbon offsets and capacity building of professional staff. Of the National Bank of Cambodia in assessing the impact of climate change on the financial sector.
Mr. Sou Sannisith welcomed the recent strengthening of cooperation between the British Embassy and the National Bank of Cambodia and informed of the support of the National Bank of Cambodia for environmental protection and climate change as well as the banking system in Cambodia.
Since 2016, the National Bank of Cambodia has adopted the principles of the banking sector for sustainable social and environmental credit for all banking and financial institutions to participate in a consistent and efficient implementation.
The National Bank of Cambodia has also partnered with organizations such as UNESCAP, the Alliance for Financial Environment (AFI), the British Embassy and the International Finance Corporation (IFC) to strengthen participation in sustainable financing and climate change.
