Microfinance Association Spokesperson: To avoid loss of property or other threats, citizens should stop borrowing online or informal loans
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association urges people in need of loans to use loans from legitimate financial institutions to avoid unofficial mortgages or online loans to avoid problems or threats.
Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy's remarks came after some people recently fell into debt due to high interest rates on loans. There have also been cases where some online lenders have posted claims from their creditors. Relatives and friends of some of the debtors were also harassed and threatened by the creditors on the phone or on social media.
He added that citizens who are threatened should complain to the competent authorities, especially for online loans should complain to the Department of Technology Crimes, which may have the technology to track and target.
The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) recently warned against taking legal action against unlicensed companies or individuals who are active in providing credit to citizens and urging all citizens to use official financial services. Under the supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia, because the customers of those institutions are protected by law.
The National Bank of Cambodia condemns all forms of informal and informal lending and cooperates with the relevant authorities to take legal action against companies or individuals who commit illegal activities in accordance with the law. . Senior official of the Ministry of Information calls on journalists to have professional ethics to avoid using abusive words that bring disgrace to the same journalists (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Meas Sophorn, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Information, called on all journalists to perform their work ethically and avoid using inappropriate words or using profanity. Its media, which brings disgrace to individuals and other journalists.
In the press conference of the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the morning of September 1, 2022, under the theme "Achievements for 5 years of the Ministry of Information", the spokesman of the Ministry of Information emphasized that journalists must study In-depth and clear understanding of the law on journalism, which states its rights, roles and responsibilities.
Mr. Meas Sophorn said, "On behalf of the Ministry of Information, I would like to call once again as well as encourage the journalists who are fulfilling their duties as journalists in Cambodia to respect the code of ethics. "Journalists need to look in depth and understand the law on journalism, which states our rights, roles and responsibilities."
He added that no one can maintain the professional values of journalists to be recognized, dignified, trusted by the public audience other than the journalists themselves, so that this value is appropriate for journalists. Always call yourself "the press is the fourth power" or a mirror of social reality, unless the journalist is a bright mirror.
The senior official of the Ministry of Information acknowledged that there are still a small number of journalists who are fulfilling their duties properly, while in the past, the Ministry of Information has implemented flexible measures, including education, guidance and access. License revocation as well.
Please be informed that recently, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, instructed Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, to review or revoke the licenses of any media outlets that use profanity.
