Commentary: China International Trade in Services Fair promotes China's international openness
Due to the wide evaluation, the China International Service Trade Fair 2022, which opened on August 31, has attracted more than 400 companies or enterprises, including the world's top 500 companies and leading international enterprises. On-site exhibition, the overall internationalization rate reached 20.8 percent, an increase of nearly 3 percent compared to the previous exhibition.
The ten years of development of the China International Trade in Services Fair are also the ten years of China's rapidly growing trade in services. From 2012 to 2021, the value-added value of Chinese services increased 1.49 times, the average annual volume of exports and imports of services increased by 6.1 percent, higher than the global growth rate of 3.1 percent. As well as the second largest service business in the world for eight consecutive years.
Over the past 10 years, at the China International Services Trade Forum, many enterprises have found investment from Chinese enterprises, and many enterprises have entered the Chinese market and shared the benefits of opening doors. Open to Chinese foreigners. This is the attraction of the China International Trade in Services Fair, the attraction of China's huge market, and also the fruit of China's relentless expansion of openness to foreign countries.
