Minister of Health: Under the care of the Royal Government, new modern hospital buildings are being built continuously to provide better health services to the people
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, stated that the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who always pays attention to the health of the people and Advise doctors to pay high attention to providing health services to people, especially the poor and disabled.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "Therefore, the Ministry is currently constructing new hospital buildings and equipping them with modern equipment at both the central and sub-national levels in response to government policies and requirements." Of people who come to receive services at hospitals.
In fact, by the end of 2022, the new 8-storey building of Ang Duong Hospital for general examination and treatment will be completed and another new building of 4-storey National Children's Hospital has been completed and is scheduled to be inaugurated soon. Coming soon. These two new hospital buildings are under the direct support of the Royal Government.
In addition, a number of new buildings are under construction, including the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, Calmette Hospital, University of Health Sciences, and hospital buildings in some provinces, such as Pailin, Tbong Khmum, Mondulkiri, Ratanakkiri, and Other provinces.
This statement was made by the professor on the occasion of inspecting the 8-storey polyclinic building at Ang Duong Hospital and the 4-storey building at the National Children's Hospital on September 1, 2022.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued that along with the expansion of modern hospital buildings, medical equipment, the Ministry must also train human resources to respond to the recent developments in the health sector, especially in response to the progress of the world. Mr. too.
"We will work to complete the construction of the hospital buildings by 2023, while the eight-storey hospital building at Ang Duong Hospital is scheduled to be completed by the end of this year to accommodate patients," he said. In a day, there are about 1,600 to 1,700 patients, including the poor, the disabled, factory workers and the general population.
Professor Lou Ly Kheang, Director of Preah Ang Duong Hospital, said that the eight-storey building was built in April 2021 and so far 90% completed with a budget of about 3 million US dollars from the Royal Government. .
He said that when the building is completed, the hospital will have 730 beds and become a modern public hospital among other public hospitals, especially to facilitate the hospitalization of patients to meet the needs. Of the people as well as improve the quality of services in the hospital to a better level.
