India launches tourism promotion program with Cambodia, strengthens cooperation after Kovid 19 failed
The event was held on the night of August 31, 2022 at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phuket, with the participation of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Ms. Tevyni Kopragade, Ambassador of India to Cambodia, Ms. Sushri Usha Thakur, Minister of Tourism and Culture of State Ambassador Ms. Chhay Sivalin, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association and several other representatives of tour companies in Cambodia.
Sheo Shekhar Shokla, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism and Culture of the Central State, told reporters that the fact that the Ministry of Tourism and Culture of the Central State of Cambodia is organizing a tour guide to the Central State of Cambodia is because the two countries have similar cultures. Having been in a relationship for thousands of years, this is also an opportunity to reminisce.
The Secretary of State said that the Ministry of Tourism and Culture of the Central State also intends to boost tourism cooperation with Cambodia after missing out on the Kovid 19 crisis for the past three years, especially with the Ministry of Tourism and the private sector. Tourism in Cambodia.
He said that Cambodians who come to India also have the opportunity to show their culture to India. In the central state of the country, there are many tourist destinations where tourists can visit and explore.
Ms. Chhay Sivalin said that through the promotion of India's tourism destinations, the Cambodian Tourism Association and the Cambodian Travel Agency have updated their tourism products to sell to tourists who want to visit India. Also show the mechanism of communication, address and location of tourist destinations to each other.
She said that through this program, the Cambodian Tourism Association expects to help accelerate the arrangement of direct flights between Cambodia and India to promote the movement of tourists from each other as tourists now have to go through. The second country comes first to India or to Cambodia.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also said that the current tour guide program will help promote the tourist destinations of the two countries and help strengthen the cooperation between Cambodia and India.
The Minister expressed confidence that the participation of the media, tourists, travel agencies, hotels and all stakeholders on the occasion will further increase the promotion of tourism destinations of the two countries, making the people of the two countries better known and understood. More specifically, strengthening the people-to-people exchanges as well as the flow of tourism between the two countries.
According to representatives from the Indian side, the Republic of India also plans to expand flights to Cambodia as well as neighboring countries. After the program, the Indian side will discuss with its government to open flights from the Indian state and other states in India to Cambodia and other ASEAN countries.
