The US Military Academy graduate emphasizes that every unit of the Army has its own core and special duties. The core task of the army is to defend the nation, religion, the king and the people. In addition to this core role, the bodyguards have another special role: to protect the national leadership, the legitimate head of government, from democratic and constitutional elections.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet said, "What is wrong with protecting the Prime Minister? The Prime Minister is born of democracy through the election of a legitimate Prime Minister. What is wrong? What is wrong with voting in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia? ”
"Millions of people voted for him democratically, in accordance with the constitution, he is a legitimate prime minister, the army is not wrong to protect him," he added. Legal power, power guaranteed by the constitution, power to serve the people. "If the power of the Prime Minister is legitimate, we will not protect anyone."
The future prime ministerial candidate from the Cambodian People's Party also stressed the importance of protecting the safety of national leaders. If the power of the national leader is not guaranteed, he will not be able to lead the nation for the benefit of the nation and the people.
"What if the power of the Prime Minister through the constitutional election does not protect that power to be strong?" If the Prime Minister or the President of a country where power is not strong, can he lead the management of national security and help the people? No, ”he said. Mr. Hun Manet confirmed.
For Cambodia, the security and safety of the Prime Minister is an important link to the national process because the Prime Minister is the leader who decides and executes the core tasks of the nation. If the Prime Minister faces a security threat, it will inevitably lead to chaos in the social process.
The Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces, a deep reformer in the Army, emphasized that protecting the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, is more than protecting the life of Samdech, that is, protecting the destiny of the nation and its people. Round once.
Mr. Hun Manet said, "When leading the nation, the life of the leader is no longer his life, it is the national life of the people of the public. "This protection is not only the life of the Prime Minister, but also the defense of the nation and the people, because he is the leader who must bear the fate of the motherland."
It should be noted that the Bodyguard Command, headed by General Hing Bun Heang, is an institution of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces under the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces General Command, established on September 4, 2009. In addition to the core work of defending the nation, religion, the King and the people, the Bodyguard Command also has a special duty to protect Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
