(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, together with relevant officials, on the morning of September 1, 2022, immediately intervened to open the water by adding additional drainage to save the rice fields of 31 hectares in Pong village, Steng commune. Chey, Cheung Prey district.
Mr. Prak Sarom, chief of Steung Chey commune, said that recently, more than 100 families in Pong village had submitted a letter to the commune authorities requesting to help widen the sewers across the road. Equally allow the water to flow faster to avoid flooding and damage to their rice fields due to flooding.
The commune chief said that at the request of such people, he took the request to the governor of Cheung Prey district to find a solution.
At the same time, the Governor of Cheang Prey District also took the request for advice from Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham. On September 1, 2022, it was found that the provincial governor had directly led the relevant officials to intervene and ordered the technical officer to control the excavator to install additional drainage according to the request of the people. Today.
The chief of Stung Chey commune confirmed that the rice crop of the people who are suffering from the flood is 31 hectares and can save about 70% by the intervention of the provincial governor now.
