(Phnom Penh): Once again, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the National Police General Commission, called on and reminded all private security agencies to continue to participate in disseminating the Royal Government of Cambodia's Safe Village-Commune / Sangkat Policy. Aims to participate in maintaining security and order in society.
The call of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey was made on the evening of August 31, 2022, on the occasion of the closing of the 41st Private Security Agency training course, which was also attended by many private security agent trainees.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey said, "Let all private security agencies participate in promoting and disseminating the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats, which is the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has been in place for many years, but is still popular." "Most popular, therefore, we all have a duty to participate in promoting, promoting and implementing."
