LONDON: A United Nations committee has said it is "deeply concerned" about the US Supreme Court's decision in June to end abortion rights nationwide, according to a report. Reuters released on Tuesday.
The report says the UN Commission on the Elimination of All Forms of Racial Discrimination has the effect that "the decision of the United States Supreme Court" has an impact on the sexual and reproductive health and rights of minorities, especially those with disabilities. "Low income."
The 18-member committee called on Washington to take specific steps to stop criminal prosecutions of women and abortion providers, the report said.
The UN body also called for compensation for black Americans as part of a broader effort to end centuries of slavery.
Battambang Provincial Governor Presides Over Groundbreaking Ceremony for Reinforced Concrete Roads and 136 Public Lighting Poles in Battambang City
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, on August 31, 2022, inaugurated the construction site of 3,410 meters long 7 meters wide reinforced concrete road and installed 136 public lighting poles in Sangkat Prek Preah Sdach, Battambang City. And O'Dambang 1 commune, Sangke district, Battambang province.
The Governor of Battambang Province expressed his pleasure to meet with civil servants, authorities and the people and also sent a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who always thinks of the well-being of the people. All circumstances.
