He added that the construction and repair of roads will be done in stages based on priorities. Apparently, this road is considered a priority because there are a lot of people living there and it is difficult to travel back and forth because there is a problem with the bank of Stung Sangke.
He also urged the relevant authorities, including communes, districts, municipalities, provincial public works and transport departments, provincial rural development departments, as well as the engineering force, to try to use their budgets to build and repair more roads in their jurisdictions. .
He added that the road will be equipped with 136 public lighting poles powered by electricity, which is the responsibility of the province. To alleviate the cost of electricity, he pointed out the use of intelligent light poles that can automatically turn on and off the lights and save energy when no driver is passing. This system will be studied to respond to the vision of the smart city of the province in the near future.
He also called on the relevant authorities to pay close attention to the problem of untidy construction and to avoid the construction of new buildings along the river. Existing old buildings should not be expanded into solid structures, and garbage should not be dumped under houses or in rivers, which will seriously affect the environment, beauty and tourism along the Sangke River.
