International aid agency urges Pakistani government to ease border restrictions with India for food imports
Pakistan: International aid agencies working to help hundreds of thousands of people displaced by devastating floods in Pakistan have demanded easing restrictions on food imports, a Pakistani minister has said. It borders India, its rival. This is according to the release by Reuters on Wednesday, August 31, 2022.
