Ministry of Foreign Affairs Reveals Outcome of Meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Delegation of Malaysian Investors and Representatives of Partner Companies in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on the morning of August 31, 2022, received a delegation of about 150 Malaysian investors and representatives of partner companies in Cambodia to pay a courtesy call and discuss work.
This business mission is organized by the Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia in collaboration with the Economic Diplomatic Coordination Team of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in order to promote the flow of bilateral trade and investment and explore the potential in Cambodia.
This is part of the implementation of the Economic Diplomacy Strategy 2021-2023, and this is the second business mission to Malaysia after its success. Of the first business mission of the Malaysian delegation from small and medium enterprises in April 2022.
The Deputy Prime Minister warmly welcomed the delegation and expressed his pleasure that the event was held on the occasion of Malaysia's National Independence Day, as 2022 marks the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries. The Deputy Prime Minister also praised the efforts of the Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia to promote the implementation of the economic diplomacy strategy.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that the Malaysian business mission reflects the high confidence of Malaysian investors in economic realities, political stability and socio-economic recovery strategies after the Kovid-19 crisis.
