The National Committee Against Torture has been assigned various roles and responsibilities by the Royal Government, including regular inspections of detention centers, prisons, and detention centers throughout Cambodia, and reports to the Royal Government on practical issues.
* This inspection mission aims to carry out its duties and responsibilities assigned by the Royal Government to ensure the prevention, prevention and complete elimination of all forms of torture and to strengthen the protection of those who have been deprived of their liberty. Free from torture in line with the Royal Government's policy to promote human rights and strengthen the rule of law in Cambodia.
* The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, is highly committed to respecting human rights and strengthening the rule of law, including the fight against torture, in accordance with the Universal Declaration on Human rights and the United Nations Convention against Torture.
For the fight against torture to be successful, we need the cooperation and active participation of all key players, especially the relevant authorities and law enforcement officers, and the unity to prevent and achieve The complete elimination of all forms of torture in Cambodia is a partnership with the Royal Government in promoting human rights and strengthening the rule of law in Cambodia.
