Chinese embassy: Cambodian corn allowed to export directly to China
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on August 30, 2022 confirmed that corn in Cambodia is allowed to export directly to China. This is according to the official Facebook post of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on August 30.
The Chinese Embassy wrote: "On August 27, the Chinese Customs Administration released a list of companies registered to export Cambodian corn to China, meaning that the Cambodian corn crop has completed its procedures. "All for export and allowed to export to China."
In addition, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia emphasized that this is the second Cambodian agricultural product to be allowed to be exported to China in 2022. The practical cooperation between China and Cambodia has increased new achievements. .
He also pointed out that until now, the Chinese side has increased the number of Cambodian agricultural products for direct export to the Chinese market, which previously imported these agricultural products to third countries and then re-exported to China.
So far, Cambodia's agricultural products that can be exported to China include: rice, cassava, cashew nuts, bananas and mangoes, while recently, Pailin lentils and trout have also been allowed to be imported by the Chinese side. China has also been waiting for the right time.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, red corn is an industrial crop with high market potential for processing into animal feed to supply the domestic market and export. Currently, the area under red corn is more than 140,000 hectares and there are export markets such as Thailand, Vietnam, Korea, Bangladesh. Cambodia always exchanges information with the meteorological powers, and the weather this week is calm, do not worry!
