(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, stated that Cambodia's success in selling carbon credits has raised Cambodia's national prestige on the international stage that not many countries in the world can do. Has and has resisted the campaign to discredit Cambodia in the image that Cambodia has the most forest crime in the world.
Mr. Net Pheaktra made this statement at a press conference on "Achievements of the Ministry of Environment for the past 5 years" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government this morning, August 30 at the office. Minister of Freedom Hall, Ground Floor.
He pointed out that since 2016, the Ministry of Environment has prepared and is implementing three REDD + projects, including: REDD + Keo Seima, REDD + Cardamom South and REDD + Prey Lang. The three REDD + projects have so far received about $ 11.6 million from the sale of carbon credits, of which these funds have been allocated.
Meanwhile, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that the three REDD + projects cover an area of about 1.27 million hectares, equivalent to 17.6 percent of the total area of protected areas. The Ministry of Environment is preparing an additional REDD + project on 1.19 million hectares, which will bring the total REDD project area to 2.46 million hectares (equivalent to 34.1% of the total protected area area). Out).
"This is an important turning point that Cambodia today, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has received revenue from its conservation and has been eliminating the view that only deforestation can bring income to the country." Proceeds from the protection and conservation of its forests under the slogan "Keep the trees standing for the benefit of the economy and society." This is an additional statement of Mr. Net Pheaktra.
Minister of Information Cremates Mr. Nhean Vibol, Advisor to the Ministry of Interior in Kampong Trabek District
(Prey Veng): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, on the afternoon of August 29, 2022, yesterday, led a delegation of the Ministry of Information to cremate Mr. Nhean Vibol (aka Chhoeu), Advisor to the Ministry of Interior, who recently passed away. Currently at the mortuary in Khlum village, Peam Mantear commune, Kampong Trabek district, Prey Veng province.
The Minister and all civil servants of the Ministry of Information are extremely saddened to learn that Mr. Nhean Vibol passed away at 9:30 pm on August 27, 2022 at the age of 68 By disease.
