Dr. Tan Monivann Calls on Local Enterprises to Strengthen Joint Capacity to Strengthen Cambodia's Economy
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Tan Monivann, Deputy General Director of Mong Reththy Group, on August 29, 2022, called on all enterprises in Cambodia to cooperate and strengthen the joint capacity to make the Cambodian economy stronger.
The call comes as Dr. Tan Monivann attends a press conference on the Cambodian Business Owners Forum on "Post-19 Challenges and Opportunities and the New Economic Wave."
Dr. Tan Monivann stated, "All enterprises must be able to work together for a strong economy, because major crises such as: Kovid-19 and the Russian war crisis between Ukraine, etc., we can not live alone, must learn to live with We will have to recognize each other, especially strengthen our joint capabilities. ”
In addition, Dr. Tan Monivann said that there are two crises, the first crisis is the global crisis and the second crisis is our own crisis to be solved, how to strengthen ourselves and how to do it. Know how to unite to make the Cambodian economy stronger.
Dr. Tan Monivann also called on traders and entrepreneurs to keep abreast of global trade, and called on traders and entrepreneurs to join the post-Kovid-19 Business Owners Forum and the new global economic wave to listen and find solutions together.
The founder and CEO of Home Education Enterprise, Mr. Kem Oeun, said that this business owner forum was held to inform traders that in the future, where is the SME development process? Where does the world economy go? Where is the economy of Cambodia's economic zone going? And has had both positive and negative effects on business owners.
In addition, Mr. Kem Oeun emphasized that this forum will help traders prepare for the challenges after the Kovid-19 crisis and the upcoming economic downturn and be ready to seize the opportunity. The program is also a platform for traders to present and promote products, as well as provide information on the protection mechanisms and policies of international institutions and the Royal Government.
The post-Kovid-19 Business Owners Forum and the New Global Economic Wave will be held on September 3, 2022 at the Phnom Penh Hotel. The forum will be held throughout the day and is expected to bring together about 10 business associations, policy makers, banks, entrepreneurs, business owners, donors, stakeholders and experts.
These 10 experts will share and debate on a variety of topics related to the challenges and opportunities after Kovid-19 and after the economic wave that affected it and its policies. What has the Royal Government prepared in helping SMEs that entrepreneurs should be prepared.
