Cambodia collects nearly $ 40 million from commercial gambling in the first half
(Phnom Penh): In the first half of 2022, the Cambodian Gambling Management Commission of the Ministry of Economy and Finance collected nearly 40 million US dollars from the gambling business in Cambodia. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which was received by Fresh News on August 29, 2022.
According to the same report, as of June 2022, the Commission for the Management of Commercial Gambling Cambodia received 142,202.11 million riels or more than 34 million US dollars.
According to the Ministry of Economy, in 2022, the Commission for the Management of Commercial Gambling of Cambodia has prepared a letter on the payment of the company's exclusive rights fee for the year 2021 with a total amount of $ 600,000 and prepared a reminder letter to the operator and / or owner. Twenty-two casinos have not yet paid their monthly gambling obligations to the state from January to May 2022.
During the past six months, the Cambodian Gambling Management Commission has inspected and evaluated the licensing applications of 125 casinos and 22 gambling companies, as well as reviewed and evaluated the application for renewal. Licenses for 2022 of operators and / or owners of casinos and gambling games, with the first phase decided to issue licenses to 13 casino companies.
