Kampong Cham Police Crack Down on Drug Cases, Detain 14 Suspects with 31 Packets of Drugs
(Kampong Cham): Police forces of Kampong Cham Provincial Police have launched an operation to crack down on one case of illegal drug trafficking at four different targets, leading to the arrest of 14 suspects with 31 packages of drugs.
The operation was carried out under the direct command of Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner, and ordered the specialized forces of the Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Office, the specialized forces of the Cheung Prey and Batheay District Police Inspectorates, and with the cooperation of the Muk Kampul District Special Forces. Kandal and two districts of Phnom Penh.
The report of Kampong Cham Provincial Police, obtained by Fresh News on August 29, 2022, said that the operation took place on August 26, with four targets, with a continuous cooperation for three days. A total of 14 suspects, 2 females, were arrested and the exhibits were confiscated, including 31 packages of white gram powder suspected to be drugs (a large package), a large number of packaging bags and 16 mobile phones.
At present, the suspects and exhibits have been compiled by the Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Office and the case has been sent to the court for legal action.
