A group of unions working in NagaWorld warns of suing unions that led former NagaWorld employees to strike and attack them
(Phnom Penh): A union that is currently working to serve and protect the interests of its employees in NagaWorld has been falsely accused and used inappropriate language by the leading union. Former NagaWorld employees have been on strike in recent months.
Heng Sophini, President of the NagaWorld Workers' Rights and Common Interests Union, held a press conference in front of NagaWorld this morning, saying that her union had been subjected to unreasonable allegations by the unions. Leading former NagaWorld employees on strike as a non-independent union and a union-sponsored union.
In response to this allegation, Ms. Heng Sophini stated that her union was formed by the founding members to participate in the election and to prepare the registration documents at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training in accordance with the Constitution, the Labor Law and the Union Law, in particular. In line with the wishes of the staff of the entire NagaWorld Company.
Regarding the word “independent union” or not, Ms. Heng Sophini stated that in the labor law, the law on unions and in the statutes of all unions, it is not just her union, if it does not prove its independence, it is an institution. Absolutely unlisted, do not talk about actions.
Ms. Heng Sophini urged individuals who repeatedly attacked her union leaders to stop immediately and if they continued to engage in verbal attacks that harmed her union name, they would take action. Legally, both individuals can also sue to dissolve their professional organizations in accordance with the law on unions.
Finally, Ms. Heng Sophini, on behalf of the union leaders, the rights and interests of NagaWorld employees, once again called on all NagaWorld employees to continue to participate in order to maintain and protect their careers. Survive through hard work, respect all laws, regulations and legal documents in force.
