Electric house fire burns down a house selling furniture, destroying a lot of property in Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province
(Koh Kong): A power outage caused a fire in a house selling no furniture and destroyed a lot of property, but this case did not cause any injuries. This incident happened at 5:15 on August 28, 2022 in Village 3, Sangkat Dang Tong, Khemarak Phoumin Municipality, Koh Kong Province.
The owner of the house is Seng Chheng, male, 56 years old, and his wife is Pen Vuchly, 54 years old.
Koh Kong provincial police chief Lt. Gen. Kong Mono said the fire did not cause any deaths or injuries, only damage to household items and furniture, and did not spread to neighboring homes. Because the special intervention force of the provincial police commissioner and the city inspector force intervened to put out the fire in time by using water for 5 vehicles and the fire was successfully extinguished at 7 o'clock.
According to the fire brigade, the fire was caused by an electric shock and the house was 7 meters by 35 meters in size. The provincial police commissioner would like to call on people from all walks of life to be careful with the electricity system, tea, incense, gas stoves to be very careful to protect better than loss.
