Duke Kouch Mengly: In a time of peace, young people have many opportunities to work hard
(Phnom Penh): Duke Dr. Kouch Mengly said that in the era of complete peace in the country, young people have a lot of opportunities, so young people must strive for a better future in life.
Speaking on August 27, 2022, Mr. Kouch Mengly recalled Cambodia's past during the war and he was one of those who had lived under the influence of the war. He says during the war, people did not have enough time to learn, only to be ready to hide under the trenches to escape the bullets.
Mr. Kouch Mengly said that unfortunately staying in the camp for a week was also transported by Thai soldiers to drop the Dangrek mountain, contrary to the expectation to go to the third country of freedom and peace. He said that wandering in the bamboo forest, sleeping in the water, begging, combined with life from childhood and going through the black-shirt regime of his youth and family were the effects of the war.
In this era of peace, Mr. Kouch Mengly also urged young people to strive to develop themselves to have the opportunity to become business owners, business owners, politicians, professors, economists, researchers and many other positions to contribute to building society. He does not want to see foreigners become leaders in some companies or private institutions in Cambodia.
