(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction revealed that in the first half of Cambodia, it approved about 2,000 investment projects in the construction sector on a total construction area of about 2.8 million square meters under an investment capital of 1 , $ 206 million.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents of Cambodia, said that if you look at the report of the Ministry of Land Management in the first half of this year, the number of applications for investment projects in the construction sector. Slightly lower than in 2021.
However, Mr. Chrek Soknim claimed that this was just a sign of the proposal to restart investment projects in the construction sector in the first half of 2022.
He expressed the expectation that construction investment projects in Cambodia will continue to increase by the end of 2022 or in 2023.
In addition, Mr. Chrek Soknim emphasized that the application for construction investment project is not yet completed because the application is sometimes implemented and sometimes delayed.
He said that the most important point is that the implementation of all these proposed projects is an important factor in boosting the Cambodian economy, especially the construction and real estate sector to grow.
As for the current real estate situation, he sees that the flow of exchanges has slowed down a bit and most of the investors are Cambodians and a large number of foreigners are declining.
According to the Royal Government, the construction sector is expected to continue to recover at 7.2 percent in 2023 due to the expected recovery of foreign investment flows for construction for tourism and trade.
The real estate sector, meanwhile, is expected to recover by 5.2 percent due to a recovery in high-end real estate buying and selling activity.
Speaking at a press conference on "Achievements of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction" for the past five years, Mr. Ly Raksmey, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, stated that the country plays the largest role in investing in Cambodia's construction and real estate sector: China, South Korea, Japan and Thailand, and has been actively involved in the development of the Cambodian economy.
