Senior official of the National Bank of Cambodia: Riel is widely used on people's daily expenses
(Kampot): Dr. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that currently the riel is widely used for the daily expenses of the people. In fact, according to a survey by the National Bank of Cambodia and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), people in Kampot use about 80 percent of their daily expenses in riel.
Dr. Chea Serey's remarks were made during a program on the riel in Kampot province on August 27, 2022 to celebrate the 42nd riel day of the re-introduction of the riel and the promotion of the riel. Understand the riel more widely throughout the country, including the participation of Ms. You Sokun, Deputy Governor of Kampot.
Dr. Chea Serey said, “For Kampot province, the data show that people use at least 80% of the daily expenses in riel, and the income and operating expenses of banking and financial institutions in Kampot province are in riel. "There is a significant increase in 2021, the income in riel increased by 70 percent compared to 2017, while expenditure in riel increased by 47 percent."
She added that the circulation of the riel went through several stages, such as the first official launch, the elimination of traffic during the Pol Pot genocidal regime, which led to Cambodia's decline in society, slavery, tragedy and the destruction of all achievements. Economy and society and the official resumption of the riel on March 20, 1980.
Dr. Chea Serey stated that these proud achievements could not be achieved if Cambodia did not have peace, political stability, macroeconomic stability and development in all areas under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister. People and investors have stronger confidence in the riel and the future of the Cambodian economy.
Ms. You Sokun said that spending riel in Kampot is a lot to be proud of, especially daily expenses. She reminded the people and enterprises present in Kampot province to continue to use the riel instead of foreign currency more.
"The economy of the region or Kampot province, in particular, could not function smoothly without the national currency acting as a lubricant to facilitate investment, production and trade activities," she said. Banteay Meanchey Provincial Commissioner Urges Municipal-District Police Inspectors to Properly Manage and Register the Permanent Residence of Foreigners Coming to Work or Doing Local Business
