(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out in a car dealership, destroying 12 cars and two motorcycles, which occurred at 1:50 am on August 27, 2022. Located along Street 273, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that upon receiving information from residents, a fire was burning in a car dealership near the Tuol Kork antenna. He also ordered the fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police at all targets to intervene.
Colonel Prohm Yorn also said that in this operation, it is difficult for our special forces to intervene in time because the electricity has not been turned off, so it is difficult for fire trucks to put out and the flames. The fire spread rapidly to neighboring car dealerships. However, our professional forces are still trying to intervene to prevent the devil from spreading to other people's warehouses.
Colonel Prohm Yorn also confirmed that during this operation, the police used more than 20 fire trucks, including 15 fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Office, using 15 trucks equal to 60 cubic meters of water. And a car of the Cambodian Beer Company uses 1 truck equal to 4 cubic meters of water and was completely extinguished at 2:35 pm on the same day.
The colonel confirmed that in the case of the above fire, the car dealership and all the damaged equipment with the size (10m x 20m) were made of galvanized iron. The cause of the fire is being investigated. More than 50 Japanese companies seek investment opportunities in Cambodia
