(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Women's Affairs on August 26, 2022 issued a press release completely denying the allegations made by this handful of individuals against the competent authorities and the Ministry of Women's Affairs. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Women's Affairs, obtained by Fresh News.
On the morning of August 25, 2022, a handful of young people staged a performance in front of the Ministry of Women's Affairs and used the media and social media to spread propaganda about their activities. Of the competent authority and the Ministry of Women's Affairs.
The Ministry of Women's Affairs would like to categorically deny the allegations made by this handful of individuals against the competent authorities and the Ministry of Women's Affairs without clear basis and evidence, especially the recent scene in front of the Ministry of Women's Affairs. Depriving the truth, intentionally slandering, inciting, confusing the public and seriously affecting the honor and dignity of the competent authorities and the Ministry of Women's Affairs.
In the past, the Ministry of Women's Affairs, which is the staff of the Royal Government, has actively worked in accordance with its mandate, achieving many proud achievements in improving the status of women and the protection of the rights of women and girls in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Ministry of Women's Affairs has never been indifferent and always focused on promoting the protection of women's rights, cooperating with relevant institutions and supporting services for women and girls affected by gender-based violence at all levels without discrimination on the basis of race or color. Any color or political situation.
Once again, the Ministry of Women's Affairs strongly rejects and denies the allegations made by a handful of individuals against the competent authorities and the Ministry of Women's Affairs, and calls on the public not to believe the unfortunate propaganda slander. These.
The Ministry of Women's Affairs strongly believes that the public, both at home and abroad, will continue to support and trust the Ministry of Women's Affairs to continue its mission to achieve more new achievements for the country.
