Ukrainian leader Zelensky has said that the generator at the reserve plant could bring electricity to the line, but that Russia has forced all of Ukraine and Europeans in danger of nearing national catastrophe. "Nuclear radiation." Atomic energy experts say they must hurry to check the situation at the plant as soon as possible to avoid the risk of destruction.
A nuclear power plant is a plant that uses uranium fuel to generate steam for electricity. This process converts uranium into various radioactive substances. If an explosion occurs at the plant, its heat and pressure will rise and water vapor, along with radioactive substances, and gases will endanger human health.
This weekend, during a telephone conversation between Russian leader Vladimir Putin and French leader Emmanuel Macron, Russian President Vladimir Putin confirmed that he had agreed to allow UN nuclear experts to enter the plant. . The head of the IAEA Atomic Energy Agency, Rafael Grossi, said on August 25 that he planned to visit the plant site.
Botum Sakor District Authorities Apply Albert on Bottles of Pools in Homes to Prevent Dengue and Malaria As the Rainy Season Comes
(Koh Kong): Mr. Hak Leng, Governor of Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province, on August 26, 2022, led the counseling and health officials, students, launched a campaign to put albatross in water bottles, pools in the homes of people to prevent malaria. As the rainy season approaches.
The district governor called on residents to take care of the environment to live well by cleaning around the house with wild grass and burying old cans that hold water, which is a source of tiger mosquitoes. On the other hand, always sleep under a mosquito net to prevent malaria, dengue fever, especially to maintain regular hygiene according to the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent Kovid 19.
