The inspections over the past four days were led by:
* First: Mr. Thou Mony, President of the Parliament of Inquiry and Vice President of the Battambang Court of Appeal * Second: Mr. Nhoung Thul, Deputy President of the Court of Appeal of Battambang * Third: Mr. Neou Monichout, Judge of the Court of Appeal of Battambang and some other working groups In collaboration with the President, Vice-Presidents, Judges, Clerks and officials of Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Siem Reap Provincial Courts.
Ms. Teang Sambo, Secretary General of Administration of the Court of Appeal of Battambang, said that the inspection is very important for the justice sector and with the direct guidance of Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice recently.
The purpose of this inspection is to strengthen the law enforcement work to effectively link the investigation of the Battambang Court of Appeal with the Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Siem Reap Provincial Courts:
* Examine the achievements and challenges in the past performance of the investigating judges * Examine the case processing procedures and detention procedures to continue during the investigation phase * Promptly investigate the investigating judge's actions as instructed Of the Minister of Justice * Examine and guide the proper appeal and send the case to the Court of Appeal as soon as possible * Solve various challenges.
