(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Civil Social Networking Association, which has about 168 members, has invited other civil society organizations to join it to become a service to the best interests and national interests in order to contribute to the development of Cambodia. Moving forward proudly.
The Cambodian Civil Society Network was established on July 22, 2022, recognized by the Ministry of Interior to mobilize and strengthen the solidarity of civil society organizations, including: organizations, associations, communities, unions and indigenous peoples to contribute to Promote the prestige and sustainable development of good governance and the rule of law in Cambodia.
Speaking to the press at a press conference on the morning of August 26, 2022, Mr. Tum Pen Virak Tou, President of the Cambodian Civil Society Network, stated that the voice of civil society organizations is very important to contribute to the development of the country with the Royal Government. According to various requests related to society to be a mirror in law enforcement and so on.
He said that the civil society network facilitates the harmonization of civil society networks and facilitates cooperation with civil society to meet the real needs of society and contribute to the development of Cambodian society with sustainability, democracy and the rule of law. With the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Cambodian civil society network for the public good.
He said that the Cambodian Civil Society Network has recruited about 168 members who are satisfied with the principles, directions and activities and have volunteered to join the Cambodian Civil Society Network. More importantly, the Cambodian Civil Society Network will organize training for all members to know how to plan, collaborate and coordinate from all walks of life in order to make the member civil society better.
In the past, the Cambodian civil society network has also observed that the current civil society is not yet interconnected. Therefore, the Cambodian Civil Society Network calls on all civil society groups to join the Cambodian civil society network for the greater good of the nation and to uphold the national interest, and to participate in building the development of Cambodia with pride.
