(Kandal): Ms. San Arun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, stated that in order for people to stop using tobacco, a win-win measure for public health and for the Royal Government is to increase taxes on tobacco products because raising taxes will help people People stop spending money on cigarettes, which are unnecessary products and can reduce young people from wanting to try cigarettes.
Ms. San Arun added that raising the tobacco tax will ease the burden on the government, especially to reduce tobacco use to a low level, while the use of tobacco causes economic losses and serious health risks, which is a burden for The Royal Government must resolve. In this sense, we must continue to work to protect the health of all people and protect young people from falling into the trap of tobacco.
Ms. San Arun added that tobacco use can lead to premature death, cancer, heart disease, stroke and chronic respiratory disease. In Cambodia, tens of thousands of people die from tobacco use and lose millions of dollars each year.
