The National Election Committee (NEC) today convened a meeting chaired by NEC Chairman Prach Chan to review and decide on the results of the short-term contract officer recruitment work at the Secretariat. Capital and provinces will hold 25 elections for the 2022 voter list and voter registration review.
According to the NEC, the examination process was conducted in two groups, with one group from 13 provinces to hold the exam on August 17, 2022 and the other group from 12 provinces to organize the exam on August 19, 2022 As a result, a total of 527 candidates have passed the exam as short-term contract officers working in the 25 provincial and provincial election secretariats for the 2022 voter list and voter registration examination.
