Samdech Techo Hun Sen Supports Opening of Turkish Commercial Office in Cambodia to Expand Trade and Investment Potential (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, supports the opening of Turkish Commercial Office in Cambodia Better trade and investment potential between the two countries.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's support was made during a working meeting with Ms. Ulku Kocaefe, Turkish Ambassador to Cambodia. On the morning of August 25, 2022, Ms. Ukul Kocha Ephe paid a courtesy call and discussed with Samdech Techo after her visit to Cambodia in July.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Personal Assistant to the Prime Minister, during the meeting, the Turkish Ambassador expressed her commitment to improve relations, cooperation and friendship between the two countries.
"Cambodia and Turkey still have a lot of potential for cooperation," she said. She added that through a number of agreements already signed, she will work to tap those potentials to boost cooperation between the two countries.
The ambassador also said that Turkey will open a trade office in Cambodia to promote cooperation in all fields, both bilaterally, regionally and globally.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Congratulates Ms. Ou Kulkoja Efe on her appointment as the new Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Turkey to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the same view as the Ambassador that Cambodia and Turkey still have a lot of potential for expanding and strengthening cooperation. In this regard, Samdech Techo welcomed the Turkish Chamber of Commerce and hoped that the Chamber of Commerce will study and understand all cooperation in the fields of economy, trade and investment, which are the foundation of cooperation in other fields.
Mr. Hun Many remembers the story that made Samdech Techo Hun Sen lose confidence for 3 years when he was an assistant (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): At the launching ceremony of Hun Many's book of hope in Siem Reap, Mr. Hun Many shared and recalled his experience Some mistakes while working as an assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister. Mr. Hun Many reminded that the waste of work made Samdech Techo lose confidence in him for 3 years.
Mr. Hun Many said that when he joined the Prime Minister's Office in 2008, he had only two roles: first, to hold the briefcase for Samdech Techo and second, to wake Samdech Techo.
Mr. Hun Many said, "I am a very disciplined person and have a clear work ethic. He not only uses clear words, he uses certain words, and this, as a secretary, must be certain, because in order to avoid him for a long time. ! Or blame something else.
Mr. Hun Many also gave wisdom that do not underestimate the small work because it helps to train clearly before moving on to the next big and small tasks.
In addition, Mr. HUN Many shared his experience of two mistakes while working in the cabinet of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mistake 1: It involves time to go to work. Mr. Hun Many reminded that in his country, he had to drive with Samdech Techo to attend meetings or to meet with foreign delegates or development partners or to meet with the people. The program must start at 8:30 and more than that, must travel on the road for half an hour before Samdech Techo leaves at 7:30.
The youngest son of Samdech Techo's three brothers recalled that when he started working at Samdech Techo's cabinet, he had interrupted twice, the first time he could not go, the second time he rode to the program. And but did not dare to enter, so he had to cross twice or note the mistake twice.
The second mistake that Hun Many made was his failed experience. Because he had studied international relations abroad at one time, Samdech Techo filed a case study on the situation of a country facing a political crisis (he asked not to be named) and there will be a new leader who is the son of the boss. Old leadership.
At the time, Mr. Hun Many simply said, "I do not know which one will go up, but it seems that this one will go up." The prince did not say a word, ate a quick meal and walked away. After that, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, the mother, re-explained to Mr. Hun Many all the facts.
Mr. Hun Many stated that he was really sorry for his irresponsible answer to Samdech Techo Hun Sen as his father. "For three years, trust was lost because my answer was irresponsible," he said.
Mr. Hun Many pointed out that a job that if he did not study in depth, is uncertain, and he dares to give advice to the management without clarity, that will lead the management to make the wrong decision, it will lead to wrong decisions. Towards a major disaster.
"If I did not study in depth, there is no certainty on the information, and I dare to give advice to senior management without certainty and could lead him to judge and make wrong decisions, this is my biggest mistake," he said. "
In other words, Mr. Hun Many would like to share the wisdom to all young people that as a leader, any person who provides information that can lead to wrong decisions is a big risk for decision making.
According to the "Book of Hope of Hun Many", Mr. Hun Many had studied in the French Republic and the United States and joined the Cabinet of Prime Minister Hun Sen in 2008.
