(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has become a success story in Southeast Asia for its way of dealing with the Kovid 19 pandemic. Analysts praised the Cambodian government's success in its highly effective vaccination campaign. This is according to the release by CGTN on Wednesday, August 24, 2022.
For a country that relies on tourism for about one-fifth of its gross domestic product (GDP), Cambodia has quickly and remarkably addressed the Kovid 19 crisis.
Cambodia fully reopened its economy on November 1, 2021, a few months before its other neighbors in Southeast Asia began to open and abolished the requirement to isolate vaccinated passengers. Complete prevention.
The Cambodian government has been continuing to provide people with the fourth or fifth dose of the vaccine to fight the disease 19 and to rehabilitate the economy.
