Biden announces nearly $ 3 billion in arms aid to Ukraine to mark Kiev's Independence Day
Kiev: US President Joe Biden celebrated Ukraine's Independence Day on Wednesday, announcing a nearly $ 3 billion security aid package to support Kiev's fight against Russian aggression. This is according to the release by The HILL on Wednesday, August 24, 2022.
The White House announcement comes as Ukraine prepares for more Russian attacks on its Independence Day, which also coincides with the six-month start of Moscow's military campaign.
Biden said in a statement Wednesday morning announcing a $ 2.98 billion arms and military package for Ukraine. "Over the past six months, the people of Ukraine have inspired the world with their great courage and dedication to freedom," he said.
The package represents the single largest US aid to Ukraine since the start of the Russian war in February. Biden said it would allow Ukraine to acquire additional air defense systems, artillery and drone systems, as well as radar.
