Many farmers in Angsnoul district, Kandal province receive training on earthworm farming techniques
(Kandal): Many farming families in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, have been trained in worm farming techniques and received vegetable seeds from NagaWorld with a generous heart, which is part of NagaWorld's social work.
"We would like to thank NagaWorld for this important initiative of a generous heart that provides a lot of knowledge and benefits to the people in our community," said San Vanthul, Deputy Governor of Ang Snoul District.
San Vanthul added that donating vegetable seeds will allow people to grow crops to increase their income, while raising earthworms is a new way to improve our agriculture.
Ongoing programs include: worm farming techniques and vegetable seed donation. The first program: is to provide a workshop on worm farming techniques. When earthworms eat decaying material (taken from the kitchen), cow dung or straw, etc., earthworms will release manure that contains many nutrients.
The manure will become a natural fertilizer and the soil will be fertile for crops and vegetables. This method reduces waste and reduces its burning, which affects the environment and health. In addition, farmers spend the least amount of capital raising worms, and they will also be able to sell worms as fish feed, which can increase additional sources of income.
The second program: is to donate vegetable seeds. This is a program that comes from the participation of NagaWorld staff who participated in the gym during the closure of Kovid-19 last year. The number of hours or distance of their exercise, such as walking, running or cycling, is calculated as the number of vegetable seeds to be distributed to many families in Ang Snoul district.
Pern Chen, Managing Director of NagaWorld, said that when more employees join the gym, it means they can find more vegetable seeds for local farmers in Ang Snoul. Many of our employees participate in exercise and maintain an active and healthy lifestyle during the closure. They work hard to stay healthy and help their community.
It should be noted that this workshop on worm farming techniques and vegetable seed donation was held on August 20, 2022 at Ang Snoul District Hall, Kandal Province. Acting Head of State issues Royal Decree appointing Lt. Gen. Em Vichet as Inspector General of the Ministry of Interior, replacing Mr. Iv Lao, appointed Undersecretary of State
