The private sector is an important and indispensable sector in pushing agriculture forward, growing and succeeding.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ngor Bunthan, Rector of the Royal University of Agriculture, said that the agricultural sector can grow and move forward depending on the indispensable participation of the private sector without the participation of the private sector. Can not lead to goals and success.
Dr. Ngor Bunthan made the remarks during the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between Davan Company and the Royal University of Agriculture on the project to use resources to improve food security and the agricultural value chain in Cambodia on the 24th. August 2022.
Dr. Ngor Bunthan said, "The national economy, the agricultural sector, can not move forward without the participation of the private sector. "Agricultural exports must have private import-export companies, such as bananas, mangoes to China, must rely on private companies that are technically responsible to export."
Dr. continued that until now, the Royal University of Agriculture has cooperated with many partners, the company that provides cooperation in the field of agriculture and promote the growth of agriculture, the Royal University of Agriculture has cooperated with both companies. That. Collaborating with private companies and universities in order to generate income and increase the agricultural sector.
Dr. confirmed that today, the Royal University of Agriculture has established a new cooperation with Davan on the project to use resources to improve food safety and agricultural value chain in Cambodia.
Chheng Makara, CEO of Davan, said that the Cambodian economy has grown rapidly in the last two decades under the political, social stability and complete shadow of peace. $ 25 billion, of which agriculture contributes 22% of GDP.
He said that while the country is continuing to develop and grow its economy as a whole, the agricultural sector seems to be less developed in line with overall growth, but instead faces major challenges in a complex situation.
He added that due to the low investment in the agricultural sector, the food safety situation was not improving and was not fast enough to adapt to the overall development. The general population is concerned about food hazards, but does not have the means or knowledge to achieve food safety goals while the food system is not yet in good condition.
Seeing this situation, Davan has launched a food safety mission in every home and people are healthier and live longer. This mission is based on a strong commitment to address the growing concerns of food safety. .
