The Kovid 19 crisis, which began in 2020, has severely affected sectors in Cambodia as well as the world. The construction sector also faces some obstacles.
However, in Cambodia, only Sihanoukville has the largest number of buildings, about 80 to 100 unfinished, while in Phnom Penh and other provinces are not obstructed. This is according to the spokesperson of the Ministry of Land Management.
The problem of unfinished construction in Sihanoukville, which has the highest number, was confirmed by Mr. Seng Lot because the coastal province has grown and the construction is the most in the past. This.
The spokesman also claimed that some buildings were suspended for a while, but later were rebuilt like this, and soon 80 to 100 buildings in Sihanoukville will be able to Construction is completed as planned by the private sector, which strives to meet demand.
According to Seng Lot, the spread of Kovid 19 has had a global impact, not only in Cambodia, but also in the real estate and other sectors, which has resulted in the failure to complete some construction.
