(Phnom Penh): In the first half of January to June 2022, Cambodia approved about 2,000 construction investment projects on a total construction area of about 2.8 million square meters under an investment capital of 1 , $ 206 million. This was confirmed by Mr. Ly Raksmey, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Ly Raksmey attending the press conference on "Achievements of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction" for the past 5 years at the Office of the Council of Ministers, Freedom Hall, Ground floor this morning. This August 24, 2022.
Mr. Ly Reaksmey pointed out that the countries that play the biggest role in investment in construction and real estate in Cambodia, first: China, second: South Korea, third: Japan, and then Thailand and the sector. This has contributed to the active development work in the Cambodian economy.
According to a senior official at the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, according to a report released by the National Bank of Cambodia, the inflow of foreign direct investment in 2019 increased by 12% to 3%. .5 billion US dollars.
Of that, 2.3 billion US dollars in foreign direct investment (FDI) went into the financial sector, with China being the largest source of foreign direct investment at 43%. South Korea has 11 percent, Vietnam 7 percent, Japan and Singapore 6 percent.
Mr. Ly Reaksmey also said that in the context of the country, which has achieved political stability, social security, has made significant progress in the construction sector, and this sector is an important part contributing to Develop the economy by fulfilling the basic purpose of social development by creating a lot of jobs for the people.
In addition, Mr. Ly Raksmey said that the sector has also increased the income of the society in relation to social services and also actively participated in the national economic growth, especially related to investment in Construction sector.
In the last five years, investment in the construction sector has reached 19,322 projects with a construction area of 71,459,233 square meters, with an investment of 31,484 million US dollars as follows:
From the beginning of the year 2000 to the first six months of 2022, 57,590 construction permits were issued nationwide, with a total construction area of 166,623,891 square meters and a total investment capital of 66,205 million US dollars.
Nationwide, there are 2,472 high-rise buildings with 5 storeys and above, 482 Borey-style housing projects and suburban housing projects, and construction business licenses have been issued to construction companies studying design and construction projects. 3,244 companies.
