Commentary: Why is China's inflation rate lower than other countries in the current context?
Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Research Association, analyzed that the two main reasons for China's low inflation are: food security and Chinese-style development, adding that there are five Chinese-style developments. Key points.
First, innovative development, as we know, China now uses a variety of technologies, including space technology, that can easily communicate from space to Earth, and at the same time, innovative development. With this innovation, we see that in the fields of Chinese fields today, there is no longer a hustle and bustle of farmers because he has used technology without having to open it by humans.
For example, unmanned tractors are an important point in which he can increase the growth associated with his agricultural products. His artificial intelligence, AI, even passenger cars do not need a driver, and a team of robotic doctors are now working to provide medical care to the Chinese people.
Second, harmonious development is about how to make each situation unique, manageable, and close the gap between rich and poor, between urban and rural people.
Dr. Chea Monirith stated that the overall food security with the five developments arising from the development experience of the past, present and future reflects the in-depth understanding of the Chinese leadership regarding governance in the field. The economy is based on the rule of law, pedagogy, and social development, focusing on security solutions, especially the maintenance of food security that China has been through for thousands of years.
