* Second: Strengthening the capacity of human resources by focusing on data management as well as the distribution and exchange of information in depth at both the national and sub-national levels, as well as in coordination with all stakeholders in the assignment. Intervention within the framework and jurisdiction of social services and social assistance.
* Third: Increasing cooperation to manage hazards and define the roles and responsibilities of relevant institutions in all social sectors on the basis of national and international legislation.
* Fourth: Continuing to strengthen multi-faceted risk management methods, taking into account economic and social vulnerabilities, as well as assessing the level of vulnerability and risk to prepare for responding to client situations at all stages of the case. Effective.
