On the morning of Wednesday, August 24, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), paid a courtesy call on Liu Jianchao, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the CPC Central Committee. Discuss work. The meeting was held in a cordial manner and discussed frankly on issues related to bilateral, regional and global frameworks.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, told the media that during this meeting, Mr. Liu Cheanchao informed Samdech Techo about the different situation in Cambodia in 2004 when he first arrived in Cambodia and now.
Mr. Liu Cheanchao informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen that on his visit to Cambodia, he now saw that Cambodia had changed dramatically. Mr. Liu Jianchao highlighted that Cambodia today has a prosperous, beautiful economy, urban growth, a fresh population development.
The senior Chinese official also noted that Cambodia now plays an increasingly important role and is recognized internationally.
"These results reflect the correct leadership of Samdech Techo and should be a model for developing countries." This is what Mr. Liu Cheanchao said, quoted by Mr. Eang Sophalleth.
Liu Jianchao also said that economic development basically meets the needs of the Cambodian people. In this regard, the Chinese side will continue to strengthen economic cooperation with Cambodia, especially to promote the export of agricultural products to the Chinese market, establish direct flights to Cambodia, encourage Chinese investors to Cambodia and help develop green energy. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the progress of Cambodia, which is the result of the tireless efforts of the leaders and civil servants as a whole.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also agreed with the concept of economic development to serve the needs of the people. Samdech Techo thanked the Chinese government and people for always supporting Cambodia's development. He also called on China to continue to expand cooperation in trade, investment, tourism and green energy in Cambodia to promote Cambodia's economic growth and improve people's lives.
