The United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) said on Tuesday that calls for help for Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh were "insufficient" as refugees called on donors not to do so. Forget about the crisis ahead of the fifth anniversary of their departure from Myanmar. This is according to a report released by AFP on Tuesday, August 23, 2022.
More than 1 million Rohingya refugees live in refugee camps in southern Bangladesh, the world's largest refugee camp, with little hope of returning to their country of origin (Myanmar). ) Which is largely deprived of citizenship and other rights.
"Nearly 1 million stateless Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh are in dire straits and they are still completely dependent on humanitarian assistance for their survival," the UNHCR said.
The UNHCR said its 2022 response plan sought more than $ 881 million for more than 1.4 million people, including Rohingya refugees and more than half a million, the most affected host communities. So far, the fund has received only 49 percent of the $ 426.2 million.
Most of the Rohingya fled to neighboring Bangladesh during the 2017 military crackdown by Myanmar, which the United Nations said was carried out with genocidal intent. Court of Appeal upholds the decision of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to sentence Ho Van and more than 10 opposition groups to 20 months to 2 years in prison, but some have been suspended
