In a statement, China's National Energy Administration acknowledged the challenges of power supply caused by high temperatures and lack of hydropower, Bloomberg reported.
China will accelerate hydropower and nuclear projects while pushing for more transmission lines across the region and expanding renewable energy capabilities such as wind and solar power in a matter of years, the Energy Administration said. Ahead. China has also pledged to balance supply and demand nationwide by 2025.
Sichuan, which relies on hydropower for 82% of its energy generation, is experiencing its worst drought in more than half a century as temperatures soared above 40 degrees Celsius.
Sichuan has declared its highest emergency and ordered a halt to industrial production to ensure electricity can be supplied to households, affecting the supply of auto parts and essential equipment. According to Bloomberg News.
