Ministry of Economy organizes "Awareness on FMIS" program for public, municipal, district and khan administrative institutions
In this program, the Secretary of State highlighted the benefits of FMIS for Cambodia as a whole and provided many benefits for individual users. FMIS users will benefit from:
1: Provide financial information and budget implementation information quickly and in various forms, both brief and detailed, both national and sub-national, at the level of ministries-institutions and budget units, both by sector and by budget content that provides the basis Clear for management to analyze, reach decisions in a timely and confident manner.
2. Strengthen the accountability, transparency and ownership of the implementation of the budget through the operation and flow of work in the system from the establishment to the end of each operation, which is clearly recorded and monitored in conjunction with the correct monitoring system along the trajectory. Audit and reduce the culture of accusations or pointing fingers.
3: Provide a digital nursery to orient the work digitally, which will reduce the use of paper documents and reduce the steps and busyness in duplicate work, which will increase the productivity of some additional work to the organization as well. Participated in a change that is beneficial for the country.
4. Provide automatic control of budget loans according to budget classification and reduce the complexity of various calculations or records, such as multi-tier budget implementation, program budget implementation, and budget unit expansion. Provides easy retrieval of data and operations.
5: Provide opportunities for capacity development of officials, because the participation in the implementation of information technology systems requires the constant development of the capacity of relevant officials, in which the FMIS project management team will organize training courses for the implementation of the stage. First, as well as a series of refresher courses.
