(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Khon Dara, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Anti-Drug Committee and the Committee on Combating AIDS and STIs of the Ministry of Interior, expressed his deep concern over the rapidly evolving drug situation in the region. Affected Cambodia.
Mr. Kao Khon Dara expressed his concern about the drug problem during the meeting on monitoring and strengthening the mechanism of the Anti-Drug Committee and the Committee on Combating AIDS and STIs on 23 August 2022 .
Kao Khon Dara said that with the crisis of the 19 epidemics of Kovid, which has been causing serious health and socio-economic hardships, crime and crime, production, trafficking and drug use in the region. And in the whole world there is also a significant increase.
In addition, Mr. Kao Khon Dara confirmed that the traffic, processing, production and trafficking of large cases were law enforcement authorities to crack down effectively and timely. However, the case of small-scale distribution and use of drugs in some villages, communes, sangkats of the capital-province is still a great annoyance and concern of the people and guardians who need to continue to consider and take further appropriate action.
Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea, director of the Secretariat of the Anti-Drug Committee, said that the production of synthetic drugs more active in the Golden Triangle is having a greater impact on countries in the region, including Cambodia.
The general continued that the Golden Triangle has recently turned from the production of opium or drugs from natural production to the production of synthetic drugs, so Cambodia also suffered greatly as they transported. Come to Cambodia and transport to third countries by water and air, while there are also attempts to use Cambodia as a place for processing.
General Neak Yuthea added that the amount of drugs seized in Cambodia is increasing, which is not a specific problem for Cambodia, but it is a common problem of the region because the countries in the region are also increasing.
