TOKYO (Reuters) - Japan is considering deploying 1,000 long-range cruise missiles to boost its anti-China capabilities as a precautionary measure amid escalating tensions in the Indo-Pacific region.
Preparations to increase the military capabilities of both Taiwan and Japan come after seeing the anger of the People's Republic of China over the visit of US Speaker Nancy Pelosi in early August 2022.
Japan has lodged a diplomatic complaint with Beijing over the firing of a missile that fell into the waters of the Japan Special Economic Zone. Defend Japan as tensions in the region gradually escalate following Nansi Pelosi's August 2 and 3 visit to Taiwan.
Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin said that Chinese military exercises near Taiwan were necessary and legal in response to US provocative actions as a precautionary measure. China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. Ms. Chou Bun Eng: In 7 months, the authorities arrested 60 human traffickers and rescued more than 600 people
(Phnom Penh): In the first seven months of 2022, the police arrested about 60 human traffickers and rescued more than 600 people. This is according to Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC).
Speaking after a meeting with UN human rights officials on August 22, 2022, Ms. Chou Bun Eng said that these crimes were found in Sihanoukville, Kandal, Koh Kong, Banteay Meanchey, Svay Rieng and Phnom Penh.
A senior official of the Ministry of Interior stated, "In the past seven months, Cambodian authorities have cracked down on 74 cases of human trafficking and arrested 60 Chinese, Malaysian, Vietnamese and 60 Cambodians on suspicion of human trafficking." "Illegal."
Ms. Chou Bun Eng said that these suspects tricked the victims from other countries into Cambodia by promising to work for a lot of money. She added that the authorities are still committed to fighting human trafficking so that Cambodia can be a safe haven without such a heinous crime.
It should be noted that on August 18, 2022, the Ministry of Interior started a large-scale operation to control the residence of foreigners in Cambodia. The operation of the Ministry of Interior, which monitors the lives of all foreigners in Cambodia, was carried out with the exception of diplomats to check the legality and find the subjects involved in human trafficking.
