Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to see the United Kingdom open a school in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, noted that many Cambodian students are interested in continuing their studies in the United Kingdom. In this regard, Samdech Techo expressed his desire to see the United Kingdom invest in education to establish schools in Cambodia so that Cambodian students receive a standard British education.
The desire to see the United Kingdom open a training school in Cambodia was stated by the Prime Minister of Cambodia in front of the British Ambassador to Cambodia, Ms. Tina Reeds, on the occasion of her farewell to Samdech Techo after completing his diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, he highlighted that in this afternoon's meeting, Samdech Techo remarked that many students are now popular to study in the United Kingdom. Therefore, the UK's investment in education in Cambodia may be highly supported.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth said that the intention made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen was accepted by Ms. Tina Reds and presented to the government as well as investors on this occasion.
In addition to raising the above issues, on the occasion of the end of the diplomatic mission in Cambodia, Ms. Tina Reds thanked Samdech Techo, civil servants and all Cambodians for their good cooperation to make his diplomatic mission. For better results.
She stressed that this good cooperation has enabled her to achieve a lot of work to contribute to the promotion of relations and cooperation in areas such as education, environment, economy, trade, health and demining.
After completing a diplomatic mission in Cambodia for the past four years, Mr. Tina Reeds told Samdech Techo that she was optimistic that Cambodia would achieve sustainable development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Ms. Tina Reds for her dedicated diplomatic mission to promote Cambodian-British relations and cooperation. Samdech Techo also thanked the Government and the United Kingdom for always providing assistance to help Cambodia contribute to peace and development.
Samdech Techo wished Ms. Tina Reds success in her other missions after leaving Cambodia.
Please note that Ms. Tina Reds came to work in Cambodia in 2018. During her four-year term, she has worked hard to improve relations and cooperation between Cambodia and the United Kingdom. She reviewed and promoted various development programs in Cambodia to contribute to the development process of Cambodia. Foreign Ministry Official Encourages UN Officials to Visit Angkor Wat
