Samdech Heng Samrin considers that the presence of the delegation of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam will continue to promote friendly relations and solidarity
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, considers the presence of the delegation of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam at this time as a contribution to further promote friendly relations, traditional solidarity and cooperation in all fields between the Party, State and The people of both Cambodia and Vietnam for the better.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin made the remarks during a courtesy call on Mr. Le Hai Chung, Member of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam and Chairman of the Foreign Relations Committee of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam. August 22, 2022 at the National Assembly.
On behalf of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the President of the National Assembly is very proud and pleased to observe the progress of relations, friendship, traditional solidarity and long-term cooperation between the Party, State and people of Cambodia-Vietnam. Constant progress for the benefit of sustainable and prosperous development for the people of both countries, as well as for regional and global peace and stability.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin congratulated the great achievements of the Party, State and people of Vietnam in building and developing the socio-economy towards rapid development.
He is confident that under the leadership of the Communist Party of Vietnam, led by Party General Secretary Nguyen Phu Trong, State President Nguyen Suon Phuoc, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and National Assembly Chairman Vung Dinh Fei will continue to achieve new achievements. In further development, the nation has become more prosperous and the prestige of Vietnam's friends on the international stage has been continuously enhanced.
Mr. Le Hai Chung informed the President of the National Assembly that his current visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia is to promote the relationship and solidarity between the Party and the Party, the State and the People and the people to make the relationship stronger and more effective. More.
He congratulated the Royal Government of Cambodia for successfully preventing 19 cases of Kovid and reopening the country, which provides better opportunities for further national development.
