Citizens sue Kampong Thom Provincial Forestry Administration officials in Kampong Thom province, accusing them of using violence, threatening to kill and illegally detaining people
(Kampong Thom): Heang Bun Koeun, a forestry administration official in Kampong Thmor, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, and his accomplices were sued by villagers carrying firewood for allegedly seizing their car and using violence to beat and injure them. Killed and detained, seriously injuring a 6-month-pregnant woman, sent to hospital, while her husband was seriously injured.
According to a complaint published by Fresh News on August 22, 2022, the plaintiff, Phuong Channy, 43, filed a lawsuit against Heang Bun Koeun, a forestry administration official in Kampong Thmor commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, and his accomplices. Many people went to the Provincial Prosecutor's Office on three counts: aggravated intentional violence, death threats, and illegal detention and detention.
The same victim confirmed that he was in the business of buying firewood, there is a business law to pay taxes to the state legally, with a receipt confirming the payment of taxes. The purchase of firewood is clean and at the depot, there is a purchase receipt for them. Usually when transported to the police and the military, when we show them, they never say anything, they let them continue their normal journey.
Separately, in the past, there was always an economic police officer in Kampong Thom province wearing a four-and-a-half-year-old name, Mak Mao, asking for money, and he also used to pay. Later, he said no because he demanded too much and not just his place while he was doing business legally.
The victim stated that later on the night of August 15, 2022, he bought firewood from Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province and transported it through Kampong Thom province, and was stopped by the Forestry Administration of Kampong Thmor commune. "We are thieves, we are threatening to handcuff them, we are threatening to shoot them," he said.
After the threat, nearly 10 officers who were intoxicated violently beat the victim and his wife, who was six months pregnant, causing serious injuries and was taken to hospital. Serious injuries. Not only that, the officers locked the victim overnight.
