Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province Asks New Commune / Sangkat Councilors to Pay More Attention to Citizens
(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of August 22, 2022, Mr. Mang Sineth, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, opened a orientation training course for Commune / Sangkat Councils of the 5th Mandate 2023 at the meeting hall of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Preah Sihanouk Province. And with the participation of all newly elected Commune / Sangkat Councils.
On this occasion, Mr. Mang Sineth expressed his appreciation to the newly elected Commune / Sangkat Council leaders in the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 and all the working groups of Human Resource Management who have worked hard to organize There is this training up.
The Deputy Governor said that the orientation training for the national target group of newly elected Commune / Sangkat Councils in the 5th Mandate Election 2022 and the Financial Contract Officer for the Commune / Sangkat Administration is now two days. From 22nd to 23rd August 2022 on Commune / Sangkat Administration, which has 9 chapters, including:
* Chapter 1: Overview * Chapter 2: Structure, Roles, Duties, Accounting and International Relations, Administration * Chapter 3: Work to be done after taking office * Chapter 4: Council meetings * Chapter 5: Planning Development and rolling three-year investment program * Chapter 6: Public service delivery * Chapter 7: Administrative affairs * Chapter 8: Change of councilors and personnel management * Chapter 9: Financial management.
In this training, Mr. Mang Sineth highlighted and encouraged all Commune / Sangkat Councils to work hard to serve the people well in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia now and in the future.
He added that all commune council leaders must know how to guide or inspire various movements related to agriculture, farming, industry, business to the people in the community, which is a benefit to generate income to help the family community. And nation. In general, it is better to spend money to buy things from outside, even if we have the time, opportunity, place to grow crops and other occupations.
