Citizens who built illegal structures in the Angkor area volunteered to start a series of demolitions after the coordination of the authorities
(Siem Reap): Residents who illegally built tents or restaurants in South Taksin Village and Veal Village, Sangkat Kork Chak, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, have started to demolish their buildings after a series of mediations from the authorities.
She said that she did not know about the compensation, just heard from the neighbors that the authorities will release her to live in Ron Ta Ek village, and she did not know whether this news is true or not. Concerns about doing business on a daily basis, far from the town and schools and hospitals.
As for Ms. Hen Sokhoeun, who was preparing the materials after the demolition, she said with a sad face that she has been living and doing business in the area for many years. If she goes to live in a new area, she is most worried about her family's livelihood, she does not know what to do to support her family, as she used to work in Angkor.
Please be informed that as of August 21, the team has cooperated to dismantle at the request of 10 owners, a total of 12 restaurants, equal to 79 khans. Mlup Chhat Angkor Grilled Chicken Restaurant Mlop Yeang Restaurant Prahok Restaurant Sok Chan Angkor Restaurant Kraya Khmer Restaurant Grilled Chicken Restaurant Bopha Kolap and Kngok Restaurant
The campaign aims to preserve the Angkor site, an ancestral heritage, national identity and soul, as well as the universal value of World Heritage properties for all mankind.
In Angkor National Park today, there are more than 8,000 cases of illegal construction. In the last three months, a total of 398 cases of illegal construction have occurred, of which more than 200 cases have been dismantled.
