Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized this during a meeting with Mr. Le Hai Chung, Chairman of the New Foreign Relations Committee of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam this morning, August 22, 2022.
Le Hai Chung has been leading a delegation to visit Cambodia to celebrate the 70th anniversary of Cambodia-Vietnam relations. Mr. Le Hai Chung informed Samdech Techo that his current visit to Cambodia is to promote the solidarity between the party and the party, the state and the people and the people. In particular, make economic relations stronger and more effective through both bilateral and multilateral mechanisms.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed the intention to improve the economic relations between Cambodia and Vietnam, which are already in good condition. Samdech Techo Ba said that economic relations play an important role in the relationship between countries, and this economic relationship also supports political relations.
The Prime Minister said that based on the existing basis, the economy should be further strengthened, turning border areas and wars into areas for trade, development and cooperation.
It should be noted that in this meeting, Mr. Le Hai Chung also praised Cambodia's progress on socio-economic development as well as Cambodia's role in the international arena. Mr. Le Hai Chung congratulated Samdech Techo Prime Minister on his successful election in the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election. Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Supports the Mission and Role of the United Nations in Strengthening International Solidarity, Peace and Security
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, on behalf of the National Assembly of Cambodia, supported the mission and role of the United Nations, especially the role of the Security Council in strengthening unity, maintaining peace and international security, as well as resolving disputes and issues. Conflicts that are happening all over the world.
This statement of support of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin was made on the occasion that Samdech allowed Mr. Abdullah Sahid, President of the 76th General Assembly of the United Nations, to pay a courtesy call on Monday morning, 22 August. This year 2022 at the National Assembly.
On that occasion, Mr. Abdullah Sahid expressed his deep gratitude to the President of the National Assembly for allowing him and his delegation to pay a courtesy call on the occasion of his visit to Cambodia.
The President of the 76th General Assembly of the United Nations also expressed his appreciation for the heroism and great dedication of the President of the National Assembly in liberating Cambodia and contributing to the development of the country for most of his life.
At the same time, he stressed that Cambodia is a model country that countries should follow because Cambodia became a country with a UN peacekeeping force in 1993, but now Cambodia has sent its own volunteer forces. Within the framework of the United Nations to carry out humanitarian missions to maintain peace in many countries around the world.
Abdullah Sahid wished Cambodia to achieve its development goals of becoming a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin thanked the United Nations for its support and cooperation in contributing to the development of Cambodia, especially the provision of Kovid 19 vaccine, technical equipment and medical equipment that contribute to the success of the fight against disease. Kovid 19.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin emphasized that from 2006 until now, Cambodia has become a country that has joined the United Nations in the cause of peace and humanity in the world by sending peacekeeping forces. More than 8,000 people participated in 11 missions in 9 countries. This active and valuable participation makes Cambodia 28th out of 122 countries.
At the same time, the President of the National Assembly added that from the first mandate to the end of the sixth mandate, the National Assembly of Cambodia has actively contributed to maintaining and building peace in the region and the world with partners in the legislature. Parliamentary diplomacy, especially through the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU), which is responsible for reporting to the UN General Assembly.
