Cambodia is a country plagued by the effects of nearly three decades of war. The flames of war have claimed the lives of millions of Cambodians and left the national economy and development buried under the smoke and ashes of the flames. Finally, the flames of war, division, and massacre in the Khmer nation were completely extinguished on December 29, 1998, under the win-win policy set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, during the meeting, Mr. Abdullah also praised Samdech Techo for sending peacekeepers to carry out missions under the umbrella of the United Nations to many countries in the world to maintain peace.
Regarding the deployment of the Blue Hat troops, Mr. Abdullah highlighted that "Cambodia is a country that has received the Blue Hat forces to keep the peace. But now Cambodia has become one of the countries that has sent its troops to help keep the peace in other countries under the auspices of the United Nations. "This is a huge success, a change of face, a respectable one for Cambodia."
The President of the United Nations General Assembly also praised and admired the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in making Cambodia achieve rapid development. He highlighted that Phnom Penh has become a capital like the capital of other developed countries in the world.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, in this meeting, Mr. Abdullah also highly appreciated the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to lead the country to achieve the goal of being a high middle income country by 2030. And a high-income country by 2050.
Mr. Abdullah also praised the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the chair of ASEAN, making ASEAN an organization respected by other countries in the world. He wants to see countries use ASEAN mechanisms for development and peace in other regions.
It should be noted that in this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Abdullah also discussed economic relations between Cambodia and the Maldives.
Mr Abdullah said Cambodia and the Maldives had great potential for cooperation, especially in trade. He said Cambodia has a source of food that can be exported to the Maldives. Mr Abdullah said he would work with the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and encourage Maldivian investors to explore investment opportunities in Cambodia to boost trade between the two countries and further boost economic cooperation.
Regarding this investment, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, requested Mr. Abdullah to encourage Maldivian investors to examine the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia to boost trade between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen informed Mr. Abdullah about the favorable conditions for investment in Cambodia, especially in the agricultural sector. Samdech Techo said that in Cambodia, foreigners are allowed to invest 100 percent, especially in the agricultural sector.
