Children with autism are noted for being lonely, not paying attention to those around them, up to two years old, unable to speak, and sometimes angry, not wanting to be comforted.
Starting from this contribution, the Department of Mental Health and Substance Abuse of the Ministry of Health, sponsored by the World Health Organization, began to draft a strategic mental health plan 2022-2030. This consultation meeting was held this morning, August 22, 2022, chaired by Mr. Hok Kim Cheng, Director General of Health Technology.
According to Hok Kim Cheng, the cause of autism also urges the Ministry of Health, especially the Department of Mental Health and Drug Abuse, to study and draft a strategic mental health plan to raise awareness and alert the people.
The Director General of Health Technology further stated that the preparation of this mental health plan is very important because it is in line with the Health Strategic Plan 2023-2030 and also responds to the needs of the Cambodian people to make sure. The well-being of the people, especially mental health problems, must be detected and treated in a timely manner.
He added that the strategic plan also has the support of the World Health Organization and many partner organizations, as well as specialized officers from national hospitals, provincial hospitals, and many other national and international experts to participate in the planning. This is comprehensive. As this mental health issue involves many areas, so does the involvement of the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
