(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Seng Sivutha, President of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal, and Mr. Ouk Savuth, Attorney General of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal this morning, 22 August 2022, presided over a meeting on strengthening cooperation. Law between judicial police officers and the court of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court.
Mr. Kim Rath Narin continued that today is a very good time as the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court and the Prosecutor of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court and the relevant departments and units related to law enforcement met to discuss and exchange views. Address some of the remaining issues and further strengthen good cooperation in order to continue the mission of better justice for the people living under the roof of "peace".
According to Seng Sivutha, the purpose of the meeting was to further strengthen law enforcement cooperation between the Judicial Police and the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Prosecutor's Office and the Prosecutor's Office of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court. Better justice for the people in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's policy, legal reform and justice system.
Separately, Mr. Ouk Savuth said that on behalf of the judicial police officers must perform their duties properly in accordance with the law in force, otherwise our work will lead to the annulment or disciplinary punishment. On the other hand, within the framework of the performance of its duties in the investigation or the implementation of the substitution order, it shall receive instructions and orders from the representative of the prosecution or the investigating judge.
Taking this opportunity, the President of the Court of Appeal of Phnom Penh and the Attorney General and the accompanying delegation also visited the development of the infrastructure of the Court of First Instance and the Prosecutor of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, which has a courtroom, a meeting room, a library and a place to receive complaints and administrative letters. Other.
