Chulkiri District Authority Repairs More Than 10 Kilometers of Roads Along the River to Facilitate Traffic for Citizens
(Kampong Chhnang): The authority of Choul Kiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, has been repairing a 10 km long road along the river to facilitate the traffic of people in Chulsar and Peam Chkork communes in Choul Kiri district.
This morning, August 22, 2022, Mr. Dov Kimsin, Governor of Choul Kiri District, said that the repair of this road in order to allow people in Chulsa and Peam Chkork communes to travel and transport dry farm produce. And agricultural crops to markets in Kampong Cham province.
According to the Governor of Choul Kiri District, this road has been repaired with a length of more than 10 kilometers and a width of 5 meters from Prey Kry Cheung Village to the front of Peam Chkork Commune Hall, Choul Kiri District, using the budget of the Choul Kiri District Administration in 2022. The CPP helped the locals in Chulkiri district and the budget of some philanthropists.
The district governor further stated that in Chulkiri district, there are two communes, Chulsar commune and Peam Chkork commune, where the roads are badly damaged and difficult to travel. This line may be repaired in the next 15 days.
