(Preah Vihear): For two days, on August 21-22, 2022, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, continued to lead the working group of the Armed Forces and local authorities to inspect the situation along the Cambodia-Thailand-Laos border and so on. Inspect the flood situation in Choam Ksan, Chey Sen and Rovieng districts to be ready to rescue people in time in case of flood.
Preah Vihear Provincial Governor inspected the water condition after a series of rains over the past few days, causing flooding in the lowlands of seven villages in Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
As of August 21, the flood had flooded 36 houses, flooded 4,135 meters of roads, drained 26 places, 21 hectares of farmland, killed one cow, damaged equipment and some means.
In this flood incident, the district and commune authorities cooperated with the district police force and the 7th Intervention Brigade to rescue in time by facilitating the transportation of materials and evacuating the victims to a safe place. Do not endanger the lives of the people.
Although the water level began to recede gradually, the rescue force was on standby 24 hours a day in the event of a flood. On the mountain of Prasat Preah Vihear, it rained continuously for about 7 days and on the night of August 21, 2022, it rained all night, causing the road to climb the mountain directly above the banana plantation.
