Dr. HUN Manet sends a message to visit and organize a get-together for students who will continue their studies in the Republic of Korea for the academic year 2022-2023
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Representative of Dr. Hun Manet, participated in a get-together with students who will continue their studies in the Republic of Korea for the 2022-2023 academic year at the Phnom Penh Hotel. The program was attended by 91 ESEA team leaders, alumni of the Republic of Korea and a total of 91 scholarship winners who will continue their studies in the Republic of Korea.
Mr. Heng Sour considered the winning scholarship students who are going to study in the Republic of Korea as a valuable resource and a bridge between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea to be better and stronger. In addition, he encouraged the scholarship students to create opportunities and seize opportunities through good communication with foreign friends, which is another important factor in addition to their studies.
On that occasion, Mr. Heng Sour joined in congratulating and bringing a heartfelt message of love from Dr. Hun Manet, who always cares about the well-being of young people, especially always initiates social gatherings. Share experiences and give feedback to young people before going to study abroad.
Mr. Heng Sour emphasized that this meeting provided an opportunity for face-to-face meetings to exchange information and experiences with each other, especially to provide opportunities for young students to learn from the experiences of seniors who have studied. In the Republic of Korea, as well as receiving successful ideas, skills, knowledge and experience from seniors for the purpose of cultivating the mindset, attitude and practice for the enhancement of their abilities.
