(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, reminded parents and guardians to take care of their children and manage their young children. To be bold.
The reminder of Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang was made after 08:45 on August 20, 2022, the people provided information through the telephone number 1291 of the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Operations Command. That found a child lost a parent at the point of Street 371, Russey Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey II, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. Immediately after receiving this information.
Upon receiving the information, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang directly ordered the team to arrive at the scene and took the boy to the Meanchey District Military Police Base to search for his parents and informed Social media also to help announce the parents to take the child home.
After researching and disseminating on social media, the boy who lost his parents was finally found by his mother, Chen Chanthy, a 38-year-old female factory worker, residing in Damnak Thom 2 Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. Get home safely. The boy is named Kate Sokhem, 5 years old.
In the case of children who have lost their parents, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang expressed his deepest sympathy and called on parents to take care of and control their children to avoid any unfortunate incidents. Our negligence can become a lifelong regret.
