Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: Planting trees is a connection between natural life and gratitude to the planet
Mr. Neth Pheaktra's remarks were made on August 21, 2022 on the occasion of His Excellency presiding over the planting of 700 seedlings in the community of Chambok Protected Area in Thmey Village, Chambok Commune, Phnom Sruoch District. Kampong Speu, a collaboration between the Ministry of Environment and Mekong University of Cambodia.
The event was attended by Mr. Tith Vuthy, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu, Mr. Om Mak Theary, Director of the Provincial Department of Environment, leaders, professors and students of Mekong University of Cambodia, Scouts, Red Cross Youth, SOSYOK and Peace Lovers, Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in Kampong Speu province and Chambok community, a total of nearly 300 people.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the tree planting ceremony will help cultivate the spirit of Cambodians respect the environment, natural resources, forests even more.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that under the auspices of Cambodia, there are enough opportunities to strengthen the management and conservation of Cambodia's natural resources, and because of the better conservation of natural resources, Cambodia is able to sell carbon credits on the voluntary carbon credit market.
The spokesman noted that Cambodians are now very interested in eco-tourism, which is a land-based tourism that creates jobs and income for local people.
Regarding the planting of trees in the community of Chambok Protected Area, Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that our participation today is to participate in the protection of natural resources, biodiversity, balance of ecosystems and conservation of our natural resources. To contribute to climate change mitigation and to contribute to the economic development of local communities through "territorial tourism".
He added that the 700 trees, including luxury seedlings of Beng Neang, Nuon Thnong, Koki and peacock trees planted in today's ceremony is also to inspire love and greater recognition of great values. Of natural resources for human and animal life and contribute to protecting the environment and boosting the national economy.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that participating in planting trees now is not only a great memory for our lives, but also shows the values of unity, cooperation in the cause of the environment and natural resources.
In this regard, Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that the establishment of the local economy is an important foundation of measures to protect and conserve natural resources.
The Secretary of State stressed that in order to be more effective in conserving natural resources, legal measures and economic measures need to go hand in hand, and the Chambok Protected Area community is an already successful model that demonstrates the establishment of a local economy to strengthen conservation.
