(Battambang): Some students at Pich Chenda High School, Phnom Preuk District, Battambang Province, were disciplined by their teachers to take out their mobile phones and call for questioning one by one because some of them were addicted to playing games in the classroom, watching porn in the classroom Falling in love and playing TikTok in class can affect your education, your lack of discipline, your dignity, and so on.
This work started on Friday, August 19, 2022, when the flag was saluted at 7 am, a disciplinary teacher named Suon Bunnath took the mobile phones from four students to check their personal data and interrogate them in person. One by one, they ran out of words in order to look for abnormal images that affected their learning, but some students were unhappy and accused the teacher of asking questions over and over the subject, violating individual rights.
In connection with this accusation, the Fresh News Agency in Battambang province contacted Mr. Suon Bunnath, a teacher on the Disciplinary Council, for clarification to ask for an explanation. He replied that the case of removing the phone from the students did exist, but he followed the order from the high school principal based on the school rules.
The principal of the high school continued that any student who misbehaves in this school, he still has measures and provides further education to prevent this from happening again in the school, in order for them to improve and study hard. Everyone is good to maintain the honor of the students themselves, parents and teachers in the school as a whole.
