Student teacher Chhun Jillian said that because AIDS is a more deadly disease than Kovid 19, he is determined that when he becomes a teacher, he will spread this knowledge to those around him, his family and community. Original. Meanwhile, student teacher Chhun Ji Lan also called on young people not to experiment with HIV.
Another student student, Moeun Thavisonita, who specializes in chemistry, similarly described HIV as a deadly disease for which there is no cure, and that the disease is transmitted through sexual intercourse, not using a condom through blood. Needles are passed from mother to child through breastfeeding. To eradicate HIV / AIDS, we need to work together to spread the word about what we have learned to educate and promote in the community the prevention and control of HIV transmission.
Teacher Seng Chanvalak, who specializes in Chemistry, also expressed his pleasure to learn new knowledge related to HIV / AIDS from a workshop organized by the Cambodian Red Cross and the National Elite Team as a student teacher. Who will be future teachers, determined not to commit any acts that cause AIDS and to continue to publish what they have learned today.
For national student teacher Thanita, who specializes in mathematics, this workshop made him aware of what AIDS, transmission and prevention are all about.
In addition, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also emphasized to the student teachers that HIV is not difficult to prevent, because the disease depends on the behavior of each person, so if each person does not act is not contagious and must remember That there is no vaccine and no cure for AIDS.
She added that the Ministry of Health and the Cambodian Red Cross are currently promoting pre-marital health screenings to prevent HIV and other diseases, so she encouraged all student teachers to participate.
At the same time, pedagogical students also pledged to work together to eradicate HIV / AIDS by 2025 and blood tests before marriage.
