Dr. Chet Chealy: Some careers may be lost due to changing society
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chet Chealy, Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, said that in the future, some careers may be lost due to the changing society.
Dr. Chet Chealy believes that technology is very important and that it has replaced some of the work that people used to do. That is why the Royal University of Phnom Penh, one of the nation's largest research institutions, aims to train young people so that they can stay up-to-date and become good citizens and help society.
The Rector added that in any country, resource training is required, and in the society of any country, there is always a shortage of human resources due to various factors. In fact, the current technology training at the Royal University of Phnom Penh also has two challenges, namely: 1: lack of funds and 2: lack of experts with foreigners.
Dr. Srun Sovila, Director of the New Business Training Center of Cambodia, said that under the auspices of the organization, the organization has helped many young people by creating four prototype products, all of which use technology to solve problems.
He said that prototype products that use technology to solve problems under the training of the center include:
1: Assistance in tourism 2: Assistance in agriculture 3: Assistance in sports 4: Assistance in education
Meanwhile, Kim Junsu, Deputy Director of Kayaka Cambodia, confirmed that Kayaka will continue to support the Royal University of Phnom Penh and the Cambodian New Business Center for other projects. Dr. Mao Havanal sends condolences to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol
