Spokesperson: The Ministry of Education does not prohibit the use of mobile phones that support learning, but if students misbehave, they will be fined according to the level of error
(Phnom Penh): Spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Ros Sovacha, confirmed that the Ministry does not ban the use of mobile phones or technology that supports student learning and teacher teaching, because in the context of the Kovid 19 crisis, the use of modern equipment These are important aids in student distance learning.
The reaffirmation comes after interest erupted in connection with a case in which a student at Pich Chenda High School, Phnom Proek District, Battambang Province, had his cell phone confiscated by his teacher and called for questioning one by one because some of them were insane. Playing games in the classroom, watching porn in the classroom, using the phone, communicating with each other and playing TikTok in the classroom, affecting education, losing discipline, degrading dignity, and so on.
In order to clarify to the public about this case, Mr. Ros Sovacha said that on October 22, 2009, the Ministry of Education has already issued a proclamation on the internal regulations for public secondary education institutions aimed at establishing secondary education institutions. In general, the public to have security, safety, order, order and good morals in order to improve the quality and efficiency of education.
The spokesman added that the proclamation stipulates discipline and morality, which requires all students to maintain moral discipline and not to commit acts that affect the honor and dignity of the institution and the country, such as the use of mobile phones. Leave learning and teaching or playing mobile games while studying.
The proclamation also states that students must not watch movies, books, magazines, pornographic images and commit obscene acts, acts that are dangerous or disruptive to the educational institution.
He added that the Ministry of Education has not banned the use of mobile phones or technologies that support learning and teaching, especially in the context of Kovid 19, where learning and teaching must continue to follow the new normal path of digital education. The role is even more important, so students need to know the positive benefits of using mobile phones and technology.
