(Preah Sihanouk): On the evening of August 19, 2022, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, met with Mr. Vitith Mutabon, UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia.
Discussion Begins Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, welcomed a delegation of the United Nations Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia to visit Sihanoukville and briefed them on the geography and development of Sihanoukville. Especially the development of the province in recent times under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia, Mr. Vith Muthtabon, thanked the Provincial Governor for allowing his delegation to understand the concerns and challenges in a timely manner, including These include the human rights situation, forced crime, human trafficking, cybercrime, online fraud, and the status of rescued victims.
At the same time, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun informed Mr. Vith Muthtabon that Cambodia has a number of constitutions and laws related to human rights, human trafficking, cybercrime and online fraud, and is working to combat this problem. The Royal Government of Cambodia is highly committed to any act that violates Cambodian law and international legal standards.
The provincial governor also claimed that the Sihanoukville provincial authorities at all levels have never avoided their role, that is, we work together to enforce the law and crack down on all crimes without compromise. At the same time, the provincial administration welcomes all relevant parties and embassies of friendly countries to cooperate in finding the root of the crime in order to reach a more effective crackdown.
He informed that in the past, Cambodia and Thailand have had an influx of illegal workers, and there have been Cambodian workers going to work in Thailand, and there have also been Thai workers coming to work in Cambodia, especially in Sihanoukville, through wrongdoing. Law. Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said, "Twenty years ago, many Cambodians were persecuted or trafficked in Thailand, Malaysia, Taiwan, China. We Cambodians are in pain. "So in Cambodia, we do not want this pain to happen again."
Mr. Vitith Mutabon expressed his support for the human rights process in Cambodia and wanted to know the general situation in Sihanoukville regarding human rights, human trafficking, cybercrime and online fraud to find a timely solution.
At the same time, the provincial governor also said that the actual situation in Sihanoukville was different from what some media outlets reported, so he requested the delegates to record what was true and wished the delegates a visit. The United Nations Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia in Sihanoukville has been successful and happy.
Although this is a supplementary lesson for the hot news writing session, Mr. Mar Yarith presented the main points and foundations of the editorial and commentary to the participants.
