By: Professor of Social Sciences, University of Phnom Penh Creating new jobs for people living in natural areas has become an important mechanism to change people's attitudes to participate in the conservation of natural resources and wildlife protection.
(Phnom Penh): The protected areas of Cambodia play an important role as natural banks, playing a role in conserving all kinds of biodiversity, maintaining water resources for people's use and ensuring sustainable development, ensuring the richness of resources. Plant genetics, edible and irrigated.
Protecting and conserving protected areas is considered an effective and effective strategy to address global issues in poverty reduction, climate change mitigation, and ecosystem services. Increasing investment in protected areas is a costly investment and will also bring great benefits to the ecosystem, social development and long-term national economic growth.
Currently, Cambodia's protected area system includes: Protected areas and biodiversity corridors cover about 41% of the country's total land area of approximately 7.3 million hectares. This number is one of the highest in the world with protected areas. In Asia, there is only Bhutan, which has a protected area similar to Cambodia.
However, the current Cambodian protected area system is under intense pressure and concern about the effectiveness of biodiversity protection and the provision of sustainable livelihood opportunities for local communities. The Natural Resource Protection Zone system is needed to ensure better management for the benefit of all generations in Cambodia.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to establish the local economy as part of an effective solution to the protection and conservation of natural resources. He said legal action alone could not succeed as perpetrators continued to commit natural resource crimes.
"Once the people in the local community have a new business, it will be a solution. Economic measures are the key to giving the community access to new businesses, income and new options beyond their traditional occupations," he added.
He said that the actual results of the carbon credit project in Mondulkiri province, which is successful, the villages living around the natural resource protection area per village can receive a budget of about 13,000 dollars a year, this is a source of inexhaustible funding. Sell carbon credits. At this point, the Ministry has further urged the community to better understand the benefits of natural resources.
In addition, Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that since the fifth mandate, the Royal Government of Cambodia has established 186 natural resource protection community communities, excluding community forestry areas of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. Hunting and fishing. KOICA and Sun Chunyang Medical University Center Organize the First Ang Duong Hospital Workshop on Nursing Care
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and Sun Joon Yang Medical University Center in collaboration with the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and Preah Ang Duong Hospital this morning, August 20, 2022, organized a seminar on The first of Ang Duong Hospital on the care of nurses "at Raffles Hotel Phnom Penh.
The purpose of this workshop was to find ways to monitor the procedures of the nurses of the five national hospitals and to strengthen their capacity after 19 cases of Kovid were under control and to share knowledge by inviting nurses from Sun Joonyang Medical University Center of the Republic of Korea came to share their knowledge and experience with all participants.
