Philippine President sends warm message to Cambodian King on 65th anniversary of diplomatic ties
(Philippines): The President of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, sends a message to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni of the Kingdom of Cambodia, expressing the warmest congratulations on the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations. Both on August 20, 2022.
He said that although the relationship between the Republic of the Philippines and the Kingdom of Cambodia was formally established on August 20, 1957, the relationship between our nation and our people dates back to before the modern nation. This is reflected in the royal visit of His Majesty King Norodom to the Philippines in 1872.
"Our relationship has grown steadily over the years through regular bilateral exchanges in the fields of politics, security, economy, socio-culture and education, as well as cooperation in regional and regional forums," he said. International. People-to-people exchanges also continue to strengthen our strong friendship.
The President pledged to further strengthen and expand the Cambodia-Philippines partnership and cooperation as our two countries are striving for greater economic and social development for the benefit of the people of Cambodia. We.
