(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for 19 Kovid Vaccination, urges the sub-national administration to continue to mobilize people who have not been vaccinated. Fourth and fifth, so that they can come and inject everyone to strengthen the community.
In the interview after the closing workshop on the plan to promote 19 doses of Kovid 19, 4 and 5 doses on the evening of August 19, 2022, organized by the Committee for Kovid 19 vaccination. With the participation of the Capital-Provincial Health Department, Ms. O Vandin continued to consider that the 19-dose Kovid vaccination is very important.
Ms. O Vandin emphasized, "It is important that we urge the sub-national administrations of the 25 capitals and provinces to urge the local authorities to mobilize the remaining unvaccinated people by Be specific with the capital-provincial health department.
According to the chairperson of the commission, most of the major targets that have been focused on in the past, such as markets, schools, factories, etc., have been injected in the third dose, with only a small amount left. The task will be pushed again so that all the target groups get the 4th dose and the 5th dose.
Ms. O Vandin emphasized that in the past, most of the provinces have achieved the vaccination against Kovid 19 with good results, which means that almost all people have been vaccinated, so the plan to continue. All those provinces practice what they have done in the past. In particular, the provinces that are not enough must continue to push more.
In addition, Ms. O Vandin said that in case there is still a delay in vaccinating the 4th and 5th boosters, the commission will ask the army doctors to visit the provinces to help with this work as usual. Past practice in 13 capitals and provinces, while TYDA volunteer doctors are also ready to assist in this work as well.
The health official stressed that although Cambodia has been able to control the situation of the 19-year-old Kovid epidemic, boosting the 19-dose Kovid vaccination campaign is essential to strengthen community resilience. There is a decline for the regular living of the people. She noted that in the event of a drop in immunity, the Kovid 19 virus would be able to attack again.
