The two Cambodian officials will receive 14 days of training from August 23 to September 5, 2022. They plan to leave Cambodia for South Korea on August 23, 2022.
The purpose of this training program is to strengthen the knowledge and management skills related to medical equipment and management of facilities in the hospital through a) capacity building of equipment management (safety, maintenance, long-term use plan, etc., and b). Capacity building of material management (maintenance of medical equipment).
It should be reminded that for 2022, the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) has invited 6 doctors from Preah Ang Duong Hospital to participate in the training program on "Training for Doctors" in South Korea from 11 to May 31, 2022 for 21 days for 3 doctors. From May 11 to June 9, 2022 for 30 days for 3 other doctors.
