Botum District Authority Leads a Group of Youths, Students and Government Officials to Plant 200 Thnong Trees in Phnom Trongol to Improve the Environment
(Koh Kong): Mr. Hak Leng, Governor of Botum Sakor District, on August 19, 2022, led a group of young people, students, government officials and people to plant 200 seedlings in Phnom Trongol to promote the environment. Charitable gift of Dr. Mong Bothy.
Mr. Hak Leng, Governor of Botum Sakor District, said that the arrangement of planting this heavy tree was indicated by Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, and he wanted to make sure that the sponsors were not disappointed, so the authorities had to fulfill this obligation. Just in time for this rainy season.
Mr. Hak Leng continued that in order to develop the tourism infrastructure and maintain the eco-tourism environment at the top of Trangoy Mountain to be attractive in the tourism sector, today, Botum Sakor District Authority led young people, students, government officials and people to plant trees. 200 trees as a charitable gift from Dr. Mong Bothy.
Mr. Hak Leng added that he was very happy to see the activities of youth groups, students, government officials and people actively participating in planting seedlings on the top of Phnom Trongol, located in Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province.
The district governor added that trees have great benefits for human and animal life and reduce natural disasters, especially the natural environment can reduce poverty in the family to some extent.
In addition, he called on people to love and take care of the environment, do not cut down the forest and plant trees for one person, because trees are beneficial to all of us. He confirmed that on the top of Phnom Trongol, the authorities plan to build a pagoda for monks and nuns as a place of worship.
