Young people push for higher technology in Cambodia's banking system
(Phnom Penh): Experts in the field of banking in Cambodia see that the use of technology in the banking sector in Cambodia (Fintech) is growing faster compared to other countries in the ASEAN region due to the large population of young people and they They like to use next-generation technology.
He added that another point in the crisis of Kovid 19 over the past two years has pushed the digital sector in Cambodia as a whole and, in particular, the use of technology in the financial sector (Fintech). Fast beyond expectations. People pay for goods and services through their mobile banking system.
Kith Sovannarith, Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that in relation to digital payments, the National Bank of Cambodia has developed a Fintech roadmap for 2020-2025 that focuses on three pillars to drive the sector's growth. Faster.
"Recently, we have announced the full implementation of the Bakong system, KHQR, and also cooperated with many countries in the region to promote easier payments through technology," he said. We are also beginning to monitor payment service providers to ensure that customers are protected and have proper risk management, especially as this payment technology continues to evolve.
In the first half of 2022, electronic payment transactions continued to increase steadily, such as the transfer of funds in riel through the retaliatory system, almost doubled, and payments in the Bakong system increased to 18.5 trillion riel, or approximately $ 4.5 billion with a total of 8.1 million transactions.
