The statement of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol was made during the meeting to review the results of road traffic safety on August 18, 2022.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "The use of electric vehicles increased significantly in the first seven months of 2022. The Ministry of Public Works registered 155 electric vehicles, compared to the same period in 2021, only 11 were "The increase is up to 1,300 percent."
He added that at present, the Ministry of Public Works has installed electric generators in 4 locations, including: 1 in Sihanoukville, 1 in Battambang, 1 in Siem Reap and 4 in Phnom Penh in the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. Accessories.
He added that there are generators in Sihanoukville, Siem Reap, Battambang and one in the Ministry of Public Works with the assistance of the United Nations Development Program (UNDP). Currently, the ministry has added three more generators using sala, not using the state electricity system.
In the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, there are 4 power stations and can supply electricity to 8 cars because this generator has 2 pipes and high speed can charge the car in 30-40 minutes. Only.
The Senior Minister added that in addition to providing power generators, UNDP also provided 30 battery-powered motorbikes to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and also helped to encourage Cambodians to turn to motorbikes or cars. Electricity, thanks to the use of motorcycles or electric cars, has helped reduce pollution, afforded and reduced tariffs by up to 50 percent.
