Cambodia Credit Guarantee Corporation provides new $ 57 million loan guarantee to business owners who lack collateral
(Phnom Penh): As of the end of July 2022, the Credit Guarantee Corporation of Cambodia (CGCC) has supported the issuance of new loans of about $ 57 million to businesses that lack collateral through financial institutions to engage business owners. It is difficult to get a loan because there is no collateral to get capital to expand and restore its business.
Song Kheng Lay, Chief Operating Officer of Canadia Bank, said that as of the end of July, Canadia Bank had provided CGCC-guaranteed loans to 249 clients totaling $ 21 million. Up to $ 22 million and 266 subscribers. The majority of those who take out loans with this guarantee are owners of small and medium enterprises, up to 83%.
She noted that in the past, some business owners who had a good business had good cash flow and adequate repayment ability, but their access to credit was limited due to the bank's calculation of collateral through collateral. This loan enables the bank to provide loans to them according to the capabilities and needs of their business.
"This credit scheme can help our clients a lot, especially small and medium-sized business owners, who have a lot of challenges, one of which is the lack of collateral," she said. "With a credit guarantee scheme, we see that our clients get credit when their collateral may not be enough or in some cases they do not have collateral at all."
She said that for business owners, small and medium enterprise owners wishing to apply for a loan with a guarantee from Canadia Bank is to properly register the business, have supporting documents for its business activities, operate through the banking system and be Have a clear business plan.
Ms. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that small and medium enterprises still face challenges with access to financing or investment through bank loans, especially for informal SMEs. Not yet properly registered.
She said that the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation project is a timely solution. But even if the loan guarantee scheme makes it easy for them to get a loan, the business owner must not be complacent, the business owner who wants to get a loan must organize his business well, register properly and have Make a clear list of accounts as well.
CGCC, a public enterprise under the technical and financial guardianship of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, provides credit guarantees on business loans provided by participating banking and financial institutions to support companies or businesses that are able to repay but lack collateral. Apply for a loan. CGCC contributes to the implementation of the Royal Government's policy to promote the financial environment and develop small and medium enterprises in Cambodia.
