Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara advises to stop selling construction materials at Angkor Heritage Site
(Siem Reap): Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land, Urban Planning and Construction, on behalf of the Chairman of the Orientation Working Group to Address Illegal Construction and Land in Angkor Resort and Other Areas Under the Control of APSARA Authority All construction materials depots in the Angkor resort area must stop selling construction materials in the area in order to avoid further illegal construction.
Such orders were issued on the occasion of the campaign to determine the norms of plots and identification of occupants of plots and illegal constructions in the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of APSARA Authority on the 18th. August 2022.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister also advised the owners of depots selling construction materials in the Angkor resort area to stop selling construction materials in the heritage area, which is to participate in avoiding the construction of illegal construction.
It should be informed that the Angkor resort area, which was registered as a World Heritage Site in 1992, has a total area of 401 square kilometers, covering 6 cities / districts of Siem Reap province: Siem Reap city, Angkor Thom district, Prasat Bakong district, Banteay Srei district. Puok and Warren counties, which are considered public property of the state, must be protected and cannot be cut off.
