Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara Inspects Land Use Measures and Identification of Land Holders and Illegal Construction in Angkor Resort Area
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the Orientation Working Group, on August 18, 2022, inspected the measurement and identification of plots and identifiers And illegal constructions in the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of the APSARA Authority.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara met with the technical working group on the purpose of surveying, defining the norms of plots and identifying the occupants of land and illegal constructions in the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of the APSARA Authority.
It should be noted that a large-scale campaign to determine the norms of plots and identities of land occupants and illegal constructions in the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of the APSARA Authority was announced yesterday.
The campaign will have a total force of 779 people divided into 32 groups, including 439 professional officers of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, 232 officials of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and 108 officials of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to visit. Measure and define plots and identities of occupants of land and illegal constructions in the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of the APSARA Authority.
The campaign aims to protect the 401-square-kilometer Angkor site, which was inscribed on the 1992 World Heritage List, an area that is considered public property of the state and must be protected.
