During the opening ceremony of the campaign to identify plots and identities of land occupants and illegal constructions in the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of the APSARA Authority, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara said that in the current Angkor National Park More than 8,000 cases of illegal construction. In the last three months, a total of 398 cases of illegal construction have occurred, of which more than 200 cases have been dismantled.
The population statistics document in the first and second protected areas of the Angkor resort, prepared by the APSARA Authority in 2004-2005, will be used as a reference document to examine the legal or illegal occupation of land and structures in the Angkor resort.
The Orientation Team examines the feasibility of providing land in the Run Ta Ek Development Zone for eventual settlement of eligible residents at the new housing location. Those who continue to encroach on the land in this area and those who do not demolish illegal structures are responsible before the law in force.
