Minister Thong Khon urges public-private institutions to provide training to rehabilitate tourism professionals in the wake of the Kovid crisis
(Phnom Penh): In the recovery phase of the Kovid-19 crisis, tourism businesses need more staff to re-employ, the Minister of Tourism also inspired the Department of Skills of the Ministry of Tourism, relevant institutions and development partners. In particular, the Tourism Vocational Training School provides training to strengthen the capacity of more tourism professionals to restore their skills and talents.
At the graduation ceremony for students at the WYTHS School of Tourism and Hospitality (WYTHS) on August 17, 2022, Mr. Thong Khon urged all tourism professionals to re-enter the tourism service business. They have been re-trained to improve their skills and abilities, while some have been temporarily suspended due to the closure or closure of businesses during the Kovid crisis two years ago.
He recalled that the suspension of business and employment caused by the Kovid crisis has resulted in the loss of skills and talents in the tourism sector, which the government has been working to build for many years. Some professionals have changed careers, young people are reluctant to take up business tourism skills, businesses are restarting, facing staff shortages, among other challenges.
The Minister urged the specialized departments of the Ministry of Tourism and relevant institutions and development partners, especially tourism vocational training schools, to co-organize training courses in accordance with current labor market needs as well as national and ASEAN curricula.
Mr. Thong Khon suggested that businesses as well as young people working in the tourism sector should identify good hospitality as a core value of service and requested training and business institutions to put in place innovative programs and ideas to support students. As well as employees.
On the other hand, young people should attend training courses in accordance with the National and ASEAN Qualifications Framework in accordance with the clear standard program taught by national and ASEAN trainers already recognized by the Ministry of Tourism.
