China urges United States to adhere to the one-China policy as committed in its joint statement (Video inside) (Beijing): China on Wednesday urged the United States to learn historical lessons by respecting The three China-US joint statements and adhere to the one-China principle. This is according to the release by Xinhua on Wednesday, August 17, 2022.
Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin made the remarks at a regular press conference when asked to comment on the 40th anniversary of the Aug. 17 statement. One of the three key Sino-US statements.
The US government said in a statement on August 17, 1982 that it would not pursue a long-term policy of arms sales to Taiwan and that its arms sales to Taiwan would not exceed Not limited in terms of quality or quantity .... and aims to reduce arms sales to Taiwan gradually and reach a final solution within a while.
Wang said the statement, the Shanghai Declaration and the Sino-US Joint Statement on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, which is the cornerstone of Sino-US policy, is at the core of adhering to the one-China principle.
