(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tol Lon and his wife, Ms. Hor Khan, and their relatives are grieving because the great monk Tol Sap is the father, father-in-law and grandfather has passed away.
Rev. Tol Sap died on Wednesday afternoon, August 17, 2022 at the age of 98 due to old age. Rev. Tol Sap is the great-grandfather of Kong Liva, a team of tycoon Ly Samet called the personal adviser of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party.
The death of Venerable Tol Sap brought great sorrow, grief, and despair for his children, children, grandchildren, great-grandchildren, and all his family and relatives. The death of the great layman Tol Sap is the loss of his father, father-in-law, grandfather, great-grandfather, a pious man who worked hard to raise, nurture and train his children to grow up to be officials and good citizens in society.
The body of Venerable Tol Sap was laid to rest at his home in Borey Thulon, AA1, Concrete Road, Prey Pring Tbong I Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The news of his death was a message to his family and relatives, as well as to His Holiness Tol Sap as well as his children to attend the last visit of His Holiness and to attend the dedication ceremony for his soul to go to his death.
