Ministry of Tourism waives duty to apply for Adult Recreation Center
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has decided to waive the obligation to apply for business classification of adult tourist resorts (KTV, Karaoke, Bars, Disco, Teak and Beer Garden) in order to promote the operation of small and medium enterprises in the recovery phase. The revival of tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis from the date of this announcement.
The above businesses have the option (voluntarily) to apply for a business rating for an Adult Entertainment Center (KTV, Karaoke, Bar, Disco, Tea and Beer Garden) according to their business conditions.
It should be noted that this Prakas is in accordance with the Notification No. 36 of the Council of Ministers dated 21 January 2021 of the Office of the Council of Ministers on the outcome of the second meeting of the Committee for the Promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises.
The following is a proclamation on the implementation of the Adult Recreation Center Classification: The Ministry of Labor calls on the workers of the Canterver Empire (Cambodia) Company, whose employer fled, to prepare the relevant documents to pay their future wages.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on August 17, 2022, informed the workers of the Canterver Empire Company that their employers ran away without paying their wages, please prepare some relevant documents and please wait. Notify me to pay my salary soon.
It should be informed that there are about 400 workers of the Canterpeper Company who ran away without being paid by their employer. The company is located in Trapeang Thleung 3 village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey. The reason why the factory does not pay the workers like this is because the company went bankrupt and the employer fired the workers.
After receiving information related to this issue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, ordered the Minister of Labor to solve the problem and pay wages to all workers by borrowing money from the Royal Government to pay workers. First, take action to deal with the factory owner later.
The Ministry of Labor has called on workers to wait for further notification on the payment of wages and other benefits from the General Secretariat of the Commission for the resolution of strikes and demonstrations in all areas in the near future.
The Ministry of Labor offers a good option while waiting for this additional notice, asking workers to apply for jobs through the National Employment Agency (NEA) to maintain income stability. Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi: Not All Suspects Are Guilty, Judicial Police Officers Must Investigate Clearly to Avoid Injustice
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, said that not all suspects involved in the investigation are guilty, as a judicial police officer must uphold the truth. Truth, justice, and clear investigation to avoid injustice to the people.
Remembrance of Lt. Gen. I Sok Khi was held on the evening of August 17, 2022, during the closing ceremony of the refresher course on the Criminal Code, Criminal Procedure Code and Investigative Measures at the General Commission of the National Police with 154 police trainees. Photo from the Department of Private Security Management and the Director of the Private Security Management Office of the 25 Capital-Provincial Police Commissions.
The senior police chief said: "The investigation phase must find the right, and if the investigation finds wrong, we will accuse, but if the investigation does not find wrong, we must report accordingly. This does not mean that as long as there are cases, the people to be investigated are all guilty suspects, so this point must be adhered to so that our society can receive justice, if there is justice, there is no protest, no pain. No, ”he said.
Open training courses on the Criminal Code, the Code of Criminal Procedure and Investigative Measures to strengthen the capacity and quality of officials to be professional and full-time. To comply with the strategic plan of the General Commission of the National Police and the action plan of the Department of Private Security Management in order to build the capacity and quality of police officers to manage private security.
At the same time, the Deputy Commissioner of the National Police also sent and issued some instructions, including:
* First, request the Department of Private Security Management to continue to pay attention to promote the skills training on the Criminal Code and the Investigative Rules to subordinate officers.
* Second: Ask all trainees after graduation, when returning to the unit, to apply the knowledge and experience from the study to apply correctly and build capacity, professional knowledge and do not use the knowledge of their role in violation of the law.
* Third: To share this knowledge gained to his subordinates to gain understanding, to contribute to the prevention and suppression of crime, and to perform their duties in accordance with highly effective procedures.
* Fourth: Adhere to the code of ethics, truth, justice, professionalism, special skills, apply the discipline 006 of the National Police Force, so that the case does not cause injustice to innocent citizens.
* Fifth: To increase cooperation with special units of the Prosecutor's Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in the investigation.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also instructed all police officers to strengthen internal unity, because individuals can not work alone successfully, so internal unity must respect the leaders of their units according to the hierarchy. These are all factors of our success.
More than 800 Families in Thala Parivat Village Receive Land Acquisition Certificates from Stung Treng Provincial Land Management Department
(Stung Treng): On August 17, 2022, 829 families living in Thala Parivat village, Thala Parivat district, Thala Parivat district, Stung Treng province came to receive 829 land titles after the Provincial Land Management Department Make measurements done.
The distribution of land tenure certificates was presided over by Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng Province, and was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Heads of Departments around the provinces.
According to the report of Mr. Minh Sichai, Director of the Provincial Land Management Department, the distribution of real estate ownership certificates in Thala Parivat village has a total of 1,316 plots, of which 829 plots have been issued. .
Mr. Minh Sichai stated that the land title is very important, the people who receive this ownership are full landowners and are protected by law. This means that legal private property is under the protection of the law without any person being deprived of the property of any person, unless the public interest is required to do so in the event that the law provides and is compensated. First, appropriately and fairly.
"If we look back to the past for generations, people in some areas have never had land titles, which has led to a series of land disputes, complicating matters," he said. And difficult to interpret. But with the wisdom of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has reformed the land sector by measuring land and issuing legal titles to the people.
Finally, Mr. Svay Sam Eang advised all people to continue to do business or grow crops on this land to get the benefits of this land better than selling land that can only be harvested once and will lose Go there forever.
Senior official of the Ministry of Interior instructs the new Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh to do a good job to get the support of the people
(Phnom Penh): Three new Deputy Governors of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh were officially appointed on the afternoon of August 17, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Sak Setha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Interior. Map Sarin, President of Phnom Penh Capital Council and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
The three Deputy Governors of Phnom Penh who will be announced to take office are: Mr. Khleang Huot, former Governor of Chroy Changvar District, Mr. Sok Penh Vuth, former Governor of Daun Penh District, and Mr. Hun Surithy, former Deputy Director General of the General Department of Immigration.
On that occasion, Mr. Sak Setha said that according to the new law, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will add four more deputy governors to serve the society and the people in Phnom Penh.
"Now we have announced the appointment of three people, the rest we will continue to organize," he said. Therefore, for the three newly appointed deputy governors, they must do a good job for the Phnom Penh administration to get the support of the people and to make Phnom Penh more prosperous and more beautiful. ”
Mr. Sak Setha also advised the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to continue to maintain security, public order, improve people's lives and continue to work to solve the remaining problems in society. As for the armed forces in the ranks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command, they must continue to manage the situation, prevent crimes well and inspire the people to participate in making sure that the villages and communes are safe.
In order to make Phnom Penh more beautiful, he asked the Capital Authority to manage the construction properly according to the technical standards, continue to plant trees in public places, improve the environment by inspiring people to pack and store garbage properly and encourage Garbage collection companies are on time, although the three garbage collection companies have done a better job.
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed the three newly appointed Deputy Governors of Phnom Penh to pay close attention to good cooperation with relevant ministries, institutions, 14 districts and civil society. Work with a high sense of responsibility and good internal unity.
