As of today, a total of 236 out of 373 former employees have agreed to accept payment of severance pay with the company, leaving 137 former employees who refused to accept compensation. Ministry of Economy: Suspect arrested in connection with 2.5 kg drug case in Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, not an employee of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Treasury
(Phnom Penh): The Secretary General of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on August 17, 2022 issued a statement regarding the publication of information on drug cases in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province on August 16, 2022, claiming that The suspect was not an employee of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Treasury.
On August 16, 2022, some local online media outlets reported on the drug crackdown in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, stating that the arrested suspects were named Vanna Panhavath, 26, works as an employee at the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Treasury.
After seeing the publication of the above article, the General Secretariat of the Ministry of Economy and Finance conducted an urgent search and a thorough examination of the data management system of civil servants of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, showing that it did not have the same name as the above person.
In this regard, the General Secretariat of the Ministry of Economy and Finance would like to categorically reject the above publication and confirm that the person named Vann Panhavath is not an employee of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Treasury as reported.
As mentioned above, the public is kindly requested not to be confused with published news articles.
Meanwhile, the General Secretariat of the Ministry of Economy and Finance would like to call on the media units that published the above information to correct the above information and to check carefully to avoid publishing incorrect news articles that lead to Confusion among the public.
The following is a statement from the Secretary-General of the Ministry of Economy and Finance: An explanation of China's changes over the past 10 years: Poverty reduction aimed at enabling 98.99 million poor people to live. Moderately prosperous
In the history of poverty eradication, China has created the first information database for poor households. Since 2014, the database has collected 22.8 billion pieces of information for nearly 90 million poor people. Based on these big data, donors can find any poor family on the map. How is their health? What is the annual income? What is life like after getting out of poverty?
Each data cable must be connected to a person that the state cares about. By current standards, China's 98.99 million rural poor have been lifted out of poverty through targeted poverty eradication and targeted policy implementation.
