Samdech Techo continued that the workers have submitted a petition to the Ministry of Labor, but almost two months ago, the workers still have not received any answer or solution and also submitted a petition to the Cabinet of Samdech Techo Director More ministers.
In response to this, the Prime Minister ordered the Minister of Labor, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, to solve the problem for the more than 400 workers and pay them their wages so that they do not have to worry about the problem anymore.
Samdech Techo also suggested that Minister Ith Sam Heng request to borrow money from the Royal Government to pay the workers first, then take action to deal with the factory owners later to solve the problem for workers who are in need and Need a budget for daily expenses.
