The following is an interview with Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: Koyka organized a orientation ceremony for 3 new scholarship officials before going to study for a master's degree in South Korea
With a mission to support the development of human resources (HRD) with partner countries, the Korea International Cooperation Agency has invited talented Cambodian civil servants and helped them develop the professional skills and knowledge that play an important role in Cambodia.
The Kayaka Scholarship Program is a fully funded program supported by the Government of the Republic of Korea to Kayaka partner countries. The scholarship program has been in Cambodia since 1994 and aims to share Korean development experiences with Cambodia to contribute to Cambodia's long-term development needs.
To achieve this mission, the Korea International Cooperation Agency has launched Master's Degree Scholarships with 20 prestigious universities in Korea in agriculture, rural development, education, governance, technology and environment and energy. In particular, for 2022, three outstanding Cambodian officials have received scholarships for master's degree programs with eight well-known universities in Korea.
Scholars selected by the scholarship recipients thanked and pledged their support to the Office of the Prime Minister and the Government of Korea, as well as committed to bringing about social and policy reforms in Cambodia after Learn from the experience of Korea.
