(Kampong Cham): A group of youth volunteers for charity of Jensana School visited and distributed gifts to 50 needy families and poor children in Prek Krabao commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province.
The event, which took place on August 14, was also attended by local authorities and youth groups and residents in need of parents. The program is designed to engage in humanitarian activities where educators, school administrators, and students prepare gifts for needy families and young children in need.
After Mr. Mak Somanak, the leader of the charity group from Jensana School, gave a presentation and a report on the charitable activities, the volunteers distributed 50 sets of gifts and materials, of which each family received: 20 kg of rice 2 bottles of fish sauce, 2 bottles of soy sauce, 5 packets of noodles.
For each child in the family, get 4 books, 2 blue pens, 2 red pens, 2 pencils, 1 long ruler and 1 eraser. After that, the working group also donated one million Riels to the commune hall.
Mr. I Kok Kong, Prek Krabao Commune Chief, thanked all the young volunteers and philanthropists who are willing to share with the poor families and promote the education of the needy students and visit to explore the development potential as well as new achievements. The other of Prek Krabao commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province.
