Mr. Hun Many made the remarks at a recent forum on the book "Hope of Hun Many" organized by the new electronic media at Heritage Tech in Siem Reap. Journalists, readers, as well as the general public have the opportunity to debate and question the authors of the characters in the book, as well as the veteran authors.
In response to this request, Mr. HUN Many commented that all work is important, which requires thorough responsibility to achieve any good results. This responsibility is "discipline." He also wants young people to create discipline, discipline themselves, adhere to that discipline at all times, because some work we have to race with time and time never remembers us.
He added that if young people know how to set goals for their own future, the future of their family or the future of the Cambodian nation, they must have a work plan for the next 5 or 10 years to achieve what they want to do can not wait tomorrow. Take action, that is, start today.
For Mr. Hun Many, personal discipline, work discipline that he adheres to today, he received from childhood when he lived in Phnom Penh with his parents when he went to study abroad, especially when he returned to work for Cambodia. He also followed the example of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as his father.
