(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Mr. Mam Sarin, President of the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, this morning, 16 August 2022, attended a meeting between the Committee in charge of Women and Children Affairs of the Association. National Capital-Provincial Council and members of Capital-Provincial Council.
The event was attended by the leaders of the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, members of the Committee in charge of Women and Children, the President of the 25-member Provincial Council, representatives of the Ministry of Interior, representatives of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, leaders of the National Alliance of Local Councils. A total of 138 people.
The Advisory Committee on Women and Children (CWRC) has the right to provide advice and recommendations to provincial councils, provincial governors and other committees on issues related to gender equality, women, youth and children in Powers, Functions and Duties of the Provincial Council In fact, the Provincial Advisory Committee on Women and Children's Affairs has made outstanding activities such as:
* Visited and brought donations in the form of food, supplies and financial support to the poor, the elderly, the helpless widows, victims of natural disasters and other risks, HIV-positive families, orphans, the poor, the homeless, the disabled and Vulnerable people in 5 cities and districts throughout the province.
Participate in education, dissemination, prevention and elimination of domestic violence, sex trafficking, labor force on women and children.
* Contribute to the provision of health services, including: antenatal care, delivery (natural and surgical), examination and treatment of STIs, antiretroviral drugs, vitamin A supplementation, and Kovid vaccination 19. Etc.
First, the Capacity Development Committee. Second, the Committee on Women and Children. Third, the Public Relations Committee, which has the role and responsibilities to reflect on achievements, share good experiences, and raise challenges to set recommendations for finding solutions. And the intervention of relevant ministries and institutions and organize visits for participants to learn about the development of Sihanoukville, a potential economic pole of Cambodia.
The Committee on Women and Children Affairs was established for the purpose of advising and assisting the technical work related to the work of women and children of the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils. "Promoting women in politics and public service" is one of the priorities that the Royal Government of Cambodia pays attention to and promotes in order to promote the implementation of democracy and good governance in Cambodia.
