(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 16, 2022, at the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and Chairman of the Organizing Committee of the ASEAN Economic Community for 2022 and related meetings chaired the third preparatory meeting of the organizing committee meeting under the pillars of the ASEAN Economic Community and related meetings.
The meeting was attended by the chairperson, vice chairperson and members of the sub-committee and the working group of the Secretariat, relevant professional officers as well as professional officials from relevant ministries and institutions.
The Minister said that the meeting focused on the main agenda, including: (1) Progress report, challenges and suggestions of all sub-committees in preparation for the 54th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and related meetings. 2) Recommendations for solving challenges and work directions to each committee and sub-committee and (3) other issues.
In this meeting, Minister Pan Sosak made some recommendations for the next work direction to each sub-committee and the Secretariat as follows:
Sub-Committee on Content and Documents and the Secretariat Working Group to finalize the video on the progress of PEDs of Cambodia and prepare the documents of the meeting and related documents to the Chair of the 54th AEM Meeting and related meetings and bilateral meetings upon request Practical bilateral.
3: Sub-Committee on Transport, Security, Health, Meeting Venue and Art, Monitor the flight list of the delegates to attend the meeting and arrange for the LOs and SOs officers to be well received and to prepare the Spouse program and other suggestions.
4: The Sub-Committee on Dissemination of Information should pay attention to monitor the progress of all meetings and follow-up of general information in order to organize the dissemination in all aspects.
5: Encourage continuous reporting on the progress of the process of organizing the 54th AEM Meeting and the expenditure plan, as well as report on challenges and suggestions to be resolved in a timely manner.
Mr. Pan Sosak expressed his deep gratitude to all the chairmen and vice chairmen of the sub-committees who have worked hard to fulfill their duties and responsibilities in a proactive and responsible manner in organizing meetings under the pillars of the economic community. Work smoothly and get good results for the nation.
