Uon Silot, President of the Cambodian Cashew Association, stated that in the first seven months of 2022, Cambodia exported 660,000 tons of raw cashew nuts to Vietnam, a decrease of 350,000 tons, earning 1,077 million USD, a decrease of 37% compared to The same period last year.
Uon Silot told Fresh News on August 16 that about 90% of all unprocessed or raw cashew nuts are exported to Vietnam. He said that if Cambodia attracts more investment in cashew processing, Cambodia will be able to reduce the export of unprocessed cashew nuts to Vietnam.
"If Cambodia can attract only 10 foreign processing plants, we can reduce our exports a lot, but so far we have not been able to attract them due to the repeated global crisis," he said. It is not yet active in opening its factory. "If there are more factories, it will add value to farmers and help create jobs in the community and reduce migrant workers."
According to the current president of the Cambodian Cashew Association, dried cashew nuts cost between 5,500 riel and 7,200 riel, depending on the quality of the seeds.
According to data from the Cambodian Cashew Association, the area under cashew cultivation in Cambodia is about 700,000 hectares. Most cultivated in 10 provinces in Cambodia, such as Kampong Thom, Kratie, Kampong Cham, Preah Vihear, Tbong Khmum.
