Kampong Chhnang Provincial Prosecutor Leads Police to Crack Down on Drugs in Rolea Bier District
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Ith Sothea, Prosecutor of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, led the Anti-Drug Police and the Anti-Terrorism Office of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police in cooperation with the forces of the Internal Security Department of the Ministry of Interior to crack down on large-scale drugs in Thnong Kambot village, Kraing Dey Meas commune, Rolea Bier district.
During the operation, police arrested a suspect and confiscated 2.50 kilograms of drugs and other items. In this case, the authorities have just allowed the media to publish after completing the investigation of this case on August 16, 2022.
The police report shows that the suspect who was detained by the police is named Vannak Panhavath, 26 years old, residing in Thnong Kambot village, Kraing Dey Meas commune, Rolea Bier district.
During the crackdown, police searched the suspect's home and found 16 packages of methamphetamine (ICE) hidden on the ceiling and nine packages hidden in the suspect's closet. There are 25 packs of drugs in each package, weighing 100 grams, total weight 2.5 kg, 5 drug scales, 1 bag ironing machine and packaging equipment (1 bag).
The police confirmed that after arresting and checking the evidence of the actual crime, the suspect and the evidence were sent to the Security Department of the Ministry of Interior for processing.
Please note that this case, the authorities have just allowed to publish because the case of the above drug crackdown operation is closed, a case of crackdown with a large number that has never been before in the territory of Kampong Chhnang province. Tomorrow afternoon, 3 Deputy Governors of Phnom Penh will be announced.
