Regarding the election process in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said that Cambodia has held regular elections since 1993. So far, Cambodia has held six general elections and five commune council elections, and has been assessed by national and international observers as transparent, free and fair.
Samdech Techo highlighted that Cambodia is proud of the success of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election on June 5, 2022, which was free, fair and just in a neutral, secure, orderly and non-violent environment. And threats, as well as 17 political parties competing and more than 80 percent of the population voting.
Regarding the priority work, technical assistance and future cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, Samdech Techo requested that the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees and the Special Rapporteur should prepare a report that reflects Really practical and transparent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees and the Special Rapporteur to address serious concerns about human rights, such as hate speech, slander, spreading false information and harassment. Incitement that takes refuge under the label of freedom of expression.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, during the meeting, Mr. Vitit Montaboun also noted the implementation of the law in Cambodia. Regarding this legal issue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that after Mr. Keut Rith took office as the Minister of Justice, the number of cases in court has been expedited and many cases have been brought to trial. In addition, the Ministry of Justice has set up an out-of-court dispute resolution mechanism that has contributed to resolving many issues.
Mr. Vitabontaboun also noted the cases of some politicians and civil society officials. At this point, Samdech Techo reminded that some countries and organizations want Cambodia to trade national sovereignty, which Cambodia can not do. Samdech Techo added that the process of the court is the right of the court that the Royal Government can not intervene or order.
Before concluding the discussion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen told Mr. Vitit Montaboun to consider and review the report in a balanced way, not one side is confidential and the other side requires accountability. Commentary: Investing in China is investing in future development
