He will pay a working visit to Cambodia from August 15 to 26. This is his first working visit to Cambodia after the United Nations assigned him to work on human rights in Cambodia.
During the current working visit, the UN Special Rapporteur, who is Thai, in addition to paying a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he also plans to meet with government officials related to human rights as well as organizations. Other civil society as well.
Mr. Vitit Montaboun's visit was welcomed by both the Royal Government and civil society organizations, looking forward to open discussions on human rights work in Cambodia.
Human rights work in Cambodia There have always been disagreements and misunderstandings between the Royal Government and the report of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also warned of the closure of the United Nations Human Rights Office in Cambodia.
Chin Malin, Vice President and Spokesperson of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, told Fresh News that on behalf of the Royal Government, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee welcomes the visit of Mr. Vitabontaboun. Mr. Jean Malin considered Mr. Vit Muntaboun's visit to be a normal process, as the UN Special Rapporteur, to visit Cambodia two or three times a year.
Mr. Malin also stated that for the report by Mr. Wit Montaboun, it was his own opinion only, that is, it did not represent the position of the United Nations, as the Special Rapporteur was an independent expert. Studying, researching and reporting is just a personal opinion, so for the report that came out, no one can force him.
Mr. Jean Malin also claimed that Cambodia was waiting to review the recommendations of the UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia, which recommendations could be considered and implemented, and which were not in line with the actual situation. Aspects of Cambodian law and procedure. Therefore, Cambodia will consider each point.
