Authorities Inspect Anlong Chrey Reservoir to Prepare for Flooding on National Road 5, Samaki Meanchey District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, on August 16, 2022, led the relevant working group to inspect the water condition in Anlong Chrey Reservoir in Chhean Leung Commune, Samaki Meanchey District to prepare for possible flooding. Flooded National Road 5 at km 40 and 41 again.
Mr. Sun Sovannarith said that according to the announcement of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on August 14, 2022 shows that from 15 to 19 August 2022, Cambodia will continue to rain almost everywhere. Rainfall in some areas and provinces may increase further rainfall, which may cause flash floods again.
In this situation, the water level in Anlong Chrey Reservoir is rising, but there are no challenges. The provincial governor instructed local authorities and officials to report the water situation regularly and open the drainage gates slowly to prevent flooding in the lower part, especially National Road No. 5.
In the past, the provincial governor has assigned provincial and district working groups, relevant departments and competent forces to cooperate with the Japanese company to build National Road No. 5 to intervene to solve the problem of high water flow on National Road No. 5 between km 40 and 41. And facilitate traffic congestion, as well as prevent accidents to people traveling.
