Significant new achievements in July 2022 of the General Department of Taxation: * Started and is implementing enterprise surveys in 14 districts of Phnom Penh, including the completion of a total of 784 enterprises in Boeung Kak Sangkat. First, Khan Toul Kork, as well as providing tax registration services to taxpayers
* Has been printing and handing out annual property tax invoices by handing out invoices to property taxpayers at home to make it easier to pay taxes.
* Continued to strengthen and take legal action in cases of systematic tax evasion and large-scale tax evasion in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions, such as the Ministry of Justice, the General Commission of the National Police, the Intelligence Unit Finance for the purpose of promoting and strengthening fiscal compliance
* Continue to disseminate and strengthen the implementation of the Lucky Billing Program with the participation of taxpayers and the general public and send it to the relevant tax units to monitor and take necessary action.
For 2022, in order to ensure the effective implementation of the management of tax revenue collection in accordance with the financial law plan for the management of 11,419.13 billion Riels (approximately 2,819.54 million USD), the General Department of Taxation will continue to strengthen Implementation of fiscal policy and administrative measures, including the following key measures:
* Continue to conduct enterprise surveys on 14 geographical districts of Phnom Penh and provide tax registration services to taxpayers.
* Continue to strengthen tax registration and updating enterprise information in order to facilitate business, but take measures to prevent maximum standing instead of tax evasion and all forms of tax evasion.
* Continue to strengthen and monitor the fulfillment of tax obligations of all enterprises that have successfully registered taxes in order to strengthen the management of tax revenue collection and in order to reduce related risks.
* Strengthen the audit of enterprises requesting the permanent closure of business activities and monitor enterprises that have been granted permission to close business activities permanently, but continue to have business activities until today.
* Strengthen the management and monitoring of enterprise tax returns, with measures for enterprises that do not file declarations.
* Continue to disseminate and strengthen the implementation of billing rules among taxpayers to ensure efficiency and transparency in the management of tax revenue collection.
* Continue to disseminate and strengthen the implementation of the Lucky Billing Program in order to strengthen the implementation of billing rules among taxpayers through the participation of the general public.
* Continue to strengthen the provision of property tax services to the public by facilitating the preparation of property tax invoices for each property.
* Continue to strengthen the management of the enterprise, request for temporary suspension or closure and request for reopening, with measures to inspect the location of the enterprise directly, monitor the filing of declarations and strengthen the audit of documents.
* Continue to strengthen tax debt collection, implement tax debt collection and tighten tax debt, especially large tax liabilities, by identifying priority debts.
* Strengthen the implementation of additional measures of the Royal Government to continue to manage the impact and support the recovery of the tourism sector.
* Continue to implement the necessary measures as set out in the Circular on the Implementation of the Law on Finance 2022 and continue to implement with attention to the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
