Dr. Chet Chealy's statement came after some reaction from the Cambodian people when they received the news that the Royal University of Phnom Penh will open to teach Vietnamese language.
During a working meeting with Mr. Pit Chamnan, Permanent Secretary of State on August 10, 2022, Mr. Nguyen Van Phuc, Deputy Minister of Education and Training of Vietnam, requested Cambodia to expedite the establishment of a Vietnamese language department at the Royal University of Phnom Penh. Contribute to strengthening educational cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam.
Due to conflicts and historical issues, some Cambodians seem unhappy with the news of the opening of Vietnamese language courses at one of the oldest state universities.
Meanwhile, some political activists tried to distort the information and the original purpose of the Vietnamese language course as a Vietnamese ploy to colonize Cambodia.
According to Dr. Chet Chealy, the Royal University of Phnom Penh plans to cooperate with Vietnam through the establishment of the Department of Vietnamese Studies, which will offer bachelor's degrees in three majors, including:
Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports spokesman Ros Sovacha said the establishment of the Department of Foreign Language Studies in Cambodia aims to strengthen educational cooperation with friendly countries by promoting higher education and teaching and learning. Other related.
The establishment of the Vietnamese language department is also an opportunity for scholarship students to learn Vietnamese before going to study in Vietnam to make it easier for them to study in Vietnam.
The Vietnamese language department can also help train Vietnamese language specialists for Cambodian students to meet the needs of various fields in both public and private institutions. Under the cooperation between the education sector between Cambodia and friendly countries, many countries also send their students to learn the Khmer language to be used in various needs of both public and private institutions, including translation work.
The Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, Dr. Chet Chealy, said that in some countries, such as France, Japan, China, Vietnam, Khmer language is also taught.
Regarding the opening of the Vietnamese language department in Cambodia, Dr. Chet Chealy explained, "It is very useful to know foreign languages, especially major international languages used at the United Nations and the languages of our own neighboring countries in the region." "
He added that many friendly countries have provided scholarships to young Cambodians. Before leaving, the scholarship recipients will first learn the language of the country in order to capitalize and learn the skills of their native language. Such cases will also apply to students going to study in Vietnam.
He added that the Department of Vietnamese Studies will teach Cambodian students who have received scholarships to study in Vietnam to gain some understanding of the Vietnamese language before leaving. This is the main benefit for students. Universities train students to many countries before they go to study in those countries.
Satellite view of the changes over the last 10 years of China's Yellow River and Yangtze River
The ever-growing green ecosystem holds more and more land along the Yellow River. Every year, the amount of mud discharged into the Yellow River is reduced by an average of 300 to 500 million tons. Over the past 10 years, the loss of land along the Yellow River has covered an area of 26,800 square kilometers, more than four times the size of Shanghai, China.
In the last 10 years, the Yangtze River has been increasing its capacity to control pollution and has achieved the basis of good quality river water throughout the river. What is the cause of the change? The first reason is to reduce the pollution of the area along the Yangtze River. Second reason: Urban wastewater treatment capacity has been greatly improved.
Today, the Yangtze River is the basis for good quality river water in the area along the river, so both sides of the river have become a good place for tourists to visit.
