More than 100 families in Prek Da and Prek Tapho villages in Takeo province have asked the Angkor Borei district authorities to resolve the issue of digging canals to build roads in violation of the contract, which affected their agricultural land.
(Takeo): About 126 families in Prek Da and Prek Tapho villages, Kork Thlok commune, Angkor Borei district, Takeo province, reacted strongly against the district authorities who are building a new road by digging a canal to make a road.
According to the villagers, the construction of this road is in violation of the contract with them and has affected agricultural land and residential land, as well as difficulty in getting in and out of farming.
They asked the Angkor Borei district authorities to help solve it, but for almost four months, there was no solution, as quiet as a horse thief, not knowing if the authorities forgot or did not intend to solve them, so now they ask the authorities Help them find a solution.
Residents said that later on March 21, 2019, the village and Kork Thlok authorities stamped their fingerprints with land to donate for road construction, and after the stamp was completed, construction began according to plan. With the Engineering Department of the Ministry of National Defense as the recipient on the construction of this road.
The villagers said the canal was "25 meters wide" and fertilized on the west side of the road, causing each of them to lose hundreds of square meters of farmland. Not only that, it affects the residential land as well as makes it difficult for them to travel in and out of the fields and houses.
After such a problem during the past May, the villagers have already protested once, and also wrote a letter requesting the intervention of the Angkor Borei district governor. But for almost four months now, there has been no solution, and the authorities seem to be ignoring their plight.
Because the lakes are shallow, they would be very happy if the authorities restore the lake, and after the restoration of the lake, there are many benefits for the people, such as making it easier to travel by water. And as a reservoir for agricultural needs as well, and stop digging encroachment on their farmland like this.
Regarding this issue, Dim Kimsan, the governor of Angkor Borei district, has not yet confirmed his position in resolving the issue to the people, he told Fresh News that he saw the letter requesting a solution from the above people The district hall was closed before the Commune / Sangkat Council election, and the district authorities also suspended construction.
Separately, Mr. Lim Leang, Deputy Chief of Commune 1, said that in this case, he had invited people to the house of Prek Da village chief to solve, but to no avail, the case was forwarded to the commune hall, and then Mr. Mak Chou. Kork Thlok commune chief has asked the villagers to send the matter to the district hall until now.
