General Neth Savoeun commends drug police officers for their continued success in cracking down on crime
(Phnom Penh): General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, praised the leaders and officials of the Anti-Drug Department for their hard work and dedication to successfully crack down on this global crime. Continued and received acclaim from the public as well.
Gen. Neth Savoeun's congratulations were made by Lieutenant General Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, during a meeting with leaders and officials of the Anti-Drug Department this morning, August 15, 2022. .
During the meeting, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun spoke about the trend of changing global drug situation, as well as in Cambodia, which is creating many challenges and concerns in Cambodian society.
He also conveyed the message of General Santebandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner to the leadership and officials of the Anti-Drug Department, praising and encouraging the anti-drug officers, especially the Anti-Drug Department. Strive to crack down on drug cases in Cambodia and reach out to crack down on ringleaders and destroy drug processing sites, which is a new problem for Cambodia.
In addition to praising and encouraging the lieutenant general, he also mentioned the lack of inactivity and some challenges that are negative signs that affect the reputation of the Anti-Drug Unit as well as the National Police due to the attack. From social media, expressing the concerns of some people, especially some events related to the activities of anti-drug officers.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun also mentioned some key measures to address the challenges such as:
* First, encourage efforts to strengthen the discipline of the forces and professional ethics, especially praise and encouragement for officials who perform and apply strict discipline and strict legal measures for officers who violate the rules or violate the law. . Educate and eliminate all inactivity that has happened in the past and will not happen again.
* Second: Update the operating method and focus on cracking down on cases with large networks, especially small cases should be directed to the specialized force at the local level to crack down.
* Third: Strengthen the management of units and officers by strengthening clear management mechanisms, enhance the capacity of law enforcement officers and have on-site training programs and experience in case destruction for officers as well as expand capacity. In the operation to crack down on drug offenses.
* Fourth: Advise to continue to implement the semester direction of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police as well as of the Ministry of Interior, especially the successful implementation of the Royal Government's anti-drug campaign plan.
