ARDB State Bank Signs Wholesale Loans to Three Financial Institutions with $ 30 Million in Farmers' Loan Scheme
(Phnom Penh): The Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture has signed a loan agreement with Cambodia Post Bank, Chamroeun Microfinance Institution and AMK Microfinance Institution under the Cambodian Agricultural Diversification Project to provide loans to farmers, agricultural communities to promote Agriculture, the mainstay of Cambodia's economy, is improving at a time when the world is facing a food crisis.
Under this project, the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank provides wholesale loans to the above three financial institutions to provide loans to project beneficiaries such as smallholder farmers, small and medium enterprises, agricultural communities and producers for all agricultural products. Except for rice.
This project aims to improve the financial environment and support the value chain of agricultural diversification in Phnom Penh and 12 target provinces, including Battambang, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri, Preah Vihear, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kratie, Siem Reap, Kandal, Kampong Speu and Kampong Chhnang.
Chan Seiha, deputy director general of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, told reporters that the Cambodian Agricultural Diversification Project has a capital of about 30 million US dollars, with funding from the World Bank to focus on agriculture, except for rice, for five years.
He added, "This project has a capital of 30 million US dollars and we have co-sponsored three of our partners agreed today, including the Bank of Cambodia Post, Chamroeun Microfinance Institution and AE Microfinance Institution. "MK, as you implement projects directly with clients, and the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank as a wholesaler to the above three financial institutions for them to do this work directly."
He added that for wholesale loans provided by the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank to the three financial institutions at an interest rate of 5% per annum, there is no service fee, but the interest rate that the three institutions provide to customers depends on Principles of each institution. However, he hopes that the three participating institutions will provide a reasonable interest rate, because this is a project of the Royal Government to promote agriculture in Cambodia.
