BANGKOK, Aug. 14 (Xinhua) - Thailand and China launched a joint air force exercise on Sunday, the first of its kind in years after a forced suspension due to the Kovid outbreak, the Thai military said. 19. According to a release by the AP.
The Defense Ministry in Beijing said last week that the exercise would include training for air support, ground attack and troop deployments, both small and large.
The Thai-Chinese air force exercises were held annually from 2015 until the outbreak.
Thailand seeks to strengthen defense ties with China and is one of the first countries to buy Chinese naval weapons under an agreement concluded in 2017.
