(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC), reaffirmed the Royal Government of Cambodia's strong commitment to the fight against human trafficking. Trafficking in persons in the country aims to make the work more progressive.
The commitment comes as the United States drops Cambodia from No. 2 to No. 3 in the fight against human trafficking, the equivalent of Cambodia doing nothing to combat crime. Human trafficking.
In the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit this morning, August 12, 2022, under the theme "Situation of Human Trafficking in Cambodia", Ms. Chou Bun Eng affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia accepts this ranking to increase further losses. What is lacking.
Ms. Chou Bun Eng said, "We are working hard and we have not given up on this work. Until now, we have been preparing a special operational plan to find the hidden situation in human trafficking." "In Cambodia, the Royal Government has never neglected to respond to human trafficking."
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia is not currently working on the issue of combating human trafficking alone, trying to expand cooperation not only within the Royal Government but also in organizations. National and international partners to respond in a timely manner and up to date.
With the adoption of this rating, the Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking seems to have expressed resentment towards the US government for finding what Cambodia lacks but not reporting directly. To the Royal Government, instead, publish the report to the public. She considers this to be like burning to the ground.
However, Ms. Chou Bun Eng also outlined the four strategies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which set out to implement this work to combat human trafficking, which many other countries in the world use the same. .
* First: Prevention work * Second: Victim protection * Third: Law enforcement or criminal justice * Fourth: Cooperation in the preparation or implementation of laws.
She added that in addition to these four strategies, the Royal Government has also divided into six groups of mechanisms with joint participation with partner organizations, including prevention, law enforcement, victim protection, Justice Working Group, Migration Working Group and International Cooperation Working Group.
