(Kampong Thom): The Zero Trap campaign, which took place in Kampong Thom province on August 12, 2022, is the fifth campaign after Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kratie and Mondulkiri provinces, in which 47 restaurant owners have announced not to sell meat. Wildlife for cooking for guests is an absolute must.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign, thanked all development partners and conservation organizations working with the Royal Government of Cambodia to address the trap crisis.
"Effective law enforcement and economic development must go hand in hand to eliminate trapping in protected areas in order to provide wildlife sanctuaries," said Neth Pheaktra.
At the same time, he urged people to stop hunting, trapping and eating wildlife. He also noted that wildlife consumption does not improve human health, wildlife meat and parts of wildlife should not be used for medicinal purposes, and increased human-to-animal exposure. Increases the risk of spreading viruses and other diseases.
"I call on all people across Cambodia to stop buying, selling and consuming wildlife," he said. "I urge all of you to join the ministries and partners in eliminating the trapping crisis, combating wildlife trafficking, as well as protecting the Kingdom's wildlife and natural resources."
"We need to take action now to reduce the demand for wildlife meat, which will encourage trapping and strengthen law enforcement," he said.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, said that the Kbal Tuek ceremony showed a good sign of good relations between the people of Cambodia and China through the practice of multi-religious beliefs. And cultural traditions.
This year's Kbal Teuk offering ceremony is held every year by Cambodians of Chinese descent. This year, the ceremony of offering the head of water coincides with Friday, the 15th day of the month of Srapon, the year of Karl Chatva Sak, Buddhist era 2566, which falls on August 12, 2022, and also coincides with the holy day and the full moon day.
He said: "This ceremony is a sign of good relations between the nations of our two countries, sealing the relationship, sealing the heart between the people of the two countries. "Not only that, the festive performance of this ceremony is to understand, share, and live harmoniously in the multicultural, multi-faith of our two peoples."
Dr. President of the Association of Cambodian-Chinese Progress Researchers said that the ceremony was held only one morning or one day to commemorate the beginning of the Mekong River and to thank the river for its importance. Irrigation of daily crops, in particular, has warned all river dwellers to be on high alert for floods and other natural disasters.
The ceremony of offering water to the head, which is known to have originated with the Chinese from one generation to the next, is performed by Cambodians of Chinese descent or those who are not of Chinese descent. Progress. It is observed that the organization combines Brahmanical beliefs through ancestral and Buddhist traditions by bringing various offerings to the pagoda.
