(Phnom Penh): A group of unions gathered to demand that the Ministry of Labor stop painting the unions related to the NagaWorld issue. The reason why the unions claim that the Ministry of Labor painted them is ridiculous is because the Ministry of Labor told a union leader, Yang Sophoan, who was not involved in NagaWorld at all, to stop inciting the NagaWorld workers to protest. Illegal anymore.
The reason why the ministry was introduced like this is because the union leader, who works elsewhere, suddenly came in to lead a former NagaWorld employee to carry out anarchic activities on public streets and use violence against the authorities. The actions of Yang Sophoan, who came to order a former NagaWorld employee to violate the authorities' ban, are clearly visible.
The Ministry of Labor, on behalf of the Labor Dispute Coordinator, has repeatedly tried for months to resolve the dispute, but the issue remains unresolved due to union leaders who do not understand the law. Incite behind the back.
Another mistake is inciting violence against public authorities. In fact, today, as in the past, a handful of former NagaWorld employees angrily violated the authorities, breaking through two police barricades. But the authorities continue to be highly tolerant.
In the case of NagaWorld, the only solution is to closely monitor the compensation to be paid to the laid-off employees to ensure that the company complies with labor laws.
At this point, the Ministry of Labor has often stated that NagaWorld actually provided proper compensation in accordance with all labor laws. On the other hand, he has never seen or heard of a union talking about compensation, as the company has properly complied with legal principles.
So why did the expired union leader, Chhim Sithor, still lead a handful of former workers to protest and refuse to accept compensation?
Not only did they lead the demonstrations themselves, but they also mobilized to shout, whisper and help the protesters to violate the authorities' ban. The Ministry of Labor saw the extremist and wrongdoing of the unions and recommended an immediate end. But unions that do not know the rules are shouting that the Ministry of Labor is painting them.
