Dr. Cheam Yeap Invites Indian Parliament to Attend the 43rd IPA General Assembly in Cambodia
(India): On the occasion of its mission in the Republic of India, the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Delegation (AIPA) led by His Excellency Dr. Cheam Yeap, First Vice President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, High Representative Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia and President of IPA 43 also led a delegation to meet with the Vice President of the Indian Parliament and relevant institutions of the Republic of India.
During a meeting with the Indian Foreign Minister on August 11, 2022, the two sides exchanged views on the importance of India-ASEAN cooperation, which this year marks the 30th anniversary of ASEAN-India friendship. The IPA delegation expressed its support for the cooperation of the ASEAN Executive Council and the Government of India in bringing benefits to the ASEAN nations and India.
In a bilateral meeting with the Vice President of the Parliament of the Republic of India, the IPA delegation also commended the activities of the Indian Parliament, IPA's oldest observer body, in contributing to the IPA becoming a highly integrated regional parliamentary body. Close and effective. The IPA and Indian Parliamentary counterparts praised the importance of parliamentary diplomacy in actively contributing to the building of ASEAN-India harmony.
In this meeting, Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cheam Yeap invited his Indian counterpart to attend the 43rd IPA General Assembly, which will be hosted by the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia in November 2022.
It should be noted that after the meeting with the Vice President of the Indian Parliament, Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cheam Yeap, the delegation also met with the Indian Parliamentary Democracy Institute and thanked the Institute for providing human resource training to ASEAN students through Scholarships to study there. The IPA delegation also thanked the training program for officials and MPs in building high capacity in the legislative work.
The Institute also informed the IPA delegation about working with the Indian Ambassador to Jakarta to establish cooperation in the field of human resources through the establishment of training programs for human resources, officials and MPs, especially the capacity building of parliamentary officials. To serve MPs more effectively.
