(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Siem Reap Province organized the opening ceremony of the Red Cross Training and First Aid Course for 24 staff members of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch in 12 Provinces of Siem Reap Province under the chairmanship of Mr. Kuch Lina, Vice President Siem Reap Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch.
Mr. Su Sam An, Director of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Siem Reap Province, said that this training course lasted for 2 days, from 11-12 August 2022 to increase the knowledge of the sub-branch staff in performing their duties as humanitarian rescue operators. To victims and vulnerable in the community effectively.
He added that the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Siem Reap has carefully implemented the work of the four priority areas of the strategy of the Cambodian Red Cross 2021-2030, including: 1. Priority areas for disaster management, crisis and climate change. Priority for health and community health care 3-Priority areas, promoting basic principles and humanitarian values 4-Priority areas for institutional development
Mr. Kuch Lina said that the current training is very important to provide complete knowledge as a basis for trainees to work in the field of humanitarian work, social work, as well as personal capacity development in the future. At the same time, he instructed all participants in this course to try to listen to all the presentations to participate in first aid training clearly to get real knowledge.
Another important task is that when returning to the city-district, participants must take this knowledge to disseminate training to the CRC, communes, CRC volunteers and people in the community as widely as possible. Can be done to expand the culture of sharing and helping each other in the society.
