Land dispute between 291 families and CHPB in Sambo district, authorities decide to hand over social land concessions to those who do not really enjoy land
(Kratie): 291 families from Kampong Cham commune, Vattanac commune, Sambo district, Kratie province, who have land disputes with the CHPB economic concession company, came to a meeting with provincial authorities in Kratie provincial hall to find a way to end the problem.
The meeting was held on the afternoon of August 11, 2022, chaired by Mr. Kong Kem Mony, Deputy Governor, Mr. Kao Madilen, Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral and other relevant authorities.
In the meeting for more than 2 hours, both the authorities and the people agreed on the basis of common principles, the authorities decided to give them a solution as a social land concession for people who do not have real agricultural land.
Mr. Kong Kimny stated that all 291 families must cooperate with the village and commune authorities, especially the Provincial Land Management Committee to make a clear registration form for the working group to hand over the land to those who lack land. Real results.
He added that the provincial authorities will expedite the settlement as soon as possible, and the provincial authorities will set up a provincial land use and allocation management committee to wait for them. He and the committee will set up a clear location to wait for the people to come and complete the formalities to get the land legally.
The 291 families also agreed to follow the authority of the authorities on the policy of social land concessions located in Kampong Cham commune, Sambo district, Kratie province, in addition to the economic land concessions of CHPB.
