Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province Urges People to Join World Vision in Contributing to Stong District Development Mission
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Prem Ratha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, requested the people to continue their activities in the mission to contribute to the development of Stong district even better after World Vision completed its 16-year mission to develop this area. Health, nutrition, as well as education and child protection, which will end this September.
Mr. Prem Ratha said this on August 10, 2022, while presiding over the closing ceremony of World Vision International-Cambodia Regional Development Program in Stong District, which was held at Stong District Hall, Kampong Thom Province.
Mr. Prem Ratha added that on behalf of the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration, it is a great pleasure for the long-term presence of World Vision to help develop the community of Stong District, especially in the three target communes and the people who have benefited from Social Accountability Project as well. All relevant departments and offices will take care of the achievements and be responsible for further development work as well.
At the same time, other important achievements such as: 30 reading camps were established with more than 1,000 children participating, as well as 15 libraries improved and standardized and benefited more than 2,600 primary school students. . In addition, 22 community savings groups and two agricultural development communities have been established to continue to improve the welfare of children and vulnerable children.
Mr. Prem Ratha added that according to the 2021 survey, 80 percent of children and adolescents feel safe and protected from abuse. More than 98% of babies born in recent years have been delivered by skilled midwives, and all 27 target villages have become defecation-free and hygienic.
As a result, a total of more than 75,000 people benefited, including more than 26,000 children and vulnerable children, including more than 13,000 girls. In a mission to contribute to the development of Stoung district, World Vision Cambodia has spent nearly $ 6 million received from the people of New Zealand through World Vision New Zealand and other projects.
Ministry of Industry: Cambodia will establish at least three science parks by 2025 to boost national economic growth (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia plans to establish science, technology and innovation parks to attract investors, business people and individuals Innovation to contribute to the promotion of science, technology and innovation, especially to contribute to national economic growth.
This was said by Mr. Heng Sok Kong, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation in the press conference of the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government on the morning of August 11, 2022 under the theme "Achievement 5 Year of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
According to Heng Sok Kong, the goal of the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Industry, which is the General Staff, is that by 2025, Cambodia will have at least three science parks. He claimed that when there is a science park, the ministry will mobilize human resources and financial resources to make the park up-to-date and technologically advanced.
He noted that countries such as Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam have established science and technology parks and innovations for many years and have made significant contributions to their economic growth. Also, we expect that when Cambodia creates this park, it will help drive Cambodia's economic growth even further.
"This science, technology and innovation park is very important for raising revenue, both domestically and internationally, as domestic investment continues to grow, especially in the field," he said. "Science, technology and innovation."
Regarding the sub-decree on the establishment and management of the Science, Technology and Innovation Park, Mr. Heng Sok Kong confirmed that he had attended six technical meetings, two inter-ministerial meetings, and two political inter-ministerial meetings.
