Ms. Phoeung Sakona: Vietnamese cultural events in Cambodia help both people understand each other
(Phnom Penh): Vietnamese cultural events in Cambodia provide opportunities for people of both countries to get to know each other. This is according to the statement of Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts.
Cambodia and Vietnam on the night of August 10, 2022, opened the event "Vietnamese Culture Week in Cambodia 2022" at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall to celebrate the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
In her speech, Ms. Phoeung Sakona stated, "I believe that this significant cultural event provides an opportunity for the people of the two countries to get to know each other and contribute to the connection and "Friendly cooperation and brotherhood with the people of the two nations at a high level to recover the country from the epidemic."
She said that the current relationship between the two countries is considered to be a comprehensive partnership, which is clearly reflected in the exchange of high-level delegations, officials and artists of the two countries. In accordance with the cultural cooperation between the two countries' specialized ministries for 2018-2022, the Vietnamese Culture Week and the Cambodian Culture Week are held in August and September this year.
At the same time, Mr. Hang Dao Kuong, Deputy Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism of Vietnam, said that Vietnam and Cambodia have a relationship of solidarity, traditional friendship and the same villagers.
"For more than half a century of diplomatic relations, we have had the pleasure of seeing the cooperation between the two countries in various fields, which is increasingly developed and nurtured in a deep and practical way," he said. "Relations between the two countries have also achieved many achievements in the fields of politics, economy, culture, education and other fields that contribute to bringing tangible benefits to the people of the two countries."
