The Netherlands will provide more than $ 160 million in funding to private companies, including in Cambodia, to help the environment.
(Phnom Penh): The state and the private sector urge investors in Cambodia, especially in the agricultural sector, to do business related to environmental protection and combating climate change to receive funding from the Netherlands to expand their business while The country plans to provide about 160 million euros (about $ 163 million) to private companies doing business to help the environment.
Tan Monivann, vice president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told reporters that if the private sector could access the fund, it would benefit all, as well as strengthen its business and contribute to Cambodia's economic development.
However, he said that the possibility of the private sector in Cambodia to receive funding from this project may be difficult. Therefore, he encouraged companies investing in agriculture and other sectors to cooperate and cooperate with relevant ministries, including the Ministry of Agriculture, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to make a project to receive this fund. One submitting this project can be difficult to obtain.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, who attended the workshop, said that this project will benefit Cambodia, reduce poverty, increase livelihoods and help the national economy because this project aims to help To climate-resilient agriculture, which enables them to access capital to expand their production for export.
