Details of the competition, please read the full statement below: Germany could spend six times more on Brexit if there is a trade war with China
BERLIN: Germany will face nearly six times the cost of Britain's exit from the European Union (Brexit) if the country and the EU Europe cuts China off from its economy. According to Reuters.
The Ifo Institute, a German-based economic research institute, said the biggest loser of the trade war with China would be the auto industry, which could lose 8.47 percent of value-added equipment, making transport equipment manufacturers lose money. 5.14 percent and mechanical engineering with a loss of 4.34 percent.
The authors of the study, controlled by the vbw industry association, said companies should turn to other countries to reduce reliance on certain markets and dictatorships.
In this analysis, I offer five scenarios, including the secession of the Western economy from China, as well as trade agreements between the EU and the United States.
The Ifo Institute said that although such an agreement could withstand the effects of a trade war with China, it would not be fully compensated. Instead, it would result in the net cost of the trade war equal to the expected cost of Brexit. According to Reuters.
