Cellcard of Duke Kith Meng forms a strategic partnership with the Ministry of Education to support educational programs
(Phnom Penh): Cellcard, a leading mobile operator and a subsidiary of the Royal Group, has signed a Strategic Support Cooperation Agreement with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports (MoEYS) to support educational programs aimed at promoting Education standards and facilitate learning, especially young Cambodians.
Through strategic sponsorship cooperation, Cellcard has been named the "Official Telecommunications Partner" for three programs as part of Cellcard's activities related to capacity building and research and development in the field of telecommunications and information and communication technology. SAF Foundation
These programs are specifically designed to address the need for innovative, skills-focused and integrated digital education, as well as to cultivate digital technology interest among women, such as the Strengthening of Teacher Education Programs in Cambodia. (STEPCam) Online Basic Education Equivalent Program (BEEP) and Factory Literacy Program (FLP).
"We believe in the impact of education to improve living standards and the economy," he said. As we move towards digitalization in Cambodia, a strong educational foundation is needed and it also plays an important role in ensuring that this vision becomes a reality. "We look forward to the successful implementation and joint efforts of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Cellcard in expanding the reach and impact of these programs."
The official signing ceremony took place on August 9, 2022 at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, chaired by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and Duke Kith Meng, CEO of Royal Group.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron welcomed the new partnership with Cellcard, a testament to the growing investment from private sector partners in improving the quality of education in Cambodia.
"Strengthening the digital skills of our teachers, educators and youth is a key priority in developing skilled human resources in the 21st century to support Cambodia's digital transformation," said Dr. Hang Chuon Naron. .
"The new strategic partnership with Cellcard will support the use of digital technology at all levels of the education system to create a more integrated system that provides quality education for all children and youth in Cambodia. "
The Strategic Support Cooperation will support the implementation and expansion of the following three educational programs:
* FLP - An initiative of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports (MoEYS) and supported by other development partners to train garment factory workers between the ages of 15 and 45 to acquire basic literacy skills by helping them understand More clearly about its rights. The project also aims to improve reading, writing and critical thinking skills to improve their day-to-day work relationships and practices.
* STEPCam - An initiative of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports (MoEYS) and supported by other development partners to improve the quality and capacity of primary school teachers. The project introduces a new pedagogical approach, bringing state-of-the-art digital education skills to improve primary education, creating a solid foundation for the quality of education as a whole and adapting it to the needs of the new digital age.
