Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum Sends Condolences to Mr. Khieu Kanharith and Ms. Tep Rainsy on the Death of Pen Yut
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, on August 9, 2022, sent a message of condolence to Mr. Khieu Kanharith and Ms. Tep Rangsey on the death of the great Buddhist disciple Pen Yut, mother-in-law. Of Mr. Khieu Kanharith and Mrs. Tep Rainsy who passed away on Tuesday, August 9, 2022 at 9:15 AM at the age of 92 years old.
In this condolence message, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum stated, "My wife and I are deeply saddened to learn that Pen Yut, a Buddhist supporter, is the mother-in-law of HE Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and Culture." She died at the age of 92 of old age.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum further stated that although the body of the great Buddhist disciple Pen Yut has disappeared, the deeds of merit, honor and dignity will remain in the hearts of all children and close relatives forever.
Samdech also prayed for the sacred objects in the world and the merits of the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks to help nurture and take care of the souls of the great devotees of Buddhism, Pen Yut, so that they would not go to death.
Ear saliva production to be boosted to meet Chinese market demand
(Phnom Penh): Ear saliva production will be enhanced to meet the needs of the Chinese market after the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) through the improvement of production quality and processing.
The Minister praised the results of the efforts of both sides leading to the signing of the MOU.
He said that in the past, Cambodian earwax was produced to supply the local market and was exported in small quantities and informally. The signed MOU will help open the Chinese market, which is the largest market for official adoption, to ensure product standards, product quality and safety for public health meet the phytosanitary requirements of the General Administration of Customs.
The Minister also congratulated and expressed his willingness to support the process of implementing the contents of the MOU of both parties, along with the relevant parties, including the sponsors. Taking this opportunity, he appealed to radiologists to contact the General Department of Agriculture for more details through Ke Monthivuth, Director of the Department of Sanitation and Hygiene.
