The Governor of Kampong Thom Province Uses a Win-Win Strategy! Resolve Land Dispute Between 7 Makara Phari Company and 99 Families in Tang Kork District
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Chairman of the Provincial Cadastral Commission, used a win-win strategy to resolve the land dispute that has arisen for many years between 7 Makara Phari Company and its people. 99 families in Koh Reas area in 2 areas on 200 hectares in the morning on August 9, 2022 at Sralao commune hall, Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that today's meeting to Angkor Chum to understand what happened on the disputed land and the image of the dispute to reach a final study of the land dispute between the land of 7 Makara Phari with the people because the dispute This land has been around for many years and has been used by the judiciary to issue protection orders to enjoy the right to use state land (Zone 2 land).
At the same time, the provincial governor asked the 7 Makara Phari Company and the people's representatives to talk about the history of the land and the history of land acquisition, as well as for the local authorities to clarify further after the previous research.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak worked for several hours to mediate and find a solution, and the two sides agreed to end the land dispute by dividing one half into 200 hectares.
At the same time, the Governor of Kampong Thom Province urged the Dani authorities to work with the representatives of 7 Makara Phari Company to meet with the 99 families to continue to divide the disputed land between 7 Makara Phari Company and the people, with a clear boundary marker. Both parties to the dispute should withdraw any complaints related to the person involved in the land dispute within the jurisdiction of the court after the working group has closed the dispute.
Finally, Mr. Nguon Rattanak requested both parties to end all matters in order to have peace, both physically and mentally and to enjoy the land, not to leave the land to be used in accordance with the time and purpose of use rather than Leave the land vacant.
