Takeo Provincial Police Rejects Allegations and Contradictions That Traffic Police Have to Pay to Stand on National Roads
(Takeo): Takeo Provincial Police has completely denied the fabrication of allegations against the leadership of the Provincial Police in connection with the extortion of money from its officers in exchange for naming them for street stands. Important nations at the provincial level to enforce road traffic laws and fine those who violate traffic laws.
Takeo Provincial Police, through a clarification letter received by Fresh News on August 9, 2022, confirmed that Takeo Provincial Police has a plan to work as a professional work force to organize the road traffic police force into 5 cooperative goals. With the intervention force of the Provincial Police together with the Police Inspectorate of Tram Kak District, Kirivong District, Bati District, Prey Kabbas District, Angkor Borey District and Daun Keo City.
In addition to enforcing the road traffic law, each target group has a duty to prevent and intervene for the people, as well as to cooperate with the police inspectorates to crack down on any crime that may occur. Also.
As for the use of cooperative force (regulatory force), it is responsible for facilitating the land traffic police force to enforce the law and to intervene in case of any use of violence or opposition to professional officers in enforcing the law according to the actual needs.
In addition, some traffic office officials are on duty at the land traffic police office and in the work plan to make daily reports and prepare case files to the provincial court in case of serious traffic accidents can not be coordinated outside the system. The court did not enforce the law.
