General Department of Taxation receives renewal of ISO certification on "Information Security Management System" from the United Kingdom
This international institution regularly reviews and evaluates the information technology security management system of the General Department of Taxation, covering both the data center and the integrated infrastructure that the General Department of Taxation is developing and using. Performs current tax management and collection duties.
Under the careful guidance and recommendation of Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Taxation, the General Department of Taxation received the official certification of ISO / IEC 27001: 2013 on Information Security Management System. First, in 2016, which is valid for 3 years, requiring annual audits to monitor the implementation of standard work.
As a result, the General Department of Taxation continued to comply with the certification of standards for the second time in 2019. Through continuous efforts, the General Department of Taxation continues to receive the third Certificate in Information Technology Security Management System for validity from 2022 to 2025 from the Enterprise Standards Assessment Institute (BSI) in the United Kingdom.
