(Phnom Penh): Ms. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia and Chair of the ASEAN Minister for Culture and Fine Arts for 2020-2022, urged the ASEAN Minister for Culture and Fine Arts to move forward together. In a more lively and energetic manner.
Her push was made to preside over the celebration of the 55th ASEAN Day at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall in Phnom Penh on the afternoon of August 8, 2022. The event was also attended by leaders, representatives of the Ministry of Culture and the Arts, diplomats of ASEAN member countries and dialogue partners, senior officials of the Royal School of Administration, as well as many students.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona stated that this event is organized for the purpose of community unity, common destiny through the expansion of community outreach and cooperation on economic, political, security, social and cultural issues.
She expressed her pride that Cambodia will chair ASEAN in 2022, and Cambodia is committed to chairing the ASEAN Summit under the theme "ASEAN Shares Together to Solve Common Challenges" for Reconciliation, Peace and Prosperity in the Region as a whole. To be successful.
"In recent years, we have set policies and strategies to protect and preserve our rich and growing cultural heritage," she said. At the same time, we also have other important tasks that require strong cooperation and partnership in bilateral and multilateral frameworks, especially in the field of culture, in our efforts to achieve the goal of achieving community. ASEAN Socio-Cultural 2025. "
"Within the framework of the ASEAN Ministers in charge of Culture and Fine Arts, we must work together to address issues, especially the current influence of Kovid-19, to find a way for the cultural sector to move forward in a vibrant and prosperous manner," she added. "More energetic."
She hopes that today's event will not only be a cultural celebration, but will strengthen friendships, cultural friendships, traditions that allow us to exchange ideas and learn from each other in line with the ASEAN spirit: "One vision, one identity." A community. ”
The agenda of this evening's program is as follows:
* ASEAN Knowledge Quiz Program * Performing ASEAN Dance Scenes * Performing and Performing ASEAN Songs * Photo Exhibition Achievements within the ASEAN Framework on Culture and Arts.
