Senior Minister Osman Hassan Attends Seminar on "Religious Coalition in Southeast Asia: Solidarity in Diversity"
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of August 8, 2022, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Mission, attended and delivered a keynote address at the seminar on "Religious Unity in Southeast Asia: Solidarity in Diversity" via video. ZOOM.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister expressed his pleasure to participate and deliver a keynote address at this important meeting. He added that in Cambodia, Buddhism is the state religion, but the head of the Royal Government is paying attention to all religions by providing policies for the general population to live with full freedom to earn a living. And practice its religion extensively.
The Royal Government of Cambodia also allows representatives of the Khmer Muslim community to be leaders in the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, senior diplomats, national and sub-national authorities, armed forces of all kinds, and civil servants.
He stressed that, of course, we really need to live together, even though our compatriots have different religions, beliefs and denominations.
He believes that this workshop will provide important messages and new experiences from countries around Southeast Asia in line with the above topics aimed at making the Muslim community more prosperous, harmonious and achievable in their countries.
