(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet is currently the Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Commander of the Army, and he is seen as strict in leading the army, including recruitment, transfer, appointment and appointment. Promotions and so on.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet affirmed that for the complementary framework, of course, priority must be given to the descendants of veterans and the offspring of soldiers on duty. However, before entering the full-time or full-time service, it is necessary to undergo three months of training to ensure the quality of the troops and to be sent to units as assigned by the Army.
He added that when entering the framework, there should be no obligations that affect the work, especially those who are studying in college is not allowed to enter the framework, when he got the framework clearly asked. Go to school, so the number of servicemen is still lacking. He asserted that his visit was to ensure that newcomers were valued by the military and not to use the term "framework".
In particular, the issue of merit status is not a high degree pool and always requires merit. According to Mr. Hun Manet, rank is not important, it is important to value oneself, one's skills, roles, duties and responsibilities of individuals.
There is a question to Mr. Hun Manet himself why the role of the Commander of the Army does not wear 4 stars? He replied that power was not important. Mr. Hun Manet reminded that when he went to a meeting abroad, the army chiefs of some countries only sat with one or two stars.
However, Mr. Hun Manet emphasized that this is just what he would like to share in my personal views regarding the leadership of the army. He does not want to show that his views are good or perfect.
