Ministry of Tourism issues Prakas on revision and implementation of "Cambodian Green Hotel Standard"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has issued a proclamation on the revision and implementation of the "Cambodian Green Hotel Standard", in which the hotel business and tourism accommodation services, which are defined as large enterprises, must comply with the Cambodian Green Hotel standard, while the hotel and tourism accommodation services. Defined as a small and medium enterprise can apply voluntarily.
According to Article 2 of this Prakas, the hotel and tourism accommodation business, which has classified tourism business as small and medium enterprises, can apply the Cambodian Green Hotel Standard on a voluntary basis. Meanwhile, the hotel and tourism business, which has classified tourism business as a large enterprise, must apply the Cambodian Green Hotel Standard as required.
At the same time, Mr. Kim Sereyroth, Director of the Department of Management of Accommodation, Tourism and Food Services of the Ministry of Tourism, added that the introduction of the Cambodian Green Hotel standard will be implemented from August 4, 2022 onwards. For Prakas No. 072 Prok. Dated March 24, 2016 on the implementation of the Cambodian Green Hotel standard shall be repealed.
He claimed that the announcement was to ease the burden on hotel owners and accommodation services for small and medium-sized tourists not to be obliged to apply for the standard of green hotels in Cambodia as before.
The Ministry of Tourism also calls on hotel and hotel business owners, as large enterprises, to hurry up and apply for the Cambodian Green Hotel Standard at the Secretariat of the Commission for the Management and Evaluation of Hotels and Tourism Services, located at the Ministry of Tourism or at its offices. Capital-provincial tourism avoids fines.
