BEIJING (Reuters) - The US Federal Reserve recently announced a 0.75 percent rate hike, matching the US Federal Reserve's target of 2.25 percent to 2.5 percent. This is the fourth time the US Federal Reserve has raised interest rates since the new year, and the second in a row to raise interest rates by 0.75 percent to tackle rising inflation. .
Some experts say that in order to curb high inflation, the US Federal Reserve has started raising interest rates too much, but the negative effect is to increase the risk of a sharp downside to the US economy.
By the end of 2021, their net worth will have grown to $ 3.4 billion. By 2021, the average per capita net profit will have increased by 51 percent, hence the gap between rich and poor Americans. Expanded rapidly.
Whether zero interest rates and QE policies have caused commodity prices to rise sharply in the past, or tight monetary policy, the United States has turned the crisis around the world through its US dollar hegemony. All of this has had a profound effect on the world's emerging economic entities, which are struggling to achieve economic recovery after the end of Kovid 19.
In the early stages of rising inflation, US government operations have been slow, only shouting that inflation is "temporary" as well as adhering to high-level loose monetary policy, which has led to a series of rising inflation. Therefore, the economic difficulties that the US government has been facing are the result of its irresponsibility.
He warned that even a "small attack" could lead to a slowdown in the US economy. According to the latest Bloomberg News forecast, after the US Consumer Confidence Index breaks record lows and interest rates are raised over the next year, the possibility of a slowdown in the US economy is likely to increase. 38 percent.
As the world's largest economy, as long as the US economy is in recession, it is likely to carry significant contagion risks. This is a risk that the whole world needs to be vigilant at all times.
Interestingly, while the US economy was in a slump, some Washington politicians did not consider their negligence in responding to the crisis to gamble. The old ones of blaming to divert conflict to the outside. This is irresponsible to the American people and irresponsible to the world.
Those politicians in Washington who insist on implementing the "United States Priority" concept should stop doing things that confuse you, turn the crisis around and blame arbitrarily, as well as implement more responsible macroeconomic policies. They are urged to take concrete measures to help the global economy recover from the spread of Kovid 19 soon.
