Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted this in a message celebrating the 55th anniversary of the birth of ASEAN (August 8, 1967 - August 8, 2022). In this message, Samdech Techo Prime Minister highlighted the many achievements that ASEAN has achieved in the past 55 years.
Samdech Techo said that over the past 55 years, ASEAN has transformed itself from an organization with a loose framework to an organization with a strong structure and based on the rule of law. ASEAN has undergone dramatic changes in both global and regional political perspectives and emerged as a strong and intelligent family.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia said that although ASEAN could not guarantee that there would be no conflicts and wars, at least ASEAN had acted as a provider of an open forum for constructive dialogue and consultation. This has made a significant contribution to promoting peace and stability in the region.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the great achievements so far highlighted the strong commitment and political will of the ASEAN leaders to maintain peace and stability as well as bring economic prosperity to an ASEAN community. With a spirit of unity and solidarity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also saw that for the future, ASEAN will continue to face many major security challenges, and the most important ones are the situation in Myanmar, the South China Sea, the Korean Peninsula and the Russian War. - Ukraine. All of these issues could destabilize regional peace and security if ASEAN does not manage them well.
In response to this issue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted Cambodia's position. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is an active contributor to the ASEAN Political-Security Community with a strong and jointly committed commitment to maintaining and promoting peace and security in the region.
"We support the momentum of ASEAN's active contribution to regional and global peace, including through UN peacekeeping operations," he added.
He stressed that Cambodia continues to attach great importance to upholding the universal principles of friendly and peaceful cooperation enshrined in the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia (TAC).
In order to overcome the current acute global crisis, Samdech Techo stressed that ASEAN must continue to focus on activities that bind together for better prosperity for our region.
"We will promote the ASEAN spirit of unity to bring together efforts within ASEAN and with external partners to promote ASEAN unity and resilience in order to achieve the goal of building the ASEAN Community Vision. 2025 with resilience. This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Samdech Techo expressed his belief that ASEAN can move forward with strength, solidarity and friendship to overcome all the challenges that are affecting the common interests of our people and our region in accordance with the ASEAN spirit: One sector, one identity, one community. ”
On the occasion of ASEAN's birthday, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the rotating chair of ASEAN in 2022, also issued a message congratulating ASEAN on its birthday, highlighting ASEAN's achievements and ASEAN's vision to respond to the problem. Lots of challenges today. The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message:
August 8, 2022 is a special day as we all celebrate the 55th anniversary of ASEAN as a regional organization. This important event is on a long journey that brings us all closer to achieving our vision of building a people-centered ASEAN community. And look forward together without abandoning anyone.
2. In the last 55 years, ASEAN has transformed itself from an organization with a loose framework to an organization with a strong structure and based on the rule of law. ASEAN has undergone dramatic changes in both global and regional political perspectives and emerged as a strong and intelligent family.
8. For the future, ASEAN will continue to face many major security challenges, and the most important ones are the situation in Myanmar, the South China Sea, the Korean Peninsula and the Russia-Ukraine war. All of these issues can destabilize the peace and security in our region if we do not manage them well.
