US Secretary of State Blinken begins visit to Africa to curb Russian influence
WASHINGTON: US Secretary of State Antony Blinken arrived in South Africa on Sunday to begin a three-nation tour of Africa aimed at curbing Russia's growing influence on the continent. . This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, August 7, 2022.
South Africa, a leader in developing countries, has remained neutral in the Ukraine war by refusing to join Western calls for condemnation of Moscow.
Blinken, who is on his second visit to Africa since his appointment earlier this year, is scheduled to travel to the Democratic Republic of Congo and Rwanda this weekend.
