BEIJING (Reuters) - China on Sunday decided to reduce the length of international flights suspended in connection with 19 Kovid crossings. This was released by Reuters on Sunday, August 7, 2022.
China Aviation Authority said in a statement on Sunday that flights linked to the route with 19 cases of Kovid would be suspended for a week if 4% of passengers were to be screened. Positive and for 2 weeks if 8% of passengers test positive.
