The new book "The Prime Minister's Oldest Son - The Journey to Take a Turn - Hun Manet", which focuses on the background of Hun Manet's activities, was compiled by Chhay Sophal and published in 20,000 copies in early August. This.
Speaking at the book handover ceremony at Fresh News, author Chhay Sophal said that although the 300-page book could not fully describe Manet's history and activities, he believed it could. A basic document on the history of His Excellency the new generation of politicians and leaders.
Mr. Chhay Sophal said that in addition to the information collected from various sources, he also received information directly from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kattipritbandit, as well as HE Hun Manet.
However, Mr. Sophal stated that if any of the authors or readers feel that this book is still lacking, they can write more according to their knowledge, skills and understanding, because a book is not. Can satisfy all readers, especially readers who are politicians and political servants with colorful tendencies.
Taking that opportunity, Mr. Lim Chea Vutha thanked Mr. Chhay Sophal for providing this book, which is a valuable literary legacy.
"I have already read this great book and gained a lot of knowledge as a basis for writing news," he said. This book also shows the excellent social activities of HE Hun Manet, as well as the history of his study abroad struggles. "After reading and knowing about the past capabilities of His Excellency Hun Manet, His Excellency is the most suitable candidate to continue to lead Cambodia in the future."
On that occasion, Mr. Chhay Sophal also thanked Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as HE Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Mr. Oknha Ing Bun Hou for supporting this book.
