Japanese Foreign Minister thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his efforts to help solve Myanmar's problems (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Japanese Foreign Minister Hayashi Yoshimasa praised the efforts of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen as President. ASEAN seeks to help resolve crisis in Myanmar The Japanese Foreign Minister thanked for this effort.
Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa said this during a courtesy call and discussion with Samdech Techo Hun Sen this morning, Saturday, August 6, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
Regarding the issue of Myanmar, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has made great efforts to mediate in order for the situation to return to normal and the path to democracy.
As chair of ASEAN, Cambodia has made great efforts to mediate and find solutions to Myanmar's problems. In particular, Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled directly to Myanmar to seek a solution to the crisis of Myanmar when he became the chair of ASEAN in January 2022, despite the pressure and some criticism.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia and Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair, also visited Myanmar twice to seek a solution to the Myanmar crisis and provide humanitarian assistance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the Japanese Foreign Minister that Cambodia has resolved the Myanmar issue based on the actual and appropriate situation, based on three principles: reduce violence, provide assistance and create a good environment for politicians on all sides in Myanmar.
However, Samdech Techo expressed regret over the latest developments in Myanmar over the execution of four opposition politicians.
Samdech Techo affirmed that Cambodia will continue to work to help solve Myanmar's problems so that the country's political situation can return to normal and on the path to democracy.
It should be noted that the US and Australian Foreign Ministers also thanked Cambodia for its efforts to help solve the problem of Myanmar in a meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen this week. Sen Sok Teuk Thla Agricultural Community issues statement in full support for the 10th Amendment to the Constitution
