Samdech Techo Hun Sen Receives Japanese Foreign Minister
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Saturday morning, August 6, 2022, received Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, leading a delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss work.
After the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the signing ceremony of an exchange of letters and related documents to provide more than $ 380 million in concessional loans for the development of a new container port in Sihanoukville.
The signing ceremony will take place between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, and Mr. Hayazi Yoshimasa, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan. Hariko, JICA Representative in Cambodia.
It should be noted that Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa paid a visit to Cambodia on August 3 at the invitation of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon to attend a meeting related to the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting.
Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa emphasized that during this visit, he intends to reaffirm the strong relationship between Cambodia and Japan. Last March, Prime Minister Kishida visited Cambodia and the two Prime Ministers issued a joint statement outlining the direction of future cooperation.
