Cambodia, Canada discuss deepening ties
(Phnom Penh) - Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with Canadian Minister of International Trade Mary Ng Ng on Export Promotion, Small Business and Economic Development, Canada, on August 5. This 2022 is on the occasion of the 55th Meeting of Foreign Ministers and related meetings within the framework of ASEAN in Phnom Penh.
In a statement released by Fresh News, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Marinok agreed to work closely to strengthen good relations between the two countries and promote broader cooperation for the common good. Each within the framework of bilateral, regional and global. The two sides agreed to hold major events to commemorate the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries this year.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon praised Canada for its assistance and technical support in demining activities in Cambodia and requested for additional Canadian contributions towards achieving the goal of "Cambodia without mines by year." 2025. "
Both sides noted with satisfaction the positive trajectory of bilateral trade, while Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his gratitude to Canada for maintaining the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP) to Cambodia.
Regarding ASEAN-Canada relations, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon praised Canada's full support for Cambodia's ASEAN chairmanship. The two sides also discussed the participation of the Canadian Prime Minister at the ASEAN Summit later this year, the ASEAN-Canada Free Trade Agreement and Canada's proposal to raise its status to the level of partnership. Strategy.
