Comment: US Congressman Nancy Pelosi's visit to Taiwan is dangerous
BEIJING (Reuters) - US Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton arrived in Taiwan on Tuesday night to escalate tensions in the Taiwan Straits. This is the highest-level US official visit to Taiwan in 25 years.
But the world's hopes were dashed when Pelosi's plane headed for Taiwan and landed on Tuesday night. Everyone knows that the Taiwan issue is the most sensitive issue for China and an indelible red line for the Chinese government.
The visit of a senior US official to the island, which is tantamount to recognizing the island, is a serious insult to China. It is not a coincidence, but this seems to be the use of new tactics to provoke China to anger, hoping that China will respond violently, which is an opportunity for the West to attack China.
This is a poisonous and cruel trick by using Taiwan as bait to lure China into its trap. At first glance, we might think that the United States seems to care about Taiwan, but if we look deeper, we see that this is a brutal ploy by the United States that it is not afraid to take its people. More than 20 million people in Taiwan come to serve as an instrument to serve their ambitions.
China's mature, patient response to this grave insult is fortunate for the whole world, but it is unknown at this time what other tricks the United States will use to seize China's territory. The biggest concern in the future.
