China suspends high-level military dialogue, other cooperation with US
BEIJING (Reuters) - Beijing on Friday announced it had decided to temporarily suspend cooperation with the United States in a number of areas, including talks between the two countries' top military commanders, in retaliation for the trip. Weekly visit by US House of Representatives Speaker Nancy Pelosi to Taiwan. This was released by CNA on Friday, August 5, 2022.
In a statement, the Chinese Foreign Ministry said that in addition to high-level military talks, Beijing has also suspended talks on climate change, as well as cooperation on cross-border crime prevention and cooperation. Repatriation of illegal migrants is one of eight specific actions. The same day, China also announced sanctions against Pelosi and her family members.
Pelosi visited Taipei on Tuesday and Wednesday this week, despite repeated warnings from Beijing. It is the highest-level visit by a US official in the last 25 years to the island, as China considers Taiwan only part of its territory.
