Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Commentary: Cambodia-China "Steel" Friendship Brings Leading Cambodian Youth to Grow
(Phnom Penh): In June 2022, the Cambodian Center for 21st Century Maritime Silk Road Research of the Royal University of Phnom Penh and the Cambodian Research Center of the Beijing University of Foreign Languages jointly disseminated the results of a survey of Cambodian youth perceptions of the country. China.
The results of the survey clearly show that since the 18th Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC), the people-to-people ties of the two countries have achieved the greatest achievements in the context of continuing to deepen trust. Political trust between China and Cambodia, the vigorous development of practical cooperation and the continuous expansion of the depth and breadth of cultural exchanges.
The same survey results show that respondents highly value the important role Chinese companies play in Cambodia's economic development. More than 70% of the respondents want to find a job in a Chinese company and hope to gain more skills and knowledge.
Deep cooperation between Cambodia and China has promoted the popularity of Chinese language learning in Cambodia. Surveys show that respondents generally believe that learning Chinese can be very helpful in finding a job, so they maintain a strong desire to learn Chinese. To meet the needs of learning Chinese in Cambodian society, the number of Confucius Institutes jointly established by Cambodia and China has increased to two.
(Author: Dr. Gu Jiayun, Deputy Director, Asia-Africa Institute, Beijing University of Foreign Languages, Dr. Nak Chendarith, Director, Cambodian Center for 21st Century Maritime Silk Road Research, Royal University of Phnom Penh)
