(Phnom Penh): Australian Foreign Minister Penny Vong has expressed her expectation that relations between Australia and Cambodia, as well as with ASEAN, will be strengthened and expanded.
The Australian Foreign Minister expressed such expectations during a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the evening of August 4, 2022.
In addition to expressing her desire to see the relationship strengthened and expanded with Cambodia and ASEAN, the Australian Foreign Minister praised the outcome of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings. She also congratulated Samdech Techo on his success as ASEAN Chair.
The Prime Minister also welcomed the Australian Ambassador. Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo expressed his congratulations on the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Australia.
The Prime Minister also congratulated the Australian Labor Party on its victory in last May's election. Samdech Techo also congratulated Ms. Penny Vong on her appointment as Minister of Foreign Affairs.
Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Australia for its contribution to the search for peace in Cambodia in the past and for the development of Cambodia. Not only that, recently provided vaccines and vaccine storage equipment to Cambodia to help Cambodia fight against Kovid 19 successfully.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his pleasure at the partnership between Cambodia and Australia. Especially pleased to see that the bilateral trade volume has increased to more than 200 million US dollars per year since 2019.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo requested Australia to increase trade activities, increase rice import quotas from Cambodia and open up a wider market for Cambodian products in order to further expand trade cooperation. Australia thanks Cambodia for its efforts to help solve Myanmar's problems
(Phnom Penh): The Australian Government, through its Foreign Minister, has thanked Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN for its hard work in resolving Myanmar's problems.
Australian Foreign Minister Penny Vong thanked Cambodia for its efforts to resolve the Myanmar issue during a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the evening of August 4, 2022.
However, Cambodia regrets and is shocked by the recent execution of four political prisoners. Reacting to this attitude, on behalf of the ASEAN Chair, Cambodia also reacted through the statement.
The Prime Minister stressed that despite the difficulties and complexities, Cambodia continues to work to help Myanmar return to normalcy and the path to democracy.
