Iran demands that the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) drop charges against Iran before reopening surveillance cameras
Tehran: Iran will resume the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) surveillance cameras at its nuclear plant unless the IAEA withdraws its charges against the city, Iran's top nuclear official said on Thursday. Tehran first. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Thursday, August 4, 2022.
In June, the IAEA Board adopted a resolution against Iran proposed by the United States, Britain, France and Germany following reports by the agency that Tehran had not provided a "credible explanation". »For uranium particles found in three unspecified places.
Following the adoption of the IAEA resolution, Iran announced a number of countermeasures, including the closure of IAEA surveillance equipment at its nuclear facilities.
