Regarding the Myanmar issue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the US Secretary of State that Cambodia was "saddened and surprised" by the recent execution of four political activists in Myanmar. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia reacted by issuing a statement on behalf of the ASEAN Chair on July 25, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that despite its regrets, Cambodia remains committed to helping Myanmar return to normalcy and the process of democratization.
The US Secretary of State also informed Samdech Techo that the US direction is to have a positive relationship with Cambodia on the basis of existing cooperation such as export markets and development assistance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure and welcome to the presence of the US Ambassador during the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings. Samdech Techo also expressed his pleasure at the outcome of the ASEAN-US Summit in May 2022 and the previous meeting with US senators and businessmen in Washington.
In the case of a vote in support of the UN General Assembly Resolution on Russia's Invasion of Ukraine, Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia adheres to the principles of the UN Charter and the recognized standards related to respect for sovereignty, territorial integrity. And the independence of all UN member states. Cambodia also called for a ceasefire, peaceful negotiations and extreme tolerance.
In connection with the search for missing American soldiers during the war, Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia had worked with the United States for many years and that Cambodia continued to cooperate on humanitarian issues.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the United States for its continued assistance to Cambodia in humanitarian work, the delivery of vaccines, the prevention of the spread of Kovid 19, the support of cultural and heritage work through the return of antiquities to Cambodia, and Assist Cambodia in other areas, including education, environment, etc. Ministry of Education and National Authority for Combating Drugs Continue to Educate Students at Meanchey National University
(Banteay Meanchey): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in collaboration with the National Authority for Combating Drugs, has continued to disseminate health education and drug education to students at Meanchey National University.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Soeur Socheata, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and was attended by representatives of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Advisers to the University Management Committee and representatives of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Drug Control Committee, Serey Sophorn City. On the afternoon of August 4, 2022 at Meanchey National University.
Speaking on behalf of Mr. Sok Khorn, Chairman of the Management Committee, Mr. Chiv Sarith, Deputy Rector, said that the seminar to promote drug prevention in educational institutions is very beneficial, especially for students and professors of the University in raising Strengthen the capacity, knowledge, health policy and meet to prevent drug problems in the family and community.
On behalf of General Meas Virith, Major General Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legislation, Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that there is peace, only life, only time to talk about health and drugs.
