Senior Minister Osman Hassan receives Sri Lankan Foreign Minister
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission, on the afternoon of August 4, 2022, met and discussed with Mr. Ali Sabry, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka on the occasion of his visit to the meeting. The 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers and related meetings organized by Cambodia.
The meeting was held to strengthen cooperation between Cambodia and Sri Lanka, which was held at the office of Senior Minister Osman Hassan in Phnom Penh.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that Cambodia, under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, has harmonized all religions in Cambodia, without religious conflicts, without discrimination, and especially the Islamic community. Receive a lot of attention and offers that have made progress in the field of education and socio-economic transformation of the general population.
The Senior Minister continued that the Royal Government has allowed community representatives to be leaders in the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, senior diplomats, national and sub-national authorities, the Armed Forces of all kinds and civil servants.
The Royal Government allows, in principle, men to wear a bag and Muslim women to wear a passport, make ID cards, or take photographs for administrative documents. Muslim students can wear traditional attire and wear a krama while studying at both public and private educational institutions. In addition, the Royal Government has included about 1,500 Khmer-Islamic teachers in the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and 180 contract officials.
