(Kampong Chhnang): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, expressed his admiration for all CMAC officers and thanked the CMAC heroes of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for their lives. Landmines liberate the territory to the people and the society.
According to the report of Mr. Heng Ratana, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), the Cambodian CMAC has been in existence for 30 years, from June 10, 1992 to June 10, 2022. He continued that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the sole guide of win-win politics, which is the policy of uniting the Khmer nation at the end of 1998 and the Khmer nation is completely peaceful to this day.
In particular, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo and with the participation of all development partners as well as demining delegates in recent years, the accident rate due to landmines and explosive remnants of war has steadily decreased. At the beginning of 2022, from January to June, the mine accident rate was only 40 people.
As a result of the past 30 years of operation, CMAC has cleared more than 1,342 square kilometers of minefields and minefields, locating and destroying all types of landmines and unexploded ordnance. 2,931,463 with national and international recognition.
For the future, CMAC has launched a four-year strategic plan to clear the area affected by more than 700 kilometers of known anti-personnel mines in the national database, out of the remaining 788 kilometers. Meanwhile, in 2022, CMAC has promoted the liberation of seven mine-free provinces, including Phnom Penh, Kep, Kandal, Kampot, Sihanoukville, Takeo and Kampong Cham.
As of July 2022, CMAC has decided to liberate Phnom Penh, Kep and Sihanoukville provinces from the threat of anti-personnel landmines. This plan will contribute to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as well as the International Mine Action Organization (NGO) to achieve the Royal Government's ambitions in implementing a strategy towards a landmine-free Cambodia by the end of 2025.
