He added that the first to play the role of educating is the family society, so if more women come to study, the society will be more prosperous by helping to teach children to be highly educated and skilled. Life for children, and for those who invest second in knowledge is the state institution.
Ministry of Telecommunications is using and developing 18 technology systems to facilitate work faster, more efficiently and can be a model for other ministries and institutions (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been developing 18 technology systems to promote Work more efficiently, save time, reduce costs and earn money.
During a press conference on "Achievements of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications for the past five years" at the Office of the Council of Ministers this morning, August 4, 2022, Mr. Chea Van Det, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, said that the system 18 technologies, of which 8 systems have been commissioned, 2 systems are ready to be launched in the near future, and 8 systems are under construction.
Two systems that have been set up but have not yet been launched include the .kh national registration system and the mobile user information management system.
"Therefore, if these 18 systems are set up, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will become the Ministry of Technology in its work, which will enable the Ministry to work efficiently, quickly and economically," he said. "Daily, monthly, annual budget."
He also said that out of the 18 technology systems, some will be able to generate revenue for the Ministry. For example, the national registration system .kh If the Ministry launches this system will be able to earn an additional $ 10 million into the national budget.
Mr. Chea Vandeth also said that using data from the Telecommunications Center (DMC) for revenue distribution has tripled the ministry's revenue in the past two years, from 2020 to 2021 compared to last year. 2018 and 2019, because the Ministry has enough data to collect debts from all operators.
