Professor of French: A good translator, in addition to being firm, clear, regular, must know how to love his own language in order to be good
(Phnom Penh): Mr. M. Lim, Professor of French in the Department of French Translation, Department of French at the Royal University of Phnom Penh for almost 30 years, said that in order to be a good translator, in addition to being firm, clear, regular, honest and flexible under the circumstances, translators must know Loving one's own national language is better.
Mr. M Lim said this on August 2, 2022, on the occasion of his participation in a program to share work experience as a translator, which was organized at the Francophone Job Center in Phnom Penh at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
Please be informed that this is the first time that the French Higher Education Agency in Cambodia (AUF-Cambodge) has invited translation experts to share their experiences in this field with more than 60 young people, students, professors and young professionals participating in Live and online programs, and also for the third time since the Francophone Job Center was established in September 2021.
He argued that machines could not replace humans because machines were not emotional, they were just faster calculators than humans, and although they could not take over human work, we had to use them to our advantage. .
Mr. Sok Limsrun, Representative of the Department of French, said that translation training was re-established at the Institute of Foreign Languages every weekend to make it easier for students to continue their studies outside of working hours. .
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that Cambodia has always attached great importance to relations and cooperation with Russia and would like to see this relationship and cooperation develop better.
The Prime Minister made this remark during a working meeting with Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov on Thursday morning, August 4, 2022.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, said that in this meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Mr. Lavrov highlighted the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Russia. In particular, the Russian Foreign Ministry urged to strengthen and expand existing cooperation and continue to promote further cooperation in tourism, investment and other fields.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that the relationship between Cambodia and Russia is a historical relationship and Cambodia has always attached great importance to strengthening friendly relations and close cooperation in various fields with Russia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the government and people of the former Soviet Union and the Russian Federation for their support and assistance to the people and the Royal Government of Cambodia during difficult times.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth quoted Samdech Techo as saying, "We can not forget the friendly and sympathetic gestures when we needed them, for example: Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, which saved many lives and The Institute of Technology of Cambodia, which has trained many students.
In order to further enhance relations and cooperation, Samdech Techo and the Russian Foreign Minister agreed to hold a meeting of the Intergovernmental Commission between the two countries, focusing on trade, economic, scientific and technical cooperation.
It should be noted that in this meeting, the Russian diplomat expressed his congratulations to the Cambodian People's Party, which won the election in the Commune / Sangkat Council elections. The Russian diplomat also briefed Samdech Techo on the situation and position of Russia on the conflict with Ukraine. ASEAN-India Foreign Ministers' Meeting kicks off in Cambodia
