In a statement sent to Fresh News on August 4, 2022, "FUNCINPEC has always adhered to the one-China policy and respected the national sovereignty of the People's Republic of China, taking into account issues related to "Taiwan is China's internal affairs."
FUNCINPEC calls on all parties concerned to seek peaceful solutions, maintain the status quo and avoid provocation for peace and stability in the region and the world. The President of the Senate pays a courtesy call on the President of the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea
On behalf of the delegation, Mr. Kim Jung Nam expressed his deep gratitude to the President of the Senate for taking the time to meet with the delegation. During their stay in Cambodia, they now see the rapid development of Cambodia. Upon their return home, the delegation will make every effort to provide more assistance to Cambodia.
Mr. Kim Jung Nam stated that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on the four-year humanitarian agreement to the Cambodian Senate will contribute to the development of Cambodia.
The President of the Senate praised the role of the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea in the global humanitarian work, which has contributed to solving the shortage of health, medical system and medical education to developing countries. In the world.
The President of the Senate expressed his pleasure at the assistance of the Global Life-Sharing Fund for the construction of the Samdech Techo Rehabilitation Center, which is a necessary and practical need of the Cambodian people. Samdech requested that this discussion lead to the successful implementation of the project in the near future.
The President of the Senate praised the friendship and solidarity between the two countries' parliaments and peoples, which has grown steadily through exchanges, visits, experiences, culture, traditions and many other fields.
The President of the Senate congratulated the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Cambodian Senate and the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea today, through the Memorandum of Understanding Cooperation in the field of health and philanthropy with the Cambodian Senate for 4 years at a cost of 10 million US dollars.
Measures in front of the Ministry and the operation of telephone service providers are jointly studying to install more antennas in Phnom Penh, especially in the cities.
Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, claimed that while studying the installation of additional antenna poles, some people also seemed to express dissatisfaction with the installation of this pole near their homes, they have Misunderstood that this antenna pole has an impact on their health and so on.
In the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit this morning, August 4, 2022, under the theme "Achievements for the past 5 years of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications", Mr. Chea Vandeth emphasized that based on what he learned Research No international institution has assessed that this antenna pole affects health.
In response to this obstruction, Minister Chea Vandeth stressed that the Ministry will take legal action against those who obstruct the installation of antenna towers for inappropriate reasons.
The minister said, "In some areas, people do not allow the construction of antennas, citing the fact that the antenna poles affect his health. So ask him if it affects health, people all over the world use all the antenna poles. This is an unreasonable reason. "If they remain stubborn, they will take action."
According to Mr. Chea Van Det, according to the study, the heat emitted from the tower is 10 times less than the sun we touch every day, so there is no reason for this tower to affect the health of the people.
Mr. Chea Vandeth still claims that the problem of poor quality of telephone service will end soon, but this work requires the participation of the people and all local authorities, especially the people must cooperate to remove the device to expand the service. They equipped this supplement so that the evaluation team can find a solution quickly.
The Forestry Administration claims that the development in Phnom Tamao has not cleared Phnom Tamao Park, more than 400 hectares of Phnom Tamao Park remains the same, people want to visit at any time!
The Forestry Administration's statement came after a series of reactions after they saw land clearing and development around Phnom Tamao.
According to a press release issued on August 4, 2022, the Forestry Administration said that Phnom Tamao is a forest rehabilitation station with acacia, oil, wind and natural trees.
The statement added that the area is full of sand, the trees are not growing well. Therefore, the Royal Government decided to use this area for development because it is an area near the city, near the new airport and close to the Tonle Bati tourist area.
The Forestry Administration emphasizes that exchanges are carried out strictly, with private company appraisals, and that there is an inter-ministerial privatization commission that properly monitors and evaluates exchanges.
The Forestry Administration also confirmed that the area does not have any important wildlife that is endangered and rare as mentioned, and this area has wild pigs that often come to disturb people's crops. The wildlife mentioned above is the wildlife kept in Phnom Tamao Zoo Park which is 100% safe and this development is not affected at all.
